hadiths[497]{hadithnumber,text}:
"9001","Al-Miqdam ibn Dawud narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us, Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq narrated to us, from Mujahid, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, 'Allah boasts of the people of Arafat to the people of heaven - the angels - saying: Look at these servants of Mine; they came disheveled and dusty.' No one narrated this hadith from Mujahid except Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq."
"9002","Al-Miqdam ibn Dawud narrated to us, Said ibn Ufayr narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Bilal narrated to us, from Kathir ibn Zayd, from al-Walid ibn Rabah, from Abu Hurayrah: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, 'Amin, amin, amin.' It was said to him, 'O Messenger of Allah, you never used to do this?' So he said, 'Jibril, peace be upon him, said to me: May the nose of a servant be rubbed in dust - or: may he be distanced - who enters Ramadan and is not forgiven, so I said amin; then he said: May the nose of a servant be rubbed in dust - or: may he be distanced - who reaches his parents or one of them and they do not admit him into Paradise, so I said amin; then he said: May the nose of a servant be rubbed in dust - or: may he be distanced - in whose presence you are mentioned and he does not send blessings upon you, so I said amin.'"
"9003","Al-Miqdam narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Salih narrated to us, Musa ibn Ulayy ibn Rabah narrated to me, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Masud who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took me with him one night and said, 'A group of the jinn, fifteen, sons of brothers and sons of uncles, are coming to me tonight and I shall recite the Quran to them.' So I went with him to the place he intended, and he drew a line for me then seated me in it and said, 'Do not go out of this.' So I spent the night in it until the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to me near dawn, in his hand a hollow bone, dung, and charcoal, and he said, 'When you go to relieve yourself, do not clean yourself with any of these.' He said: When morning came I said, I must know where the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was, so I went and saw the place of seventy camels. Ulayy ibn Rabah did not narrate from Ibn Masud any hadith other than this."
"9004","Al-Miqdam narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa narrated to us, al-Masudi narrated to us, from Dawud ibn Yazid al-Awdi, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah who said: It was said, O Messenger of Allah, what most admits people into the Fire? So he said, 'The two hollows: the private part and the mouth.'"
"9005","Al-Miqdam narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us, Misar ibn Kidam narrated to us, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Abu al-Abbas, from Abdullah ibn Amr who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, 'Have I not been told that you stand the night and fast the day?' I said, 'I do that.' He said, 'If you do, you will harm your eyes; every month three days, that is the fast of a lifetime.' So I said, 'I find strength.' So he said, 'Fast the fast of Dawud: he used to fast a day and break fast a day.'"
"9006","And from Abdullah ibn Amr who said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asking his permission for jihad, so he said, 'Are your parents alive?' He said, 'Yes.' He said, 'Then strive in them.'"
"9007","Al-Miqdam narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us, Misar ibn Kidam narrated to us, from Muharib ibn Dithar, from Jabir who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, 'The best of you are the best of you in repaying debts.'"
"9008","Al-Miqdam narrated to us, Khalid ibn Nizar narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Umar al-Umari narrated to us, from Wahb ibn Kaysan, from Jabir ibn Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) set out from Makkah for hajj or umrah or a campaign, and when he was partway he said, 'Who will fill for us the cisterns of al-Uthayah?' Jabir said: So I said, 'I will, O Messenger of Allah.' So we went until we came to al-Uthayah and I filled the basin, and in part of the night a man came and dismounted, and behold it was the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He went and relieved himself, then came and performed ablution from the basin, then came and prayed, wearing a waist-wrapper wrapped around him. So I performed ablution, then came and stood at his left, and he took my hand and placed me at his right, and he prayed two rakahs. No one narrated this hadith from Wahb ibn Kaysan except Abdullah ibn Umar."
"9009","Al-Miqdam narrated to us, Nuaym ibn Hammad narrated to us, Abdullah ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Yunus, from Uqayl, from Ibn Shihab, from Urwah, from Aishah: she used to order talbinah for the sick and the one grieved over the dead, and she would say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying, 'Talbinah comforts the heart of the sick and removes some grief.'"
"9010","Al-Miqdam narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Yusuf narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from his brother Isa ibn Lahiah, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas who said: When the verse of inheritance shares in Surat al-Nisa was revealed, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade habs (life endowment). No one narrated this hadith from Ikrimah except Isa, and it is not narrated from Ibn Abbas except with this chain."
"9011","Al-Miqdam narrated to us, my uncle Said ibn Isa narrated to us, Mufaddal ibn Fadalah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ajlan who said: al-Harith ibn Yazid al-Ukli and Said ibn Abdurrahman al-Hamdani narrated to me, from Amir al-Shabi who said: I heard al-Numan ibn Bashir al-Ansari saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying, 'Place a screen between yourselves and the unlawful; whoever does that is freer of blame for his honor and religion, and whoever falls into it is like one grazing beside the sanctuary, about to fall into it. Every king has a sanctuary, and Allah's sanctuary on earth is His prohibitions.'"
"9012","Al-Miqdam narrated to us, my uncle Said narrated to us, Mufaddal ibn Fadalah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ajlan, from Said al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, 'Faith has seventy-odd branches, the highest is the testimony that there is no god but Allah, the lowest is removing harm from the road, and modesty is a branch of faith.' No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Ajlan from al-Maqburi except Mufaddal ibn Fadalah."
"9013","Al-Miqdam narrated to us, my uncle Said ibn Isa narrated to us, Abdurrahman ibn Ashras narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Umar, from Humayd, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, 'When I was admitted into Paradise I saw in it a palace of gold, so I said to Jibril: Whose palace is this? He said: For a man of Quraysh. So I hoped I was he, and I said: And who is he? So he said: Umar ibn al-Khattab.' Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mentioned that to Umar and said, 'Were it not for what I know of your jealousy, O Abu Hafs, I would have entered it.' So Umar wept and said, 'With my father and mother, would I be jealous of you, O Messenger of Allah?' Abdullah ibn Umar said: And Zayd ibn Aslam narrated to me, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the like of it, except that he said: Umar is jealous, and I am more jealous than he, and Allah is more jealous than us. No one narrated this hadith from Zayd ibn Aslam except Abdullah ibn Umar, nor from Abdullah except Abdurrahman ibn Ashras; Said ibn Isa is alone in it."
"9014","Al-Miqdam narrated to us, Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated to us, Abdullah ibn al-Samh al-Tujibi narrated to us, from Abbad ibn Kathir, from Uqayl, from Ibn Shihab, from Anas ibn Malik: Zaynab, daughter of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), granted protection to Abu al-As ibn al-Rabi ibn Abd Shams, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) upheld her protection."
"9015","Al-Miqdam narrated to us, Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated to us, Yahya ibn Salih al-Ayli narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Umayyah, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Ibn Abbas: the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Attab ibn Usayd, 'I have sent you over the people of Allah, the people of Makkah, so forbid them from selling what they have not taken possession of, from profiting on what they have not guaranteed, from two conditions in a condition, from a sale combined with a loan, and from a sale combined with an advance.' No one narrated this hadith from Ismail ibn Umayyah except Yahya ibn Salih, nor from Ata except Ismail; Yahya ibn Bukayr is alone in it."
"9016","Al-Miqdam narrated to us, Said ibn Ufayr narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Bilal narrated to us, from Kathir ibn Zayd, from Amr ibn Tamim, freedman of Banu Zamanah, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when Ramadan drew near would say, 'This month of yours has overshadowed you; by the oath of Abu al-Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) by which he swore, nothing like it has passed over the Muslims. Allah records its reward and its supererogatory acts before He brings it in, and records its burden and wretchedness before He brings it in; that is because the believer prepares his spending and his family's provision, and the wicked prepares for the heedlessness of the Muslims and their exposed faults. So it is a blessing for the believer and a calamity upon the disbelievers.'"
"9017","Al-Miqdam narrated to us, Said ibn Ufayr narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Bilal narrated to us, from Humayd al-Tawil, from Anas ibn Malik: he heard him saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took an oath of abstention from his wives, and his foot had been sprained, so he stayed in an upper room twenty-nine nights, then came down. They said, 'O Messenger of Allah, you swore a month.' So he said, 'The month is twenty-nine.'"
"9018","Al-Miqdam narrated to us, Khalid ibn Nizar narrated to us, Hammad ibn Abi Humayd narrated to us, from Yaqub, freedman of al-Huraqah, from Abu Hurayrah: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, 'Whoever follows a funeral until prayer is offered over it has a qirat, and whoever follows it until it is buried has two qirats, the smaller of them like Uhud.' Hammad ibn Abi Humayd - he is Muhammad, thus the people of Madinah say Hammad - did not narrate from Yaqub, freedman of al-Huraqah, any hadith other than this."
"9019","Al-Miqdam narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us, Sufyan al-Thawri narrated to us, from Ayyub al-Sakhtiyani and Khalid al-Hadhdha, from Abu Qilabah, from Anas ibn Malik who said: It is from the Sunnah that when a man marries a virgin while having a previously married wife, he stays with her seven nights, and when he marries a previously married woman while having a virgin, he stays with her three nights."
"9020","Bakr ibn Sahl and al-Miqdam ibn Dawud narrated to us, saying: Abdullah ibn Salih narrated to us, Musa ibn Ulayy ibn Rabah narrated to me, from his father, from Amr ibn al-As who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent for me and ordered me to take my clothes and weapons, so I came to him while he was performing ablution; he looked me up and down, then said, 'O Amr, I want to send you at the head of an army so that Allah grants you victory and safety, and I shall allot for you an allotment of wholesome wealth.' So I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, I did not accept Islam out of desire for wealth; rather I accepted Islam out of desire for Islam and to be with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him).' So he said, 'Yes - and how excellent is wholesome wealth for a righteous man.'"
"9021","Al-Miqdam narrated to us, Khalid ibn Nizar narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Abu Qabus, from Abdullah ibn Amr who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, 'The merciful will be shown mercy by Allah; show mercy to those on earth and He who is in heaven will show mercy to you.'"
"9022","Al-Miqdam narrated to us, Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Abduljabbar ibn Umar narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Jabir who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would not turn around when he walked, and sometimes his cloak would catch on a tree or something and he would not turn until they lifted it off him; and they would laugh and joke, for they felt safe from his turning around."
"9023","And from Jabir, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: 'Every good deed is charity.'"
"9024","Al-Miqdam narrated to us, Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Wahb narrated to us, Abu Hani Humayd ibn Hani narrated to me, from Abu Said al-Ghifari: he heard Abu Hurayrah saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying, 'My nation will be afflicted with the disease of the nations.' They said, 'O Messenger of Allah, what is the disease of the nations?' He said, 'Insolence, arrogance, mutual estrangement, competing in the world, mutual hatred, and miserliness, until there is transgression, then there is killing.' No one narrated this hadith from Abu Said al-Ghifari except Abu Hani."
"9025","Al-Miqdam narrated to us, Uthman ibn Salih narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Shuayb, from his father, from his grandfather, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said, 'Whoever says when he stirs at night: In the name of Allah, ten times, and Glory be to Allah, ten times, I believe in Allah and disbelieve in the false god, ten times, he is protected from everything he fears, and no sin should overtake him until the like of it.'"
"9026","Al-Miqdam narrated to us, my uncle Said ibn Isa narrated to us, Mufaddal ibn Fadalah narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said regarding things he forbade: 'And the price of the dog.' No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Jurayj except Mufaddal."
"9027","Al-Miqdam narrated to us, Khalid ibn Nizar Abu Yazid al-Ayli narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Salih al-Tammar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, from Attab ibn Usayd: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said regarding the zakat of vineyards, 'It is estimated as date-palms are estimated, then its zakat is paid as raisins just as the zakat of date-palms is paid as dates.' No one narrated this hadith from al-Zuhri except Muhammad ibn Salih."
"9028","Al-Miqdam narrated to us, Khalid ibn Nizar narrated to us, Kathir ibn Abdullah al-Muzani narrated to us, from Rubayh ibn Abdurrahman ibn Abi Said al-Khudri, from his father, from his grandfather: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took zakat al-fitr from the desert people as dried yogurt. This hadith is not narrated from Abu Said except with this chain; Kathir ibn Abdullah is alone in it."
"9029","Al-Miqdam narrated to us, Khalid ibn Nizar narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah: the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, 'Indeed some poetry is wisdom.' No one narrated this hadith from al-Zuhri except Sufyan; Khalid ibn Nizar and Nahshal ibn Kathir al-Misri are alone in it."
"9030","Al-Miqdam narrated to us, my uncle Said ibn Isa narrated to us, Mufaddal ibn Fadalah narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ata and Abu al-Zubayr: they heard Jabir ibn Abdullah saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade mukhabarah, muzabanah, muhaqalah, and selling fruit until it becomes edible, except araya. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Jurayj except Mufaddal."
"9031","Miqdam narrated to us, my uncle Said ibn Isa narrated to us, Mufaddal ibn Fadalah narrated to us, from Khalid ibn Yazid: Ata ibn Abi Rabah narrated to me, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr: Aishah narrated to him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would pray while she lay across between him and the qiblah. No one narrated this hadith from Khalid ibn Yazid except Mufaddal."
"9032","Al-Miqdam narrated to us, my uncle Said ibn Isa narrated to us, Mufaddal ibn Fadalah narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Ayyub, from Yunus and Uqayl, from Ibn Shihab, from Said and Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said, 'When the reciter says amin, then say amin; whoever's amin coincides with the amin of the angels is forgiven what preceded of his sin.'"
"9033","Al-Miqdam narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Jabir who said: When the people of Paradise enter Paradise, Allah, mighty and majestic, says, 'O My servants, do you ask Me for anything that I may add to you?' They say, 'O our Lord, what is better than what You have given us?' He says, 'My pleasure is greater' - raised as a report to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). No one narrated this hadith from Sufyan in raised form except Abdullah ibn al-Mughirah and al-Firyabi."
"9034","Al-Miqdam ibn Dawud narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Hammam ibn Yahya narrated to us, from Qatadah, regarding His saying, 'And I do not know what will be done with me nor with you': he said: The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to know after that what would be done with him when Allah revealed, 'Indeed We have granted you a clear victory.' Hammam said: He narrated to us from Anas ibn Malik that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when this verse was revealed to him, said, 'There has been revealed to me a verse dearer to me than the whole world.' When the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited it, a man of the people said, 'Congratulations to you, O Prophet of Allah; Allah has made clear to you what will be done with you, so what will be done with us?' So Allah revealed, 'That He may admit the believing men and believing women into gardens beneath which rivers flow' - the verse. No one narrated this hadith from Hammam except Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Mughirah."
"9035","Al-Miqdam narrated to us, Khalid ibn Nizar narrated to us, Abdullah ibn al-Muammil narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, 'The water of Zamzam is for whatever it is drunk for.' No one narrated this hadith from Abu al-Zubayr except Abdullah ibn al-Muammil."
"9036","Al-Miqdam narrated to us, Khalid narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Yahya ibn Talhah ibn Ubaydullah narrated to us, from Mujahid, from Abdullah ibn Amr: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, 'Whoever lies upon me deliberately, let him take his seat in the Fire.' No one narrated it from Mujahid except Ishaq."
"9037","Al-Miqdam narrated to us, Khalid ibn Nizar narrated to us, Nafi ibn Umar al-Jumahi narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah who said: Abdullah ibn Umar said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, 'My Basin is a month's journey; its corners are equal, its water whiter than silver, its scent sweeter than musk, its cups like the stars of the sky; whoever drinks from it never thirsts again.' No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Abi Mulaykah except Nafi ibn Umar."
"9038","Miqdam narrated to us, Khalid ibn Nizar narrated to us, Nafi ibn Umar narrated to us, Bishr ibn Asim narrated to us, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, 'Allah hates the eloquent among men who rolls speech with his tongue as cattle roll herbage with their tongues.' This hadith is not narrated from Abdullah ibn Umar except with this chain; Nafi ibn Umar is alone in it."
"9039","Al-Miqdam ibn Dawud narrated to us, Khalid ibn Nizar narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Tahman, from Humayd al-Tawil, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw during his pilgrimage a man being led between his two sons between Makkah and Madinah, so he said, 'What is the matter with this one?' They said, 'He vowed to walk to the House.' So he said, 'Allah has no need of this one's tormenting himself; let him ride.'"
"9040","Al-Miqdam narrated to us, Khalid ibn Nizar narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated to us, Abu Uthman al-Yashkuri narrated to me, saying: Anas ibn Malik passed by us in the mosque of Banu Rifaa, and we had prayed the dawn prayer, and with him were some people; one of them called the adhan, then he bowed the two rakahs, then the iqamah was made, and Anas ibn Malik stepped forward and led them in the dawn prayer. When he finished his prayer, he sent for two cushions, and they were brought, and they were arranged for him, and he sat narrating to us. Among what he narrated to us was that he served the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ten years, and he never said to him for something he did, 'Why did you do this?' nor for something he did not do, 'Why did you not do such-and-such?'"
"9041","Al-Miqdam narrated to us, Khalid ibn Nizar narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Ubayd ibn Umayr narrated to us, Abu al-Zubayr narrated to us, from Jabir: the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, 'This House is a pillar among the pillars of Islam; whoever performs hajj of the House or umrah is guaranteed by Allah: if he dies He admits him into Paradise, and if He returns him to his family He returns him with reward and spoils.' No one narrated this hadith from Abu al-Zubayr except Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Ubayd ibn Umayr."
"9042","Al-Miqdam narrated to us, Khalid narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Abdullah narrated to us, from Malik ibn Anas, from Ibn Shihab, from Anas: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered Makkah on the day of the conquest with a helmet on his head, not in ihram; when he removed it, he came to him and said, 'Ibn Khatal is clinging to the curtains of the Kabah.' So he said, 'Kill him.'"
"9043","Al-Miqdam narrated to us, Khalid narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Umar narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas: the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was cupped while in ihram for an ailment in his head. No one narrated this hadith from Humayd except Abdullah ibn Umar."
"9044","Al-Miqdam narrated to us, Khalid narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Umar narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade selling fruit until it ripens. It was said to him, 'What is ripening?' He said, 'Until it reddens.'"
"9045","Al-Miqdam narrated to us, Khalid ibn Nizar narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah, from Anas ibn Malik who said: Eight men from Ukl came to Madinah and accepted Islam, but found the land unhealthy; so they came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and complained to him, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to them, 'Go out to the camels and drink from their milk and urine.' So they went and stayed among them as long as Allah willed, then killed the herdsman and drove off the camels. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent in pursuit of them, and they were brought, and he cut off their hands and feet and branded their eyes."
"9046","Al-Miqdam narrated to us, Khalid ibn Nizar narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Muslim narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Yahya ibn Jadah: Abdullah ibn Abd al-Qari narrated to me that he heard Abu Hurayrah saying: It is not I who forbade fasting on Friday; rather the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade it."
"9047","Al-Miqdam narrated to us, Khalid ibn Nizar narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ziyad, from Abu Hurayrah who said: When people brought dates to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he would ask about them; if they said charity, he said, 'Eat,' and would not eat; and if they said a gift, he ate with them."
"9048","And from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, 'Your Lord, blessed and exalted, says: Every deed of the son of Adam is for him, except fasting; it is for Me and I reward for it. The breath of the fasting person's mouth is sweeter to Allah than the scent of musk.'"
"9049","And from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, 'The poor one is not the one who goes around whom a morsel or two, or a date or two, turns away; rather the poor one is he who finds nothing to suffice him and does not ask people so that they give him.'"
"9050","Al-Miqdam narrated to us, Khalid narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Umar, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, 'Every deed of the son of Adam is for him, and fasting is for Me and I reward for it. The breath of the fasting person's mouth is sweeter to Allah than the scent of musk. He leaves his wife, his desire, his food and his drink for My sake; so it is for Me and I reward for it. The fasting person has two joys: joy at his breaking fast, and joy when he meets Me. Fasting is a shield; if someone fights him or insults him, let him not speak to him, but say: I am fasting.' No one narrated this hadith from Abdullah ibn Umar except Khalid ibn Nizar."
"9051","Al-Miqdam narrated to us, Khalid ibn Nizar narrated to us, and Yahya ibn Ayyub al-Allaf narrated to us, Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Jafar ibn Abi Kathir narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Muhammad ibn Kab al-Qurazi who said: I entered upon Anas ibn Malik near Asr on a day when they doubted whether it was Ramadan, intending to greet him, and he called for food and ate. So I said, 'Is what you do Sunnah?' He said, 'Yes.' No one narrated this hadith from Zayd ibn Aslam except Muhammad ibn Jafar."
"9052","Al-Miqdam narrated to us, Khalid ibn Nizar narrated to us, al-Munkadir ibn Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir narrated to us, from his father, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said, 'Every good deed is charity; and among good deeds is meeting your brother with a cheerful face, and pouring from your bucket into your brother's vessel.'"
"9053","Al-Miqdam narrated to us, Khalid ibn Nizar narrated to us, saying: I heard Sufyan ibn Uyaynah saying: When Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir mentioned the Qadariyyah he would say, 'The Qadariyyah are the polytheists.'"
"9054","Al-Miqdam narrated to us, Khalid ibn Nizar narrated to us, Hisham ibn Sad narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Said al-Khudri who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying, 'Whoever strives to be patient, Allah will make him patient; whoever seeks sufficiency, Allah will suffice him; whoever asks us, we give him; and no one has been given a provision broader for him than patience.'"
"9055","Al-Miqdam narrated to us, Khalid narrated to us, Hisham ibn Sad narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Said al-Khudri who said: I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, which people are most severely tried?' So he said, 'The prophets.' I said, 'Then who?' He said, 'Then the righteous. One of them would be tried with poverty until he finds nothing but a date or the like, and one of them would be tried until lice infest him and he casts off the lice; and one of them would be more joyful in tribulation than him in ease.' No one narrated this hadith from Zayd ibn Aslam except Hisham ibn Sad."
"9056","Al-Miqdam narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Yusuf and Uthman ibn Salih narrated to us, saying: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Zayd ibn al-Muhajir ibn Qunfudh, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Jabir: a man of Thaqif gifted the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a waterskin of wine after wine had been forbidden, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered it split open. A man said, 'If only you ordered it sold.' So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, 'He who forbade drinking it forbade selling it.' No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn Zayd except Ibn Lahiah."
"9057","Al-Miqdam narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Yusuf and Uthman ibn Salih narrated to us, saying: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Jabir: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, 'Do not depart on the day of Arafah until the imam departs.' No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir except Ibn Lahiah."
"9058","Al-Miqdam narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Yusuf and Uthman ibn Salih narrated to us, saying: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Jabir: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say, 'O Allah, I ask You for beneficial knowledge, and I seek refuge in You from knowledge that does not benefit.'"
"9059","Al-Miqdam ibn Dawud narrated to us, Uthman ibn Salih and Abdullah ibn Yusuf narrated to us, saying: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Jabir: a woman between whom and her husband was a dispute came with her husband to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The woman said, 'This is my husband; by Him who sent you with the truth, there is nothing on earth more hateful to me than he.' And the husband said, 'This is my wife; by Him who sent you with the truth, there is nothing on earth more hateful to me than she.' So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered them to draw near to him, then supplicated for them, and they did not part from him until she said, 'By Him who sent you with the truth, Allah has created nothing dearer to me than he,' and the husband said, 'By Him who sent you with the truth, Allah has created nothing dearer to me than she.' No one narrated this hadith from Ibn al-Munkadir except Ibn Lahiah."
"9060","Al-Miqdam narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Yusuf and al-Nadr ibn Abduljabbar narrated to us, saying: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Bukayr ibn Abdullah ibn al-Ashajj: Asim ibn Umar ibn Qatadah narrated to him that Jabir ibn Abdullah visited him sick, then said, 'I shall not leave until you are cupped, for I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying, Cupping is a cure.'"
"9061","Al-Miqdam narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Yusuf narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Jafar ibn Rabiah, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Jabir ibn Abdullah who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the year of the conquest saying, 'Allah has forbidden the sale of wine, carrion, swine, and idols.' It was said, 'O Messenger of Allah, what about the fat of carrion, for ships are greased with it, skins are greased with it, and people use it for lamps?' So he said, 'Forbidden.' Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said at that, 'May Allah curse the Jews; Allah forbade them fats, so they melted them, sold them, and ate their prices.'"
"9062","Al-Miqdam ibn Dawud narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Yusuf, Abdullah ibn al-Hakam and Uthman ibn Salih narrated to us, saying: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Khayr ibn Nuaym, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Jabir ibn Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the price of the cat."
"9063","Al-Miqdam narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Yusuf narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Khayr ibn Nuaym, from Ata, from Jabir: the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, 'Gifts to the ruler are misappropriation.'"
"9064","Al-Miqdam narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Yusuf narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Muslim al-Taifi narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Jabir who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade mukhabarah, muzabanah, and muhaqalah. Mukhabarah is for a third, a quarter, or half on the whiteness of the land; muzabanah is selling fresh dates for dry dates, and selling grapes on the tree for raisins; and muhaqalah is selling standing crops on their stalks for food."
"9065","Al-Miqdam narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Yusuf narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Muslim narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Jabir who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, 'There is no sadaqah in any crops, date-palms, or vines until their harvest reaches five wasqs.'"
"9066","And from Jabir who said: A man came while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was delivering the sermon on Friday, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him, 'Have you prayed?' He said, 'No.' He said, 'Then pray two rakahs.'"
"9067","And from Jabir who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade a man placing one foot over the other while lying on his back. No one narrated these hadiths from Amr ibn Dinar except Muhammad ibn Muslim."
"9068","Al-Miqdam narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Yusuf narrated to us, al-Layth ibn Sad narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Said, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir who said: A man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on his return from Hunayn, and in Bilal's garment was silver from which he took handfuls and gave the people, so he said, 'O Muhammad, be just.' So he said, 'Woe to you; who is just if I am not just? I have failed and lost if I am not just.' So Umar ibn al-Khattab said, 'Let me kill this hypocrite.' So he said, 'Allah forbid that people say I kill my companions. This one and his companions recite the Quran and it does not pass their throats; they shoot out of the religion as the arrow shoots out of the game.'"
"9069","Al-Miqdam narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Yusuf narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Said, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir who said: The sun set while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was at Sarif, and he prayed Maghrib at Makkah, and between them are ten miles; and the sun set at Dhat al-Jaysh, and he prayed Maghrib at Madinah, and between them are eleven miles."
"9070","Al-Miqdam narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Yusuf narrated to us, Malik ibn Anas narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade eating sacrificial meat after three days, then said afterwards, 'Eat, take provision, and store.'"
"9071","And with it: from Jabir: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade eating sacrificial meat after three days, a man eating with his left hand, and walking in one sandal."
"9072","And from Jabir: the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, 'A cow suffices for seven, and a camel for seven.'"
"9073","And from Jabir: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, 'Close the door and tie the waterskin.'"
"9074","Al-Miqdam narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Yusuf narrated to us, al-Layth ibn Sad narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to me, from Ibn Jurayj, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) bought a camel from a bedouin of Banu Amir ibn Sasaah, and when the sale became binding he said to him, 'Choose.' The bedouin said to him, 'I have never seen today a sale better than your sale; by your life with Allah, from whom are you?' He said, 'From Quraysh.'"
"9075","Al-Miqdam narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Yusuf narrated to us, al-Layth narrated to me, from Khalid ibn Yazid, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came from the mountain having relieved himself, and before them were dates on a mat; so they invited him to it, and he sat eating with us, and did not touch water. No one narrated this hadith from Khalid ibn Yazid except al-Layth."
"9076","Al-Miqdam ibn Dawud narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Yusuf narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Khalid ibn Yazid, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir who said: When 'Say: He is able to send punishment upon you from above you' was revealed, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, 'I seek refuge in Allah from that'; 'or from beneath your feet' - the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, 'I seek refuge in Allah from that'; 'or clothe you in factions' - he said, 'This is easier.' And had he sought refuge, He would have granted him refuge. No one narrated this hadith from Khalid ibn Yazid except Ibn Lahiah."
"9077","Al-Miqdam narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Yusuf narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir: when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) alighted at al-Hijr during the campaign of Tabuk, he stood and addressed the people, saying, 'O people, do not ask your Prophet for signs. These are the people of Salih; they asked their prophet to send them a she-camel and he did. She would drink from this mountain pass, drinking their water on her day of drink, and they would milk from her milk like what they got on the day of her absence; then she would issue from this mountain pass. They transgressed their Lord's command and hamstrung her, so Allah gave them three days' respite, and Allah's promise was not belied. Then the Cry came to them, and Allah destroyed everyone among them between heaven and earth except a man who was in Allah's sanctuary, and Allah's sanctuary protected him from Allah's punishment.' It was said, 'O Messenger of Allah, who is he?' He said, 'Abu Righal.'"
"9078","And from Jabir: he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying, 'I precede you at the Basin; its extent is what is between Aylah and Makkah, and men and women will come, but will not taste anything from it.'"
"9079","And from Jabir: he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying, 'Hardness of hearts and harshness are among the people of the east, and faith and tranquility are among the people of the Hijaz.'"
"9080","And from Jabir: a slave-girl belonging to some of the Ansar came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said, 'My master forces me into prostitution.' So Allah revealed, 'And do not force your slave-girls into prostitution if they desire chastity.'"
"9081","And from Jabir who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying, 'If a woman pleases one of you and settles in his heart, let him go to his wife and be intimate with her, for that repels what is in his heart.'"
"9082","And from Jabir: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, 'Do not deem provision slow, for no soul dies until it reaches the last of its provision; so seek beautifully in lawful seeking, and beware of the unlawful.'"
"9083","Al-Miqdam ibn Dawud narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa, Abdullah ibn Yusuf and al-Nadr ibn Abduljabbar Abu al-Aswad narrated to us, saying: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying, 'We on the Day of Resurrection are upon a mound above the people. The nations will be called with their idols and what they used to worship, first then first, until our Lord comes to us after that and says: What are you waiting for? So we say: We await our Lord. So He, blessed and exalted, says: I am your Lord. So they say: Until we look at You. So He manifests Himself to them, then He proceeds and they follow Him. Then every man, hypocrite and believer - on the day He envelops him - is given shade; then they follow Him, and with them the hypocrites upon the bridge of Hell, on which are hooks and thorns that seize whom Allah wills. Then the light of the hypocrite is extinguished and the believer is saved. The first group is saved, their faces like the moon on the night of fullness, seventy thousand not taken to account; then those after them like the brightest star in the sky, then likewise. Then intercession is permitted and they intercede, until whoever said there is no god but Allah and has in his heart a barley-grain's weight of faith is brought out, and they are placed in the courtyard of Paradise, and the people of Paradise pour water over them until they sprout like the sprouting of rubbish in the flood. Then they ask Allah until one of them is given the like of the kingdom of the world and ten times its like.'"
"9084","Al-Miqdam narrated to us, Said ibn Abi Maryam, Abdullah ibn Yusuf and al-Nadr ibn Abduljabbar narrated to us, saying: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying, 'This nation is tried in its graves. When the believer enters it and his companions turn away from him, an angel severe in rebuke comes to him and says: What did you say about this man? So the believer says: I say he is the Messenger of Allah and His servant. So the angel says to him: Look at your seat you see of Paradise, and your seat Allah saved you from of the Fire. So he sees both. Then the believer says: Let me go give glad tidings to my family. So it is said to him: Dwell.' 'And as for the hypocrite, his family turns away from him, and it is said to him: What did you say about this man? So he says: I do not know; I say what the people say. So it is said to him: You did not know. Look at your seat that was yours of Paradise; you have been given your seat of the Fire in its place.' Jabir said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying, 'Every servant is raised upon what he died upon: the believer upon his faith, and the hypocrite upon his hypocrisy.'"
"9085","Al-Miqdam narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Yusuf narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir: he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying, 'There will ever remain a group of my nation fighting upon the truth, dominant until the Day of Resurrection; and between a man and disbelief is abandoning prayer.'"
"9086","Al-Miqdam narrated to us, Asad ibn Musa and Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, saying: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir: he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying, 'A group of my nation will fight upon the truth, dominant until the Day of Resurrection; then Isa son of Maryam descends, and their leader says: Come forward and lead us in prayer. So he says: No; some of you are leaders over others, as an honor from Allah to this nation.'"
"9087","Al-Miqdam narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Mughirah al-Kufi narrated to us, Sufyan al-Thawri narrated to us, from Muzahim ibn Zufar, from Mujahid, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, 'A dinar you gave a poor person, a dinar you gave for freeing a neck, a dinar you spent in the path of Allah, and a dinar you spent on your family - the best of them is the dinar you spent on your family.'"
"9088","Maslamah ibn Jabir al-Lakhmi narrated to us, Munabbih ibn Uthman narrated to us, al-Wadin ibn Ata narrated to us, from Mahfuz ibn Alqamah, from Ibn Aidh: Shurahbil ibn al-Simt said to Amr ibn Abasah, 'Will you narrate to me a hadith you heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with no forgetfulness in it nor lie?' He said, 'Yes; I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Allah said: My love is assured for those who love one another for My sake, and My love is assured for those who aid one another for My sake. No believing man or woman to whom Allah takes in advance three children of his loins who have not reached puberty, except Allah admits him into Paradise by virtue of His mercy upon them.' No one narrated this hadith from al-Wadin ibn Ata except Munabbih ibn Uthman."
"9089","Maslamah ibn Jabir narrated to us, Munabbih ibn Uthman narrated to us, Sadaqah narrated to me, al-Wadin ibn Ata narrated to us, from Ata al-Khurasani, from al-Hasan, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said, 'Woman was created from a rib, and she will never be straight for you on one character; if you straighten her you break her, so manage her and live with her.' No one narrated this hadith from al-Wadin except Sadaqah; Munabbih ibn Uthman is alone in it."
"9090","Maslamah ibn Jabir narrated to us, Munabbih ibn Uthman narrated to us, Thawr ibn Yazid narrated to us, from Mujalid, from al-Shabi, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): he said one day, 'Would you like a sixth of Paradise to be yours?' They said, 'Yes, O Messenger of Allah, whose expanse is the heavens and the earth.' He said, 'Then a fifth of it?' They said, 'Yes.' He said, 'Then a quarter?' They said, 'That is even more.' The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, 'I hope that I am the remaining half.' No one narrated this hadith from Thawr ibn Yazid except Munabbih ibn Uthman."
"9091","Maslamah ibn Jabir al-Lakhmi narrated to us, Munabbih ibn Uthman narrated to us, Sadaqah narrated to us, al-Numan ibn al-Mundhir narrated to me, from Makhul and Yahya ibn al-Harith, from Abu Umamah: the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, 'Whoever loves for Allah and hates for Allah, gives for Allah and withholds for Allah, has completed faith.' No one narrated this hadith from al-Numan except Sadaqah; Munabbih ibn Uthman is alone in it."
"9092","Maslamah ibn Jabir al-Lakhmi narrated to us, Munabbih ibn Uthman narrated to us, Safwan ibn Amr narrated to us, from Shurayh ibn Ubayd al-Hadrami: Thawban, freedman of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, 'Perhaps your term will be extended until you are among those appointed over ten when people settle the outlying villages; so beware of being appointed over ten or more, for no man is placed over ten or more except he comes to Allah with his hand chained to his neck, and nothing frees him from that chain except justice, if he was just among them. And do not settle the outlying villages, for the settler of the outlying villages is like the settler of graves.' 'No ruler of ten' is not narrated from Thawban except with this chain; Safwan ibn Amr is alone in it."
"9093","Maslamah ibn al-Haytham ibn Maslamah al-Asbahani narrated to us, al-Abbas ibn al-Faraj al-Riyashi narrated to us, Abdulmalik ibn Qurayb al-Asmai narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Abu Ghalib, from Abu Umamah: the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, 'The Khawarij are the dogs of the Fire.'"
"9094","Masadah ibn Sad al-Attar al-Makki narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir al-Hizami narrated to us, Abu Damrah Anas ibn Iyad narrated to us, from Abdurrahman ibn Harmalah, from Umar ibn Munabbih, from Abu Abdullah al-Qarraz, from Sad ibn Abi Waqqas: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, 'No one intends Madinah with evil except Allah melts him as salt melts in water.' No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Harmalah except Abu Damrah."
"9095","Masadah ibn Sad narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir narrated to us, Abu Damrah narrated to us, from Ibn Harmalah, from Sad al-Zafari: the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade cauterization. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Harmalah except Abu Damrah."
"9096","Masadah ibn Sad narrated to us, Said ibn Mansur narrated to us, Abdulhamid ibn Sulayman narrated to us, saying: I heard Umarah ibn Ghaziyyah narrating from Fatimah bint al-Husayn, from her father, that Abdullah ibn Amr said: O Messenger of Allah, is it arrogance for one of us to have a noble swift camel? He said, 'No.' He said, Is it arrogance for one of us to have a fine suit? He said, 'No.' He said, Is it arrogance for one of us to have two fine sandals? He said, 'No.' He said, Is it arrogance for me to prepare food and invite my people so they walk behind me and eat with me? He said, 'No.' He said, What is arrogance, O Messenger of Allah? He said, 'To belittle the truth and despise people.' No one narrated this hadith from Umarah ibn Ghaziyyah except Abdulhamid ibn Sulayman, and it is not narrated from al-Husayn ibn Ali except with this chain."
"9097","Masadah ibn Sad narrated to us, Said ibn Mansur narrated to us, Nuh ibn Qays narrated to us, Salamah ibn al-Kindi narrated to us, saying: Ali - may Allah be pleased with him - used to teach the people the prayer upon the Prophet of Allah, saying: 'O Allah, Spreader of the spread-out lands, Creator of the raised-up heavens, Mender of hearts upon their primordial natures, their wretched and their felicitous: place the noblest of Your prayers, the choicest of Your blessings, and the highest of Your greeting upon Muhammad, Your servant and Messenger, the seal of what preceded, the opener of what was closed, the proclaimer of truth with truth, the crusher of the armies of falsehoods, as he perfected and bore Your command in obedience to You, fully devoted to Your pleasure without weakness of resolve at the outset nor feebleness in determination, calling to Your revelation, guarding Your covenant, proceeding upon the execution of Your command until he kindled a smile for the seeker of light; through him hearts were guided after the conjectures of trials and sin by the clarifying signs, the joys of Islam and the legacies of rulings. He is Your trusted trustworthy one, the treasurer of Your treasured knowledge, Your witness on the Day of Judgment, Your envoy as a blessing, Your messenger with truth as a mercy. O Allah, make spacious for him a spacious place in Your justice, reward him with multiplied good from Your bounty, pleasant and untroubled, from the known triumph of Your reward and the abundant portion of Your ample gift. O Allah, raise his building above the building of the remaining ones, honor his abode and lodging with You, perfect for him his light and his reward, from Your sending him forth, accepted in testimony, pleasing in speech, of just logic, decisive speech, and a great proof and evidence.' It is not narrated from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, except with this chain; Nuh ibn Qays al-Tahi is alone in it."
"9098","Masadah ibn Sad narrated to us, Said ibn Mansur narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Abdulaziz ibn Ubaydullah, from Said ibn Abi Hind: Abu Murrah, freedman of Aqil ibn Abi Talib, informed them that Umm Hani informed him that she granted protection to two men of Banu Makhzum on the day the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) conquered Makkah. Ali came upon her and said, 'What is this, O Umm Hani? I shall surely kill them.' She said: So I locked them in, then went to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and found him bathing while his daughter Fatimah screened him with a garment. He bathed, then took the garment and wrapped himself, then prayed Duha eight rakahs, then said, 'What is the matter with you, O Umm Hani?' I said, 'I have granted protection to two men of my in-laws, and Ali came wanting to kill them.' So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, 'We have granted safety to whom you granted safety, and protected whom you protected.' No one narrated this hadith from Abdulaziz ibn Ubaydullah except Ismail ibn Ayyash."
"9099","Masadah ibn Sad narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir narrated to us, Abbas ibn Abi Shamalah narrated to us, from Kathir ibn Abdullah al-Muzani, from his father, from his grandfather who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, 'Indeed some poetry is wisdom.' No one narrated this hadith from Kathir except Abbas ibn Abi Shamalah; Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir is alone in it."
"9100","Masadah ibn Sad narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Ala al-Thaqafi narrated to us, saying: I heard al-Walid ibn Ibrahim ibn Abdurrahman ibn Awf narrating from his father, from his grandfather: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, 'I find a fallen date and take it and eat it.'"
"9101","Masadah ibn Sad narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Ala al-Thaqafi narrated to us, from al-Walid ibn Ibrahim ibn Abdurrahman ibn Awf, from his father, from his grandfather who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, 'Do not force your sick to eat and drink, for Allah feeds them and gives them drink.' These two hadiths are not narrated from Abdurrahman ibn Awf except with this chain; Muhammad ibn al-Ala al-Thaqafi is alone in them."
"9102","Masadah ibn Sad narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir narrated to us, Man ibn Isa narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Hazim narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr, from Salim, from Ibn Umar, from Hafsah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said, 'There is no fasting for one who did not fix it with intention before dawn' - meaning: intend it. No one narrated this hadith from Ishaq ibn Hazim except Man. And al-Layth ibn Sad narrated this hadith from Yahya ibn Ayyub, from Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from his father, from Hafsah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he did not say 'fix it' but said 'obligate it.'"
"9103","Masadah ibn Sad narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Hamzah narrated to us, from Kathir ibn Zayd, from al-Muttalib ibn Abdullah ibn Hantab, from Abu Dharr who said: My beloved (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) enjoined upon me three: the Duha prayer, not to sleep except upon witr, and fasting three days of every month. No one narrated this hadith from al-Muttalib except Kathir ibn Zayd; Sufyan ibn Hamzah is alone in it."
"9104","Masadah ibn Sad narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir narrated to us, Abbas ibn Abi Shamalah narrated to us, from Musa ibn Yaqub al-Zamai, from Quraybah bint Wahb ibn Abdullah ibn Zamah, from Zaynab bint Umm Salamah who said: I entered upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was bathing, so he took a handful of water and struck my face with it and said, 'Behind you, O disagreeable one.' This hadith is not narrated from Zaynab except with this chain; Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir is alone in it."
"9105","Masadah ibn Sad narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir narrated to us, Abbas ibn Abi Shamalah narrated to us, Musa ibn Yaqub narrated to me, from Yazid ibn Abdullah ibn al-Had, from Abu Bakr ibn Sulayman ibn Abi Hathmah, from Hakim ibn Hizam who said: We heard a sound from the sky falling to earth as if a pebble falling into a basin, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) threw that pebble and we were routed. This hadith is not narrated from Hakim ibn Hizam except with this chain; Musa ibn Yaqub is alone in it, and none narrated from Musa except Abbas ibn Abi Shamalah and Ibn Abi Fudayk."
"9106","Masadah ibn Sad narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir narrated to us, Abbas ibn Abi Shamalah narrated to us, from Musa ibn Yaqub, from Ibn al-Asqa, from Rubayh ibn Abdurrahman ibn Abi Said, from his father, from his grandfather: his father Malik ibn Sinan, when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was wounded in his face on the day of Uhud, sucked the blood of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and swallowed it. It was said to him, 'Do you drink blood?' He said, 'Yes, I drink the blood of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him).' So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, 'My blood has mixed with his blood; the Fire shall not touch him.' This hadith is not narrated from Abu Said except with this chain; Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir is alone in it."
"9107","Masadah ibn Sad narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir narrated to us, Abbas ibn Abi Shamalah narrated to us, from Musa ibn Yaqub, from Yazid ibn Abdullah ibn al-Walid ibn Uthman, from Asma bint Abi Bakr: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, 'Stone the jamrahs of Mudar' - and every tribe used to stone one jamrah. This hadith is not narrated from Asma except with this chain; Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir is alone in it."
"9108","Masadah ibn Sad narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fulayh narrated to us, Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us, from his father who said: Abdullah ibn Amr was asked, 'What is the worst you saw the polytheists do to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)?' He said: The worst I saw them do to him was that I saw them agree against him one day; they seized him while he was circumambulating - they took hold of his cloak together - and said, 'Are you the one who reviles our gods and forbids what our fathers worship?' So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, 'Yes, I am he.' And Abu Bakr embraced him, saying at the top of his voice, 'Would you kill a man for saying: My Lord is Allah, and he has come to you with clear proofs from your Lord?' - and his eyes overflowed. No one narrated this hadith from Hisham ibn Urwah except Muhammad ibn Fulayh; Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir is alone in it."
"9109","Masadah ibn Sad narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fulayh narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Zayd ibn al-Muhajir ibn Qunfudh narrated to me, from his father, from Umm Salamah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, 'A woman's prayer in her house is better than her prayer in her chamber, her prayer in her chamber better than her prayer in her courtyard house, and her prayer in her courtyard house better than her prayer outside.' It is not narrated from Umm Salamah except with this chain; Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir is alone in it."
"9110","Masadah narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fulayh narrated to us, Abu Ghassan Muhammad ibn Mutarrif narrated to me, from Umar ibn Nafi, from his father Nafi: a man asked Abdullah ibn Umar, saying: I have a maternal uncle who parted from his wife, and grief and distress entered him and it weighed hard upon him, so I wanted to marry her, though he did not order me to nor know. So Ibn Umar said, 'No, unless you marry a marriage of desire: if she suits you, you keep her, and if you dislike her, you part from her; for we used to count this in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) as fornication.' No one narrated this hadith from Umar except Abu Ghassan Muhammad ibn Mutarrif."
"9111","Masadah ibn Sad narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Jafar ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Jafar al-Mukharrimi narrated to me, from Uthman ibn Muhammad al-Akhnasi, from Said al-Maqburi, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said, 'Whoever takes charge of judging has been slaughtered without a knife.' No one narrated this hadith from Ishaq ibn Jafar except Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir."
"9112","Masadah ibn Sad narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir narrated to us, my maternal uncle Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muttalib ibn al-Saib ibn Abi Wadaah narrated to me, Abdullah ibn Musa ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Umayyah al-Makhzumi narrated to me, my uncle Musab ibn Abdullah narrated to me, from Umm Salamah bint Abi Umayyah who said: In the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) people would pray following his prayer and one's gaze would not go beyond the place of his feet. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed away, and there was Abu Bakr, and when one of them stood praying his gaze would not go beyond the place of his sides. Then Abu Bakr passed away and there was Umar, and when one of them stood his gaze would not go beyond the place of the qiblah. Then there was Uthman ibn Affan, and when one of them stood he would not turn in prayer right or left. It is not narrated from Umm Salamah except with this chain; Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir is alone in it."
"9113","Masadah ibn Sad narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Ikrimah ibn Musab ibn Thabit narrated to me, from his father, from his grandfather, from Abu Qatadah who said: Muadh ibn Jabal went out seeking the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and did not find him; he sought him in his houses and did not find him, then followed him street by street until he was directed to him at Mount Thawab. He went up Mount Thawab and looked right and left, and saw him in the cave to which people had made a path toward the Mosque of the Conquest, and behold he was prostrating. So I descended from the mountaintop while he was prostrating, and he did not raise his head until I thought ill and thought he had died. When he raised his head I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, I thought ill of you and thought you had died.' So he said, 'Jibril, peace be upon him, came to me in this place and said: Allah, blessed and exalted, greets you with peace and says to you: What would you like Me to do with your nation? I said: Allah knows best. Then he left and came to me and said: He says: I shall not displease you regarding your nation. So I prostrated, and the best by which one draws near to Allah is prostration.' This hadith is not narrated from Abu Qatadah except with this chain; Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir is alone in it."
"9114","Masadah ibn Sad narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Man al-Ghifari narrated to us, Musa ibn Sad narrated to us, from his father: he went out with Abdullah ibn Umar, and Abdullah ibn Umar said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying, 'Whoever gives his pledge then breaks it shall meet Allah, mighty and majestic, on the Day of Resurrection without his right hand (oath).' No one narrated this hadith from Musa except Muhammad ibn Man; Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir is alone in it."
"9115","Masadah ibn Sad narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Jafar ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Jafar al-Mukharrimi narrated to me, from al-Harith ibn al-Fudayl, from Jafar ibn Abdullah ibn al-Hakam, from Abdurrahman ibn al-Miswar ibn Makhramah, from Abu Rafi who said: Ibn Masud said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, 'There was never a prophet but he had among his nation disciples of his companions who follow his command and are guided by his Sunnah.' No one narrated this hadith from Ishaq ibn Jafar except Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir."
"9116","Masadah ibn Sad al-Attar narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fulayh narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Husayn ibn Ata narrated to me, from Dawud ibn Bakr ibn al-Furat, from Sharik ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Namir, from Anas ibn Malik: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed for rain; he delivered the sermon before the prayer, faced the qiblah, turned his cloak, then came down and prayed two rakahs in which he uttered no takbir except one takbir each time. No one narrated this hadith from Abdullah ibn Husayn except Muhammad ibn Fulayh; Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir is alone in it."
"9117","Masadah ibn Sad narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Talhah al-Taymi narrated to me, Ishaq ibn Yahya ibn Talhah narrated to me, saying: I was with Musa ibn Talhah in the mosque, and al-Saib ibn Yazid entered. He said: Go to that elder and say to him: Your nephew Musa ibn Talhah says to you: Did you see the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? So I went to him and said: Did you see the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? So he said: I saw him. So we entered upon him, I and some lads with me, and found him eating dates in a basket, with some of his companions with him; so he grasped for us from those dates handful by handful, and wiped over our heads. No one narrated this hadith from Ishaq except Muhammad ibn Talhah; Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir is alone in it."
"9118","Masadah ibn Sad narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Nafi narrated to us, Abu Mashar narrated to me, from Ubaydullah ibn Umar, from Hamzah ibn al-Mughirah ibn Shubah, from his father who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) set out on the campaign of Tabuk, and when he was partway he went to relieve himself and I followed him. When he finished I said, 'Here is water, O Messenger of Allah.' So he withdrew from me and I withdrew from him; he cleaned himself with water, then said, 'Pour upon me.' So I poured upon him, and he washed his face three times and his hands three times, wiped his head, and wiped over the two khuffs. No one narrated this hadith from Ubaydullah ibn Umar except Abu Mashar, nor from Abu Mashar except Abdullah ibn Nafi; Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir is alone in it."
"9119","Masadah ibn Sad narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Ali ibn Hasan ibn Abi Rafi narrated to us, Kathir ibn Abdullah narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather, from Abdullah Dhu al-Bijadayn, who died in the campaign of Tabuk: he died in the depth of the night, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) descended into his grave pit and said to Abu Bakr and Umar, 'Lower your brother to me.' When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) placed him in his niche he said, 'O Allah, I am pleased with him, so be pleased with him.' So Abu Bakr said, 'By Allah, I wish I were the occupant of the pit.' No one narrated this hadith from Kathir ibn Abdullah except Ibrahim ibn Ali; Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir is alone in it."
"9120","Masadah ibn Sad narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Talhah al-Taymi narrated to us, Abdulhakim ibn Sufyan ibn Abi Namir narrated to us, from Sharik ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Namir, from Jabir ibn Abdullah who said: We set out on the campaign of Dhat al-Riqa until, when we were at Harrah Waqim, a bedouin woman with her son presented herself, and came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said, 'O Messenger of Allah, this son of mine - Satan has overpowered me through him.' So he said, 'Bring him near to me.' So she brought him near, and he said, 'Open his mouth.' So she opened it, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) spat in it, then said, 'Be gone, enemy of Allah, and I am the Messenger of Allah' - he said it three times - then said, 'Take your son; there is no harm upon him, and nothing of what afflicted him shall return to him.' Then we set out and alighted at mid-morning in a waterless desert with no tree, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Jabir, 'O Jabir, go and look for a place for me' - meaning for relieving himself. So I went out and found only two separate trees, which if joined would have screened him. So I returned to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said, 'O Messenger of Allah, I saw nothing to screen you except two separate trees which, if joined, would screen you.' So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, 'Go to them and say to them: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) says to you: Join together.' So I went out and said it to them, and they joined until they were as if upon one root. Then I returned and told the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out until he relieved himself, then returned and said, 'Go to them and say to them: The Messenger of Allah says: Return as you were, each one to its place.' So I returned and said to them, and they returned. Then we set out and alighted in a valley of Banu Muharib, and a man of Banu Muharib called Ghawrath ibn al-Harith confronted him while the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wore his sword hanging. He said, 'O Muhammad, give me this sword of yours.' So he unsheathed it and handed it to him; he brandished it and looked at it a while, then turned to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said, 'O Muhammad, what protects you from me?' He said, 'Allah protects me from you.' So his hand trembled until the sword fell from his hand, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took it, then said, 'O Ghawrath, who protects you from me?' He said, 'No one; may my father be ransom for you.' So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, 'O Allah, suffice us against Ghawrath and his people.' Then we came back, and a man of the companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came carrying a birds' nest with chicks in it, their parents following him and alighting upon the man's hand. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) turned to those with him and said, 'Do you marvel at what these two birds do with their chicks? By Him who sent me with the truth, Allah is more merciful to His servants than these two birds are to their chicks.' Then we came back until, when we were at Harrah Waqim, the bedouin woman who had come with her son met us with a skin of milk and a sheep, and gave them to him as a gift. So he said, 'How is your son? Has anything of what afflicted him befallen him?' She said, 'By Him who sent you with the truth, nothing of what afflicted him has befallen him.' And he accepted her gift. Then we came on until, when we were at a descent of the Harrah, a camel came trotting. So he said, 'Do you know what this camel said?' They said, 'Allah and His Messenger know best.' He said, 'This is a camel that came to me seeking my protection against its master; it claims it plowed for him years until, when it became mangy and emaciated and old, he wanted to slaughter it. Go with him, O Jabir, to his owner and bring him.' So I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, I do not know its owner.' He said, 'It will guide you to him.' So it went out ahead of me, hastening, until it stood with me in a gathering of Banu Khatmah. I said, 'Where is the lord of this camel?' They said, 'So-and-so son of so-and-so.' So I went to him and said, 'Answer the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him).' So he came out with me until he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him, 'This camel of yours seeks my protection against you; it claims you plowed with it a long time until you made it mangy and emaciated and it grew old, then you wanted to slaughter it?' He said, 'By Him who sent you with the truth, it is indeed so.' So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him, 'Sell it to me.' He said, 'Yes, O Messenger of Allah.' So he bought it from him, then set it free among the trees until it raised a hump, and whenever any of the Emigrants' or Helpers' water-camels ailed, he would give it to him; and it remained thus a long time. Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir said: Muhammad ibn Talhah said to me: The campaign of Dhat al-Riqa used to be called the campaign of marvels. No one narrated this hadith from Sharik ibn Abdullah except Abdulhakim ibn Sufyan, nor from Abdulhakim except Muhammad ibn Talhah; Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir is alone in it."
"9121","Masadah ibn Sad narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Nafi narrated to us, from Khalid ibn Ilyas, from Abu Bakr ibn Sulayman ibn Abi Hathmah, from al-Shifa Umm Sulayman: the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) employed Abu Jahm ibn Hudhayfah over the spoils, and he struck a man with his bow, wounding him with a bone-displacing wound, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) judged in it fifteen camels. This hadith is not narrated from al-Shifa except with this chain; Khalid ibn Ilyas is alone in it."
"9122","Masadah ibn Sad narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Nafi al-Saigh narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Umar ibn Hafs, from Yazid ibn Ruman, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, from Abu Humayd al-Saidi who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) employed a man of his companions over the charities; he came back with what he brought and said, 'This is for you and this is for me.' That reached the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he addressed the people and said, 'Why is it that I employ one of you over matters Allah has entrusted to me, and he comes back saying: This is for you and this was gifted to me? Would one of you not sit in his father's house and his mother's house until he is gifted?' Then he said, 'Would one of you not sit in his father's house and his mother's house until he is gifted?' Then he said, 'None of you shall come on the Day of Resurrection carrying upon his back a camel with a bellow, or a cow with a moo, or a sheep with a bleat.' Then he raised his hands to heaven and said, 'Have I not conveyed?' No one narrated this hadith from Yazid ibn Ruman except Abdullah ibn Umar, and none narrated from Abdullah except Abdullah ibn Nafi and Dawud ibn Khalid al-Khayyat."
"9123","Masadah ibn Sad narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Jafar ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Jafar al-Mukharrimi narrated to me, from Umm Bakr, from al-Miswar ibn Makhramah: Abdurrahman ibn Awf sold a vineyard to Uthman for forty thousand dinars, and Uthman ordered Abdullah ibn Sad ibn Abi Sarh to give him the price. So Abdurrahman distributed it among Banu Zahrah, the poor of the Muslims, and the wives of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Al-Miswar said: So I came to Aishah, and she said, 'What is this?' I said, 'Abdurrahman sent it.' So she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, 'None shows kindness to you after me except the patient ones; may Allah give Ibn Awf to drink from Salsabil of Paradise.' No one narrated this hadith from Ishaq ibn Jafar ibn Muhammad except Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir."
"9124","Masadah ibn Sad narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir narrated to us, Man ibn Isa narrated to us, Faid - freedman of Abadil - narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Abi Rafi, from his father: the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went early to Banu Qurayzah upon a bare donkey called Yafur. This hadith is not narrated from Abu Rafi except with this chain; Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir is alone in it."
"9125","Masadah ibn Sad narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir narrated to us, Abu Damrah narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Said ibn Abi Hind narrated to us, from Abdulmajid ibn Suhayl ibn Abdurrahman ibn Awf, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me, 'This pulpit of mine is upon a rivulet of the rivulets of Paradise.'"
"9126","Masadah ibn Sad narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, Dawud ibn Abdurrahman al-Attar informed me, from Amr ibn Yahya al-Mazini, from Yusuf ibn Muhammad ibn Thabit ibn Qays ibn Shammas, from his father, from his grandfather, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): he entered upon him and said, 'Remove the harm, O Lord of men, from Thabit ibn Qays ibn Shammas.' Then he took dust from Buthan, placed it in a cup with water, and poured it upon him. No one narrated this hadith from Yusuf ibn Muhammad ibn Thabit except Amr ibn Yahya, and none narrated from Amr ibn Yahya except Dawud al-Attar; Ibn Wahb is alone in it."
"9127","Masadah ibn Sad narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Ali ibn Hasan ibn Ali ibn Abi Rafi narrated to us, Faid - freedman of Abadil - narrated to me, from his master Abadil, from Abu Rafi: he sold a plot the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had granted him, by the house of Sad ibn Abi Waqqas, to Sad for eight thousand dirhams. A man had preceded him with it before, offering ten thousand dirhams for it, but he refused to sell to him. Abu Rafi said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying, 'The people of the courtyard are most entitled to their courtyard' - and Sad was the nearest neighbor. This wording 'the people of the courtyard' is not narrated except in this hadith with this chain; Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir is alone in it."
"9128","Masadah ibn Sad narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Ali ibn al-Hasan ibn Ali ibn Abi Rafi narrated to us, Abdurrahman ibn Abi Ziyad narrated to me, from his father who said: I heard Rabiah ibn Abbad al-Dayli saying: As for what I hear you saying - that Quraysh used to harm the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - the most I saw was that his dwelling was between the dwellings of Abu Lahab and Uqbah ibn Abi Muit, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would return to his house and find placentas, blood, and filth piled upon his door; so he would remove it with the limb of his bow and say, 'What an evil neighborhood this is, O company of Quraysh.' This hadith is not narrated from Rabiah ibn Abbad except with this chain; Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir is alone in it."
"9129","Masadah ibn Sad narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir narrated to us, Abdulaziz ibn Imran narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Hilal narrated to me, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah who said: Allah, majestic in majesty, revealed to His Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at Makkah, 'The multitude will be defeated and turn their backs.' So Umar ibn al-Khattab said, 'O Messenger of Allah, which multitude?' - and that was before Badr. When the day of Badr came and Quraysh were routed, I looked at the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in their tracks, sword unsheathed, saying, 'The multitude will be defeated and turn their backs.' And it was for the day of Badr. Then Allah, mighty and majestic, revealed concerning them, 'Until when We seize their luxurious ones with punishment' - the verse; and Allah revealed, 'Have you not seen those who exchanged Allah's blessing for disbelief' - the verse. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) threw at them, and the throw encompassed them and filled their eyes and mouths, until a man would be killed while wiping his eyes of what had been thrown. So Allah revealed, 'And you did not throw when you threw, but Allah threw.' And Allah revealed concerning Iblis, 'But when the two companies sighted each other he turned upon his heels and said: I am quit of you; I see what you see not; I fear Allah, and Allah is severe in punishment.' And Utbah ibn Rabiah and some of the polytheists with him said on the day of Badr, 'Their religion has deluded these.' So Allah revealed, 'When the hypocrites and those in whose hearts is disease say: These have been deluded by their religion.' This hadith is not narrated from Abu Hurayrah from Umar except with this chain; Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir is alone in it."
"9130","Masadah ibn Sad narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir narrated to us, Abdulaziz ibn Imran narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Sahl ibn Abi Hathmah narrated to me, my father informed me, from his father: Abu Barzah al-Harithi came on the day of Badr with three heads carrying them to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw him he said, 'Your right hand has prospered.' He said, 'O Messenger of Allah, as for two, I killed them; as for one, I saw a white man, handsome, of beautiful face, strike his head.' So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, 'That is so-and-so, an angel of the angels.' This hadith is not narrated from Sahl ibn Abi Hathmah except with this chain; Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir is alone in it."
"9131","Masadah ibn Sad narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir narrated to us, Abdulaziz ibn Imran narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Musa narrated to me, from Umarah ibn Ammar ibn Abi al-Yasar, from his father, from Abu al-Yasar who said: I looked at al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Muttalib, and he was as if an idol, his eyes shedding tears. When I looked at him I said, 'May Allah reward you with evil from a kinsman: you fight your nephew alongside his enemy?' He said, 'What happened - was he killed?' I said, 'Allah is mightier for him and more helpful than that.' He said, 'What do you want of me?' I said, 'Captivity, for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade killing you.' He said, 'This is not the first of his kinship.' So I took him captive, then brought him to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). This hadith is not narrated from Ammar ibn Abi al-Yasar except with this chain; Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir is alone in it."
"9132","Masadah ibn Sad narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir narrated to us, Abdulaziz ibn Imran narrated to us, Rifaa ibn Yahya narrated to me, from Muadh ibn Rifaa ibn Rafi, from Rifaa ibn Rafi who said: On the day of Badr the people gathered upon Umayyah ibn Khalaf, so I advanced toward him and saw a piece of his armor broken open beneath his armpit; so I stabbed him with the sword in it and killed him. And I was shot with an arrow on the day of Badr and my eye was gouged, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) spat in it, then supplicated for me, and nothing in it ever hurt me. This hadith is not narrated from Rifaa ibn Rafi except with this chain; Ibn al-Mundhir is alone in it."
"9133","Masadah ibn Sad narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir narrated to us, Abdulaziz ibn Imran narrated to us, Ayyub ibn Thabit narrated to us, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas who said: The angels did not fight alongside the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except on the day of Badr; otherwise they were reinforcements. And the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had no horses with him except two mares: one of al-Miqdad ibn al-Aswad, and the other of Abu Marthad al-Ghanawi. No one narrated this hadith from Ata except Ayyub ibn Thabit, nor from Ayyub except Abdulaziz; Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir is alone in it."
"9134","Masadah ibn Sad narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir narrated to us, Abdulaziz ibn Imran narrated to us, Said ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Jabir who said: Abu Jahl ibn Hisham said, 'Muhammad claims that if you do not obey him there will be slaughter among you.' So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, 'And I say that, and you are of that slaughter.' When he saw him slain on the day of Badr he said, 'O Allah, You have fulfilled for me what You promised me.' Then he directed Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Asad toward Abu Jahl. It was said to Ibn Masud, 'Did you kill him?' He said, 'Rather Allah killed him.' Abu Salamah said, 'Did you kill him?' He said, 'Yes.' So Abu Salamah said, 'Had He willed He would have placed you in His palm.' Ibn Masud said, 'By Allah, I killed him and stripped him.' He said, 'So what is his mark?' He said, 'A black mole on his right thigh.' So Abu Salamah recognized the description and said, 'You stripped him; and we stripped no Qurashi but him.' No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir except Said ibn Muhammad, nor from Said except Abdulaziz; Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir is alone in it."
"9135","Masadah ibn Sad narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir narrated to us, Abdulaziz ibn Imran narrated to us, Abdurrahman and Abdullah, sons of Zayd ibn Aslam, narrated to me, from their father, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Ibn Abbas: Arbad ibn Qays ibn Juzayy ibn Khalid ibn Jafar ibn Kilab and Amir ibn al-Tufayl ibn Malik ibn Jafar came to Madinah to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). They came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he sat, and sat before him. So Amir ibn al-Tufayl said, 'O Muhammad, what will you give me if I accept Islam?' So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, 'For you what is for the Muslims, and upon you what is upon them.' Amir said, 'Will you give me authority after you if I accept Islam?' So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, 'For you what is for the Muslims, and upon you what is upon them.' Amir said, 'Will you give me authority after you if I accept Islam?' So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, 'That is neither for you nor for your people; but for you is the command of the cavalry.' He said, 'I already have now the bridles of horses drawn; give me the desert and yours be the towns.' So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, 'No.' When Arbad and Amir went out, Amir said, 'O Arbad, I shall distract Muhammad from you with talk, so strike him with the sword; for if you kill Muhammad, the people will do no more than accept blood-money and dislike war, so we shall give them the blood-money.' Arbad said, 'I shall do it.' So they came back to him, and Amir said, 'O Muhammad, stand with me that I may speak to you.' So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood with him, withdrawn toward the wall, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood with him speaking to him, while Arbad drew the sword. When he placed his hand upon the sword it stiffened upon the hilt of the sword, and he could not draw the sword. And Arbad was slow with the striking upon Amir, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) turned and saw Amir and what he was doing, and turned away from them. When Amir and Arbad left the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), they went on until, when they were at the Harrah - the Harrah of Banu Waqim - they alighted, and Sad ibn Muadh and Usayd ibn Hudayr came out to them and said, 'Depart, O enemies of Allah.' So Amir said, 'Who is this, O Sad?' He said, 'Usayd ibn Hudayr al-Kataib.' So they left until, when they were at al-Raqm, Allah sent a thunderbolt upon Arbad and killed him, and Amir went on until, when he was at al-Khuraym, Allah sent an ulcer which seized him. Night overtook him in the house of a woman of Banu Salul, and he kept touching the ulcer in his throat, saying, 'A gland like a camel's gland in the house of a Salul woman; he wishes to die in her house.' Then he mounted his horse and spurred it until he died upon it, returning. Concerning them was revealed, 'Allah knows what every female bears and what the wombs diminish and increase' up to His saying, 'and they have besides Him no protector' - he said: The successive angels by Allah's command guard Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Then he mentioned Arbad and what killed him, saying, 'He it is who shows you lightning in fear and hope' up to His saying, 'and He is mighty in assault.' No one narrated this hadith from Zayd ibn Aslam except his two sons, and none narrated from them except Abdulaziz ibn Imran; Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir is alone in it."
"9136","Masada ibn Sad narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir narrated to us: Fadalah ibn Yaqub narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Ismail, from Hisham ibn Urwah, that Urwah narrated to him, from Aishah: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sat on the minbar on Friday, and when he sat he said: Sit down. Abdullah ibn Rawahah heard the words of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Sit down, so he sat down among Banu Ghanm. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, that is Ibn Rawahah sitting among Banu Ghanm; he heard you saying to the people, Sit down, so he sat in his place. No one narrated this hadith from Hisham ibn Urwah except Ibrahim ibn Ismail, and none from Ibrahim except Fadalah ibn Yaqub; Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir is alone in transmitting it."
"9137","Masada ibn Sad narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir narrated to us: Fadalah ibn Yaqub narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Ismail, from Ibn Ajlan, from Nafi, he narrated to him, that Abdullah ibn Umar passed by a man sitting in his prayer who had placed his left hand over his eye in prayer, and he said to him: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not sit the sitting of a people who were punished. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Ajlan except Ibrahim ibn Ismail; Fadalah ibn Yaqub is alone in transmitting it."
"9138","Masada ibn Sad narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir narrated to us: Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Urwah narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you wakes from his sleep, let him not put his hand into the vessel until he washes it, for he does not know where it spent the night, and let him mention the name of Allah before putting it in. No one narrated this hadith from Hisham ibn Urwah except Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Urwah; Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir is alone in transmitting it. And none of those who narrated this hadith from Abu al-Zinad said, and let him mention the name of Allah before putting it in, except Hisham ibn Urwah."
"9139","Masada ibn Sad narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir narrated to us: Abu Damrah narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Amir al-Aslami, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Seven will be shaded by Allah in the shade of His Throne on the Day of Resurrection: a just leader; a man who gives charity with his right hand hiding it from his left; a man to whom a woman of rank and beauty offered herself and he said: I fear Allah, Lord of the worlds; a man with whom Allah was mentioned and his eyes overflowed from fear of Allah; and a man who met a man and said: By Allah, I love you for the sake of Allah, and he replied: And I love you for the sake of Allah. No one narrated this hadith from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih except Abdullah ibn Amir al-Aslami; Abu Damrah is alone in transmitting it. And the well-known version is from the hadith of Habib ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Hafs ibn Asim, from Abu Hurayrah."
"9140","Masada ibn Sad narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Ismail ibn Abi Fudayk narrated to me, from Kathir ibn Abdullah, from his father, from his grandfather, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard a man saying: Here it is, green and fresh, so he said: O, at your service; we take your good omen from your mouth. No one narrated this hadith from Kathir except Ibn Abi Fudayk."
"9141","Masada ibn Sad narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn Ali al-Rafii narrated to us: Kathir ibn Abdullah narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed over al-Najashi and said takbir over him five times. No one narrated this hadith from Kathir except Ibrahim ibn Ali al-Rafii; Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir is alone in transmitting it."
"9142","Masada ibn Sad narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir narrated to us: Ibn Wahb narrated to us: Makhramah ibn Bukayr informed me, from his father, who said: I heard Yunus ibn Yusuf narrating, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, who said: Aishah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no day on which Allah frees more servants from the Fire than the Day of Arafah, and He draws near and boasts of them to the angels, saying: What did these people want? This hadith is not narrated from Aishah except with this chain; Makhramah ibn Bukayr is alone in transmitting it."
"9143","Masada ibn Sad narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir narrated to us: Ibn Wahb narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Ayyub, from Ibn Harmalah, from Yahya ibn Hind, that Hamzah ibn Amr al-Aslami narrated to him, saying: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at Arafah, with my uncle riding behind me, and he was placing one finger over the other, so I said: What is the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying? He said: He is saying: Throw the pebbles with the like of the pebbles for flicking. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Harmalah, from Yahya ibn Hind, from Hamzah ibn Amr, except Yahya ibn Ayyub; Ibn Wahb is alone in transmitting it. And people narrated it from Ibn Harmalah, from Yahya ibn Hind, from Asma ibn Kharijah."
"9144","Masada ibn Sad narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir narrated to us: Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us, from Ibn Abi al-Zinad, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Abdullah ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The world is the prison of the believer and the paradise of the disbeliever. No one narrated this hadith from Musa ibn Uqbah except Ibn Abi al-Zinad, and none from Ibn Abi al-Zinad except Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Mughirah; Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir is alone in transmitting it."
"9145","Masada ibn Sad narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir narrated to us: Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Mughirah narrated to me, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad, from Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Atiq, from his father, I do not know it except from Aishah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There was never a prophet but that in his nation there was one or two taught ones, and if there is any of them in my nation it is Umar ibn al-Khattab; indeed the truth is upon the tongue of Umar and his heart. This hadith about Aishah, indeed the truth is upon the tongue of Umar and his heart, is not narrated except with this chain; Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir is alone in transmitting it."
"9146","Masada ibn Sad narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir narrated to us: Ibn Abi Fudayk narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn al-Fadl, from Abdullah ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Husayn al-Makki, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the Day of Resurrection comes it will be called out: Where are the children of sixty? And that is the lifespan of which He said: Did We not give you long life in which whoever would remember could remember, and the warner came to you. No one narrated this hadith from Ata except Ibn Abi Husayn, and none from Ibn Abi Husayn except Ibrahim ibn al-Fadl; Ibn Abi Fudayk is alone in transmitting it, and it is not narrated from Ibn Abbas except with this chain."
"9147","Masada ibn Sad narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir narrated to us: Ishaq ibn Jafar ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Jafar al-Mukharrimi, from Ismail ibn Muhammad ibn Sad, from his father, who said: Sad ibn Abi Waqqas said: I was present at Badr and there was nothing on my face except a single hair, then Allah increased beards afterwards. No one narrated this hadith from Ishaq ibn Jafar except Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir."
"9148","Masada ibn Sad narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir narrated to us: Ishaq ibn Jafar ibn Muhammad narrated to me: Abdullah ibn Jafar al-Mukharrimi narrated to us, from Uthman ibn Muhammad al-Akhnasi, from Said al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: What is between the east and the west is the qiblah. No one narrated this hadith from Ishaq ibn Jafar except Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir."
"9149","Masada ibn Sad narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir narrated to us: Man ibn Isa narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Sad, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Rafi, that he brought the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a shoulder of sheep, and he ate it and did not perform ablution. No one narrated this hadith from Zayd ibn Aslam except Hisham ibn Sad; Man ibn Isa is alone in transmitting it."
"9150","Masada ibn Sad narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir narrated to us: Abdullah ibn Musa al-Taymi narrated to us, from Usamah ibn Zayd, from Muadh ibn Abdullah ibn Khubayb, from Jabir ibn Usamah al-Juhani, who said: I met the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) among his companions in the market, and I said: Where is the Messenger of Allah heading? They said: He intends to mark out a mosque for your people. He said: So I came after he had marked out a mosque for them, and he planted a piece of wood in its qiblah direction and set it up as the qiblah. This hadith is not narrated from Jabir ibn Usamah except with this chain; Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir is alone in transmitting it."
"9151","Masada narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir narrated to us: Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Urwah narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from Wahb ibn Kaysan, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, that his father died leaving thirty wasqs owed to a Jewish man, so Jabir asked him for respite and he refused to grant him respite. Jabir spoke to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to intercede for him, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to him and spoke to the Jew to take all his dates, but he refused; and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) spoke to him to grant him respite, but he refused. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered and paid him the thirty wasqs in full, and ten awsuq remained over for him. Jabir came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and informed him of the surplus. He found the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praying Asr; when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) finished, he came to him and informed him that he had paid him in full, and informed him of the surplus that remained. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Inform Umar ibn al-Khattab of that. Jabir went to Umar and informed him, and he said: I knew when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) walked among them that Allah would bless them. No one narrated this hadith from Wahb ibn Kaysan except Hisham ibn Urwah, and none narrated it from Hisham except Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya; Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir is alone in transmitting it."
"9152","Masada ibn Sad narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir narrated to us: Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Thabit narrated to us: Abu Bakr ibn al-Numan ibn Abdullah ibn Kab ibn Malik narrated to me, from his father, from his grandfather Kab ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) declared the trees of Madinah inviolable for a barid in a barid, and he sent me and I marked the sanctuary: upon the height of Dhat al-Jaysh, and upon Sharith, and upon Makhid, and upon Nabat. This hadith is not narrated from Kab except with this chain; Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir is alone in transmitting it."
"9153","Masada ibn Sad narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir narrated to us: Abu Damrah narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Abi Asid, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is not lawful for a believer to boycott his brother for more than three days. No one narrated this hadith from Nafi except Ibrahim ibn Abi Asid."
"9154","Masada ibn Sad narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir narrated to us: Man ibn Isa narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Abd al-Aziz al-Laythi, from al-Zuhri, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn Utbah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Al-bid is what is between seven and ten. No one narrated this hadith from al-Zuhri except Abdullah ibn Abd al-Aziz, and none narrated it from Abdullah ibn Abd al-Aziz except Man and Muhammad ibn Khalid ibn Athmah."
"9155","Masada ibn Sad narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir narrated to us: Abd al-Aziz ibn Imran narrated to us: Shibl ibn al-Ala narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I am an Arab, and the Quran is Arabic, and the language of the people of Paradise is Arabic. No one narrated this hadith from Shibl except Abd al-Aziz ibn Imran; Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir is alone in transmitting it, and it is not narrated from Abu Hurayrah except with this chain."
"9156","Masada ibn Sad narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir narrated to us: Man ibn Isa narrated to us, from Adi ibn al-Fadl, from Ayyub al-Sakhtiyani, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, raised up, who said: The hyena is game, and the pilgrim in ihram was forbidden from killing it. No one narrated this hadith from Ayyub except Adi ibn al-Fadl, and none from Adi except Man; Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir is alone in transmitting it."
"9157","Masada ibn Sad narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Sadaqah al-Fadaki narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Sahl ibn Abi Hathmah narrated to us, from his uncle Abu Ufayr ibn Sahl ibn Abi Hathmah, that his father informed him that Abu Burdah ibn Niyar slaughtered a sacrifice at dawn, and when he returned he mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Whoever slaughtered before the prayer, that is not the sacrifice; the sacrifice is only what is slaughtered after the prayer, so go and sacrifice. He said: O Messenger of Allah, I find nothing for sacrifice, and I have nothing except a young goat of the goats. He said: Go and sacrifice with it, and there is no concession in it for anyone after you. This hadith is not narrated from Sahl ibn Abi Hathmah except with this chain; Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir is alone in transmitting it."
"9158","Masada ibn Sad narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Sadaqah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Sahl ibn Abi Hathmah al-Harithi, from his father, from his grandfather, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent his father Abu Hathmah as an estimator, then a man came to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, Abu Hathmah has added extra against me. So he called Abu Hathmah, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Your cousin claims that you added extra against him. He said: O Messenger of Allah, I left the uncovered produce of his family, and what feeds the poor, and what the wind strikes. He said: Your cousin has added to you and been fair. This hadith is not narrated from Sahl ibn Abi Hathmah except with this chain; Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir is alone in transmitting it."
"9159","Masada ibn Sad narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Sadaqah narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Sahl ibn Abi Hathmah al-Harithi narrated to us, from Bashir ibn Abdullah ibn Miktaf ibn Muhayyisah: Sahl ibn Abi Hathmah narrated to me, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out, and Abd al-Rahman ibn Sahl went out with him, and when they were at al-Harrah a snake bit Abd al-Rahman ibn Sahl. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Call Amr ibn Hazm for me. He was called, and he presented his ruqyah to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: There is no harm in it, perform ruqyah on him. Ibn Hazm placed his hand on him and said: O Messenger of Allah, he is dying, or: he has died. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Perform ruqyah on him even if he is dying, or: has died. So he performed ruqyah on him, and Abd al-Rahman recovered and went on. This hadith is not narrated from Sahl except with this chain; Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir is alone in transmitting it."
"9160","Those named Musab: Musab ibn Ibrahim ibn Hamzah ibn Muhammad ibn Hamzah ibn Musab ibn al-Zubayr ibn al-Awwam narrated to us: Ubaydullah ibn Muhammad al-Jahshi narrated to us: My uncle Umar ibn Muhammad narrated to me, from Muhammad ibn Ajlan, from Humayd al-Tawil, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: I served the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for ten years; I never knew anything at all that agreed with him nor anything at all that opposed him; he was content with what Allah decreed, and if one of his wives said: If only you had done such and such, why did you do such? He would say: Leave him, for only what Allah wills will be. And I never saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) take revenge for himself for anything at all except that a sanctity of Allah be violated; if a sanctity was violated he was the angriest of people for the sake of Allah. And never were two matters presented to him but he chose the easier of them, so long as there was no displeasure of Allah in it; if there was displeasure of Allah in it he was the farthest of people from it. No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn Ajlan except Umar ibn Muhammad al-Jahshi; Ubaydullah ibn Muhammad al-Jahshi is alone in transmitting it."
"9161","Musab ibn Ibrahim ibn Hamzah al-Zubayri narrated to us: My father narrated to me: Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad al-Darawardi narrated to us, from Safwan ibn Sulaym, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Said al-Khudri, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: If he refuses, push him back, and if he refuses then fight him, for he is only a devil, concerning the one who passes in front of the praying person. No one narrated this hadith from Safwan ibn Sulaym except al-Darawardi."
"9162","Musab ibn Ibrahim ibn Hamzah al-Zubayri narrated to us: My father narrated to me: Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Abdullah, nephew of al-Zuhri, from his uncle Muhammad ibn Muslim, from Anas ibn Malik, that a Bedouin man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, when will the Hour come? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: And what have you prepared for the Hour? The Bedouin said: I have not prepared for it much deeds except two, except that I love Allah and His Messenger. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Then you are with those whom you love."
"9163","Musab ibn Ibrahim ibn Hamzah narrated to us: My father narrated to me: Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Muslim, from his uncle, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out when the sun had passed its zenith and prayed with them the noon prayer, then when he gave salam he stood on the minbar and mentioned the Hour, and mentioned that before it there are great matters, then he said: Whoever wishes to ask about something, let him ask about it; by Allah, you will not ask me about anything but I will inform you of it so long as I am in this station of mine. Anas said: The people wept much when they heard, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) often said: Ask me whatever you wish. Abdullah ibn Hudhafah al-Sahmi stood and said: Who is my father? He said: Your father is Hudhafah. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) often said, Ask me, Umar stood on his knees and said: O Messenger of Allah, we are pleased with Allah as Lord, with Islam as religion, and with Muhammad as prophet. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fell silent when Umar said that, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, Paradise and Hell were shown to me in the breadth of this wall, and I have never seen like today in good and evil."
"9164","Musab ibn Ibrahim narrated to us: My father narrated to me: Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Abdullah, nephew of al-Zuhri, from his uncle, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn Utbah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) circumambulated the House upon his mount, touching the Corner with his whip."
"9165","Musab ibn Ibrahim narrated to us: My father narrated to me: Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, from the nephew of al-Zuhri, from his uncle, from Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever swears by al-Lat and al-Uzza, let him say: There is no god but Allah; and whoever says to his companion: Come, let me gamble with you, let him give charity."
"9166","Musab narrated to us: My father narrated to me: Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Abdullah, nephew of al-Zuhri, from his uncle, from Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Muawiyah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: For whomever Allah intends good, He gives him understanding in religion; I am only a distributor, and Allah, exalted be His remembrance, gives."
"9167","And with the same chain, from Muhammad ibn Abdullah, nephew of al-Zuhri, from his uncle, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, from Aishah, who said: Salim, the freedman of Abu Hudhayfah, was the freedman of a woman of the Ansar, and Abu Hudhayfah had adopted him just as the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had adopted Zayd ibn Harithah. And whoever adopted a man in the Jahiliyyah, people attributed him to him and he inherited from his inheritance, until Allah revealed: Call them by their fathers; that is more just with Allah."
"9168","Musab narrated to us: My father narrated to me: Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Abdullah, nephew of al-Zuhri, from his uncle, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, from Aishah, that a woman used to borrow jewelry in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and then deny it, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered her hand to be cut. Al-Zuhri said: And al-Qasim ibn Muhammad narrated to me, from Aishah, who said: That woman then married a man of Banu Sulaym, and she was with him well-dressed; she would come to me and I would convey her need to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"9169","And with the same chain, from the nephew of al-Zuhri, from his uncle, from Urwah, from Aishah, who said: The sun eclipsed during the lifetime of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he prayed with the people, the long hadith in full."
"9170","And with the same chain, from the nephew of al-Zuhri, from his uncle, from Kathir ibn al-Abbas, that Abdullah ibn Abbas used to narrate about the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day the sun eclipsed in Madinah, that he did not add more than two rakahs like the morning prayer."
"9171","And with the same chain, from the nephew of al-Zuhri, from his uncle, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah, from Ibn Abbas, that he heard Abu Talhah saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The angels do not enter a house in which there is a dog or an image."
"9172","And with the same chain, from the nephew of al-Zuhri, from his uncle, from Salim, from his father, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: While I was sleeping I saw myself circumambulating, and there was a brown man with lank hair between two men, his head dripping. I said: Who is this? They said: Isa son of Maryam. I went and turned, and there was a red bulky man with curly head, blind in the right eye, as if his eye were a protruding grape. I said: Who is this? They said: The Dajjal; the closest of people to him in resemblance is Ibn Qatan."
"9173","And with the same chain, from the nephew of al-Zuhri, from his uncle, from Salim, from his father, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The Jews will fight you and you will gain mastery over them, until the stone says: O servant of Allah, this is a Jew behind me, so kill him."
"9174","And with the same chain, from the nephew of al-Zuhri, from his uncle, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: There will enter Paradise from my nation a group of seventy thousand, and the light of their faces like the light of the moon on the night of full moon."
"9175","And with the same chain, from the nephew of al-Zuhri, from his uncle, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If you say to your companion on Friday, Be quiet, while the imam is preaching, you have engaged in idle talk."
"9176","And with the same chain, from the nephew of al-Zuhri, from his uncle, from Abu Salamah, from Aishah, that Abu Bakr entered the mosque while Umar was speaking to the people, and he went on until he entered the house of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in which he had died, and it was in the house of Aishah, and he uncovered from the face of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a Hibarah cloak with which he had been covered, and he looked at his face and bent over him kissing him."
"9177","And with the same chain, from the nephew of al-Zuhri, from his uncle, from Anas, that he heard the last sermon of Umar, when Abu Bakr sat upon the minbar of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and that was the morning after the day the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) died."
"9178","And with the same chain, from the nephew of al-Zuhri, from his uncle, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon her while she was screened with a curtain in which there was an image of figures, so he tore it down and then said: The most severely punished of people are those who imitate the creation of Allah."
"9179","And with the same chain: from Muhammad ibn Abdullah, nephew of al-Zuhri, from his uncle, from Ubayd ibn al-Sabbaq, who said: Ibn Abbas informed me that Maymunah informed him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) woke one morning gloomy, so Maymunah said to him: O Messenger of Allah, I noticed your appearance today. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) remained that day upon that, then there occurred in his mind a puppy that was under a table of ours, so he ordered it and it was taken out, then he took water in his hand and sprinkled its place. When evening came, Jibril, peace be upon him, met him, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: You had promised to meet me last night. He said: Yes, but we do not enter a house in which there is a dog or an image. None narrated these hadiths from the nephew of al-Zuhri except al-Darawardi; Ibrahim ibn Hamzah is alone in transmitting them."
"9180","Musab narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn Hamzah narrated to us: My father narrated to me: Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Abu Bakr ibn Nafi, from his father, from Safiyyah bint Abi Ubayd, who said: I heard Umar ibn al-Khattab saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever goes to a fortune-teller, his prayer will not be accepted for forty nights. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Bakr ibn Nafi except al-Darawardi."
"9181","Musab narrated to us, saying: My father narrated to me: Abdullah ibn Musab ibn Thabit ibn Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from al-Zubayr, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah favored Quraysh with seven qualities: He favored them in that they worshipped Allah for ten years with none worshipping Him but a Qurashi; He favored them in that He aided them on the Day of the Elephant while they were polytheists; He favored them in that a surah of the Quran was revealed about them in which none other than them was included: For the protection of Quraysh; He favored them in that among them are prophethood, the caliphate, the covering of the Kabah, and the providing of water to pilgrims. No one narrated this hadith from Hisham ibn Urwah except Abdullah ibn Musab, and it is not narrated from al-Zubayr except with this chain."
"9182","Musab ibn Ibrahim ibn Hamzah narrated to us: Isa ibn Mina, Qalun, narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Jafar ibn Abi Kathir narrated to us, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Harith, from Ali, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Shall I not point you to what removes the rancor of the chest? Fasting three days of every month. No one narrated this hadith from Musa ibn Uqbah except Muhammad ibn Jafar; Isa ibn Mina, Qalun, is alone in transmitting it."
"9183","Musab ibn Ibrahim al-Zubayri narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir al-Hizami narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Dinar narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Umar, from Amir ibn Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr, from Amr ibn Sulaym, from Abu Qatadah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you enters the mosque, let him not sit until he prays two rakahs."
"9184","Musab narrated to us: My father narrated to me: Ayyub ibn Abi Khalid al-Khayyat narrated to us: Umarah ibn Ghaziyyah narrated to me, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: While a man was walking in a fine suit, admiring himself, the earth swallowed him, and he will be sinking in it until the Day of Resurrection. No one narrated this hadith from Umarah ibn Ghaziyyah except Ayyub ibn Abi Khalid; Ibrahim ibn Hamzah is alone in transmitting it."
"9185","Those named Muwarri: Muwarri ibn Abdullah Abu Dhuhl al-Massisi narrated to us: al-Hasan ibn Isa al-Harbi narrated to us: Rawh ibn al-Musayyib narrated to us, from Yazid al-Rishk, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Intercession was only made for the people of major sins of my nation. No one narrated this hadith from Yazid al-Rishk except Rawh ibn al-Musayyib; al-Hasan ibn Isa is alone in transmitting it."
"9186","Muwarri ibn Abdullah narrated to us: Dawud ibn Muadh, son of the daughter of Makhlad ibn al-Husayn, narrated to us: Mismar ibn Abd al-Malik narrated to us, from Sarrar ibn Mujashshir Abu Ubaydah, from Ayyub al-Sakhtiyani, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: People of this nation will delve deeply until one of them says: This is Allah who created me, so who created Him? No one narrated this hadith from Sarrar except Mismar; Dawud ibn Muadh is alone in transmitting it."
"9187","Muwarri ibn Abdullah narrated to us: Umar ibn Yazid al-Sayyari narrated to us: Abd al-Warith narrated to us, from Layth, from Mujahid, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever goes to women in their backsides has disbelieved. No one narrated this hadith from Layth except Abd al-Warith; Umar ibn Yazid is alone in transmitting it."
"9188","Muwarri narrated to us: Dawud narrated to us: Thabit ibn Zuhayr narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The one who plays with dice is like one who puts his hand in the flesh of swine, and the one who looks at it is like one who puts his hand in the blood of swine."
"9189","Muwarri ibn Abdullah narrated to us: Dawud ibn Muadh narrated to us: Thabit ibn Zuhayr narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, who said: A Bedouin came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Prophet of Allah, I saw last night in a dream that there is no servant who testifies that there is no god but Allah and testifies that you are the Messenger of Allah but Allah raises him a degree in Paradise, except the companions of al-shah, and it is chess. None narrated these two hadiths from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, except Thabit ibn Zuhayr; Dawud ibn Muadh is alone in transmitting them."
"9190","Muwarri ibn Abdullah narrated to us: Dawud ibn Muadh narrated to us: Thabit ibn Zuhayr narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The caravan in which there is a bell is not accompanied by the angels. No one narrated this hadith from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, except Thabit ibn Zuhayr. And people narrated it from Nafi, from Salim, from al-Jarrah, from Umm Habibah."
"9191","Muwarri ibn Abdullah narrated to us: Dawud ibn Muadh narrated to us: Ayyub ibn Waqid narrated to us, from al-Amash, from al-Minhal ibn Amr, from Abbad ibn Ubaydullah al-Asadi, from Ali, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to seek refuge for al-Hasan and al-Husayn: I seek refuge for you two in the perfect words of Allah, from every devil and vermin, and from every envious eye. No one narrated this hadith from al-Amash, from al-Minhal, from Abbad, except Ayyub ibn Waqid; Dawud ibn Muadh is alone in transmitting it. And Abu Hafs al-Abbar narrated it from al-Amash, from al-Minhal ibn Amr, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas."
"9192","Muwarri ibn Abdullah narrated to us: al-Hasan ibn Isa narrated to us: Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, from al-Ala ibn al-Musayyib, from al-Hakam ibn Utaybah, from Jafar, from Sawdah bint Zamah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The woman with prolonged bleeding leaves prayer during the days of her menstrual periods in which she used to sit, then she takes one bath, then she performs ablution for every prayer. No one narrated this hadith from al-Hakam except al-Ala ibn al-Musayyib, and none from al-Ala except Hafs ibn Ghiyath; al-Hasan ibn Isa is alone in transmitting it."
"9193","Those named Mufaddal: Mufaddal ibn Muhammad al-Janadi narrated to us: Ali ibn Ziyad al-Lahji narrated to us: Abu Qurrah Musa ibn Tariq narrated to us, saying: Zamah ibn Salih mentioned it, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, that he heard Umaymah bint Ruqayqah saying: I pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he stipulated upon me what he stipulated upon the believing women, then he said: In what you are able. No one narrated this hadith from Musa ibn Uqbah except Abu Qurrah."
"9194","Mufaddal ibn Muhammad al-Janadi narrated to us: Ali ibn Ziyad al-Lahji narrated to us: Abu Qurrah narrated to us, saying: Ibn Jurayj mentioned: Warqa ibn Umar informed me that Ata informed him that Abdullah ibn Abbas called al-Fadl on the Day of Arafah and he said: I am fasting. Abdullah said: Do not fast, for the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought a milking vessel in which there was milk, and he drank from it on this day, and people follow your example. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Jurayj except Abu Qurrah."
"9195","Mufaddal narrated to us: Ali narrated to us: Abu Qurrah narrated to us, saying: Zamah ibn Salih mentioned, from Ziyad ibn Sad, from al-Zuhri, from Muhammad ibn Jubayr ibn Mutim, that Jubayr ibn Mutim narrated to him that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The one who severs kinship will not enter Paradise. No one narrated this hadith from Ziyad ibn Sad except Zamah; Abu Qurrah is alone in transmitting it."
"9196","And with the same chain: Abu Qurrah narrated to us, saying: Zamah ibn Salih mentioned, from Ziyad ibn Sad, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Ibn Abbas, who said: Shall I not show you how I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) perform ablution? He took water with one of his hands and sniffed it into his nose, then joined the other to it and poured and flowed it over his face, and washed his hands, then wiped his head and his ears, then wiped over the tops of his feet above the sandals, then stood and prayed. No one narrated this hadith from Ziyad ibn Sad except Zamah; Abu Qurrah is alone in transmitting it."
"9197","And with the same chain: Abu Qurrah narrated to us, saying: Zamah mentioned, from Ziyad ibn Sad, from Abu al-Zubayr: Yunus ibn Khabbab al-Kufi narrated to me, saying: I heard Abu Ubaydah ibn Abdullah ibn Masud mentioning that he heard Abdullah ibn Masud saying: He was with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a journey to Makkah, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he went out to relieve himself, would go far so that no one would see him. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw two distant trees and said: O Ibn Masud, go to these two trees and say to them: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commands you to join together for him so that he may conceal himself with you. So one of them walked to the other, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) relieved himself, then they returned to their places. Then he went on until we came to the lanes of Madinah, and a camel came running until it prostrated to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then stood before him with its eyes shedding tears. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Who is the owner of this camel? They said: So-and-so. He said: Call him for me. They brought him, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: What is the matter with you and this camel complains of you? He said: O Messenger of Allah, we have used this camel for drawing water for twenty years, then we intended to slaughter it. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He complained of that; evil is how you repaid him: you used him for twenty years until, when his bones grew thin and his skin grew thin, you intended to slaughter him; sell him to me. They said: Rather he is yours, O Messenger of Allah. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered concerning him and sent him with the riding camels. His companions said to him: O Messenger of Allah, this camel prostrated to you and we are more deserving of prostration. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah forbid that one should prostrate to anyone; if one were to prostrate to anyone I would have commanded the woman to prostrate to her husband. No one narrated this hadith from Ziyad ibn Sad except Zamah; Abu Qurrah is alone in transmitting it."
"9198","Mufaddal narrated to us: Ali ibn Ziyad al-Lahji narrated to us: Abu Qurrah Musa ibn Tariq narrated to us, saying: Zamah ibn Salih mentioned, from Ziyad ibn Sad, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), from Allah, He said: If My servant remembers Me alone, I remember him alone; and if he remembers Me in a gathering, I remember him in a gathering of angels; and if he comes to Me walking, I come to him hastening. No one narrated this hadith from Ziyad ibn Sad except Zamah; Abu Qurrah is alone in transmitting it."
"9199","And with the same chain: Abu Qurrah narrated to us, saying: Zamah ibn Salih mentioned, from Ziyad ibn Sad, from al-Zuhri, from Malik ibn Aws ibn al-Hadathan, from Umar ibn al-Khattab, that he said: Allah singled out the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from this fay with something He did not give anyone other than him. Allah Almighty said: And what Allah restored to His Messenger from them, you did not press forward upon it any horse or camel, the verse. So this was exclusively for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); by Allah, he did not choose it apart from you, nor keep it selfishly from you; he gave it to you until there remained of it this wealth that remains. He said: And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to spend upon his family their yearly maintenance from this wealth, then take what remained and make it as the wealth of Allah. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) acted thus his whole life until he died. Then Umar said afterwards to Uthman and Abd al-Rahman and al-Zubayr and Sad, while they were with him: I adjure you by Allah, do you know that? They said: Yes. No one narrated this hadith from Ziyad except Zamah; Abu Qurrah is alone in transmitting it."
"9200","Mufaddal ibn Muhammad al-Janadi narrated to us: Ali ibn Ziyad narrated to us: Abu Qurrah narrated to us, saying: Zamah mentioned, from Ziyad ibn Sad, from al-Zuhri, that Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to him, that he heard Abu Hurayrah saying: The prayer was established, so we stood and straightened the rows before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to us. No one narrated this hadith from Ziyad ibn Sad except Zamah; Abu Qurrah is alone in transmitting it."
"9201","And with the same chain: Abu Qurrah narrated to us, saying: Zamah mentioned, from Ziyad ibn Sad, from al-Zuhri, from Safwan ibn Abdullah, from Abu al-Darda, from Kab ibn Asim al-Ashari, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Righteousness is not fasting while traveling. No one narrated this hadith from Ziyad except Zamah; Abu Qurrah is alone in transmitting it."
"9202","Mufaddal narrated to us: Abu Humah narrated to us: Abu Qurrah narrated to us, from Zamah ibn Salih, from Ziyad ibn Sad, from Aban, from Anas, who said: When we raised our heads from bowing, none of us would put his head down until we saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prostrating. No one narrated this hadith from Ziyad except Zamah; Abu Qurrah is alone in transmitting it."
"9203","Mufaddal narrated to us: Abu Humah narrated to us: Abu Qurrah narrated to us, saying: Zamah mentioned, from Ziyad ibn Sad, from Aban: Anas narrated to me that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: When the call to prayer is made, Satan turns back between him and al-Rawha until he does not hear the voice of the call, and the doors of heaven and the doors of Paradise are opened, and supplication is answered. No one narrated this hadith from Ziyad except Zamah; Abu Qurrah is alone in transmitting it."
"9204","Mufaddal narrated to us: Abu Humah narrated to us: Abu Qurrah narrated to us, saying: Zamah mentioned, from Ziyad ibn Sad, from Zayd ibn Aslam, who said: I heard my father narrating, from Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Eat olive oil and anoint with it, for it comes from a blessed tree. No one narrated this hadith except Zamah; Abu Qurrah is alone in transmitting it."
"9205","And with the same chain: Abu Qurrah narrated to us, saying: Zamah mentioned, from Ziyad ibn Sad, from Abu al-Zubayr, that he heard Jabir saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) slaughtered seventy camels on the Day of al-Hudaybiyyah, sharing each seven in one camel."
"9206","Mufaddal narrated to us: Ali ibn Ziyad al-Lahji narrated to us: Abu Qurrah narrated to us, saying: Zamah mentioned, from Ziyad ibn Sad, from Abu al-Zubayr, that he heard Jabir saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) shaved at al-Hudaybiyyah, and many of his companions shaved. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: May Allah have mercy on those who shave. A man said: O Messenger of Allah, and those who shorten? He said: May Allah have mercy on those who shave. He said on the third time: And those who shorten."
"9207","And with the same chain: He said: Zamah mentioned, from Ziyad ibn Sad, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, while mentioning the False Messiah: I shall tell you about him a word no prophet before me said: He is one-eyed, and Allah is not one-eyed; between his eyes is writing: disbeliever. Jabir said, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Every believer, literate and illiterate, will read it. He will roam the earth for forty days, entering every land except these two: Madinah and Makkah; Allah has forbidden them to him. One of his days is like a year, and a day like a month, and a day like Friday, then the rest of his days like these days of yours; there remain only forty days."
"9208","And with the same chain: He said: Zamah mentioned, from Ziyad ibn Sad, from Abu al-Zubayr, that he heard Jabir ibn Abdullah saying: Umm Salamah asked permission of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for cupping, and he gave her permission, so she sent to a foster mother of hers, and she cupped her."
"9209","And with the same chain: He said: Zamah mentioned, from Ziyad ibn Sad, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no servant but upon his head is a knotted silk thread; when he wakes and praises Allah, and stands and performs ablution and prays, the knots are untied; and if he wakes and does not praise Allah, Satan says to him: Upon you is a long night, sleep on. So Satan ties the silk upon him."
"9210","Mufaddal narrated to us: Abu Humah narrated to us: Abu Qurrah narrated to us, from Zamah ibn Salih, from Ziyad ibn Sad, from Abu al-Zubayr, that he heard Jabir ibn Abdullah saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent us with Abu Ubaydah ibn al-Jarrah, and we were six hundred and a few men, to meet the caravan of Quraysh. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) found for us no provision except a bag of dates; he would give us a date a date each day, which we would suck and drink water over. We felt its loss when it ran out. Then we turned to tree leaves, beating them down with our sticks, then eating them fine and drinking water over them, until we were called the army of leaves. We passed by the seashore, and the sea cast out for us a beast called al-anbar, like a sand dune. Abu Ubaydah said: It is carrion, not lawful for us. Then he said afterwards: Rather we are in the path of Allah, and we are compelled. So we ate from it for about half a month and more, and we cut strips of dried meat in plenty; we would scoop out fat from the socket of its eye with jars until we finished it. Thirteen men of us sat in the socket of its eye. Then Abu Ubaydah took a rib of its ribs and set it upon its two ends, and ordered the tallest camel in the riding party to be saddled; a man rode upon it and passed under it without touching his head. We came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Do you have anything of it with you? We said: Yes. He said: Feed us of it. So we sent him dried strips, and he ate of them. None narrated these hadiths from Ziyad ibn Sad except Zamah; Abu Qurrah is alone in transmitting them."
"9211","Mufaddal narrated to us: Ali narrated to us: Abu Qurrah narrated to us, saying: Zamah mentioned, from Ziyad ibn Sad, from al-Zuhri, from Nafi, freedman of Abu Qatadah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: What will you do when the son of Maryam descends and your imam is from among you? None narrated it from Ziyad except Zamah; Abu Qurrah is alone in transmitting it."
"9212","Mufaddal ibn Muhammad narrated to us: Ali ibn Ziyad narrated to us: Abu Qurrah narrated to us, saying: Zamah mentioned, from Ziyad ibn Sad, from al-Zuhri, from Hind bint al-Harith, she narrated to him, from Umm Salamah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) woke one night saying: Glory be to Allah, what treasures have been sent down? And what tribulations have been sent down? Who will wake the dwellers of the chambers? Many a clothed one in this world will be naked in the Hereafter. No one narrated this hadith from Ziyad ibn Sad except Zamah; Abu Qurrah is alone in transmitting it."
"9213","Mufaddal narrated to us: Ali ibn Ziyad narrated to us: Abu Qurrah narrated to us, saying: Zamah ibn Salih mentioned, from Yaqub ibn Ata, from al-Zuhri, from Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman, that his mother Umm Kulthum bint Uqbah ibn Abi Muayt informed him that she heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The liar is not the one who makes peace between people, saying good or conveying good. She said: And I did not hear him permit anything of what people call lying except in three: in war, in reconciliation, and in a man speaking to his wife."
"9214","Mufaddal ibn Muhammad narrated to us: Ali ibn Ziyad narrated to us: Abu Qurrah narrated to us, saying: Zamah mentioned, from Yaqub ibn Ata, from al-Zuhri: Abu Bakr ibn Hazm informed me, from Urwah, from Aishah, who said: A woman with two sons came to me, and I found nothing for her except a date, so I gave it to her, and she split it between them."
"9215","And with the same chain: He said: Zamah mentioned, from Yaqub ibn Ata, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Idris, that Abu Thalabah al-Khushani informed him that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbidding every carnivore with fangs among beasts."
"9216","And with the same chain: He said: Zamah mentioned, from Yaqub ibn Ata, from Nafi, from Abdullah ibn Umar, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he stood between the two jamrahs in the Hajj which he performed, and that was on the Day of Sacrifice, and he said: This is the day of the Greater Hajj."
"9217","And with the same chain: He said: Zamah mentioned, from Yaqub ibn Ata, from al-Zuhri, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah, from Abu Said al-Khudri, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade wrapping in one garment and that a man sit with his knees drawn up in a single garment with nothing of it over his private part."
"9218","And with the same chain: He said: Zamah mentioned, from Yaqub ibn Ata, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, that he heard Abu Hurayrah saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever obeys me has obeyed Allah, and whoever disobeys me has disobeyed Allah; and whoever obeys my commander has obeyed me, and whoever disobeys my commander has disobeyed me."
"9219","Mufaddal ibn Muhammad narrated to us: Abu Humah narrated to us: Abu Qurrah narrated to us, saying: Zamah mentioned, from Yaqub ibn Ata, from al-Zuhri, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith ibn Hisham, from Aishah, that she said, and she mentioned Zaynab bint Jahsh, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), saying: I never saw any woman at all better in religion than Zaynab: more God-fearing, more truthful in speech, more joining of kinship, greater in charity, and more self-sacrificing in the work by which charity is given and nearness to Allah is sought."
"9220","Mufaddal narrated to us: Ali ibn Ziyad narrated to us: Abu Qurrah narrated to us, saying: Zamah mentioned, from Yaqub ibn Ata, from al-Zuhri, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah, from Umm Qays bint Mihsan, and she was among the first emigrant women who pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and she was the sister of Ukkashah ibn Mihsan, she informed him, that she brought the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a son of hers who had not reached eating food, and she informed him that her son urinated in the lap of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called for water and sprinkled it over his urine, and did not wash it with washing."
"9221","Mufaddal narrated to us: Ali ibn Ziyad narrated to us: Abu Qurrah narrated to us, saying: Zamah mentioned, from Yaqub ibn Ata, from al-Zuhri, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah, from Ibn Abbas, that Sad ibn Ubadah consulted the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about a vow that was upon his mother to fulfill it on her behalf, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded him to fulfill it on her behalf. None narrated these hadiths from Yaqub ibn Ata except Zamah; Abu Qurrah is alone in transmitting them."
"9222","Mufaddal narrated to us: Abu Humah narrated to us: Abu Qurrah narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ibn al-Huwayrith, from Nuaym al-Mujmir, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: My nation, bright-faced and bright-limbed on the Day of Resurrection; so whoever can improve his brightness, let him do so. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Jurayj except Abu Qurrah."
"9223","Mufaddal narrated to us: Abu Humah narrated to us: Abu Qurrah narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj: Abu Qazah informed me, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked for water for ablution, and it was said to him: We found that only in the skin of a dead animal. He said: Did you tan it? They said: Yes. He said: Then bring it, for that is its purification. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Jurayj except Abu Qurrah."
"9224","And with the same chain Abu Qurrah narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Abu Khalid, that he informed him, from Awn ibn Abi Juhayfah, from his father Abu Juhayfah, who said: I prayed with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at al-Abtah, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was in a dome of leather, and he performed ablution in a stone vessel; Bilal came out with its remainder, and he prayed Zuhr and Asr, with man and woman and donkey passing before him from beyond the spear. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Jurayj except Abu Qurrah. And Abu Khalid from whom Ibn Jurayj narrated this hadith is al-Dalani."
"9225","Mufaddal narrated to us: Ali ibn Ziyad narrated to us: Abu Qurrah narrated to us, saying: Ibn Jurayj mentioned, from Qays, that he informed him, from Abu Ishaq, that he heard him saying: Abdullah ibn Abi Sufyan informed me that he heard Ubayy ibn Kab informing, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he missed some men at Fajr and said: Where is so-and-so? And where is so-and-so? He said: There is no prayer heavier upon the hypocrite than the Isha and Fajr prayers; if they knew what is in them they would come to them even crawling. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Jurayj except Abu Qurrah. And Qays from whom Ibn Jurayj narrated this hadith is Qays ibn al-Rabi."
"9226","Mufaddal narrated to us: Abu Humah narrated to us: Abu Qurrah narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj: Yahya informed me, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was the lightest of people in prayer while completing it. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Jurayj except Abu Qurrah. And Yahya from whom Ibn Jurayj narrated this hadith is Yahya ibn Said al-Ansari."
"9227","Mufaddal ibn Muhammad narrated to us: Abu Humah narrated to us: Abu Qurrah narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from al-Ala ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Mabad ibn Kab ibn Malik, from his brother Abdullah ibn Kab, who said: I heard Abu Umamah, companion of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), saying: Whoever cuts off the right of a Muslim by his oath, Allah has made the Fire obligatory for him and forbidden Paradise to him. A man said: Even a small thing, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Even if it be a stick of arak. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Jurayj except Abu Qurrah."
"9228","Mufaddal ibn Muhammad narrated to us: Abu Humah narrated to us: Abu Qurrah narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj: Ismail ibn Umayyah informed me, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Suhayb, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: I served the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for ten years; he never said to me about something I did: Why did you do it? Nor about something I did not do: Why did you not do it? He said: And Mamar added to me in it: about anything at all. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Jurayj except Abu Qurrah and Abd al-Majid ibn Abi Rawwad."
"9229","Chapter of Nun, those named Nasr: Nasr ibn Abd al-Malik al-Sinjari narrated to us: Mamar ibn Muhammad ibn Ubaydullah ibn Abi Rafi narrated to us: My father Muhammad ibn Ubaydullah narrated to me, from his father Ubaydullah ibn Abi Rafi, from Salma, wife of Abu Rafi, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was above his house sitting, and he said: O Salma, bring me washing water. I brought him a vessel in which there was lote water, and I strained it for him. Then he knelt upon a cushion stuffed with fiber, and I poured upon his head and washed it, and I was looking at every drop dripping from his head into the vessel, as if it were shining pearls. Then I brought him water and washed him. When he finished his washing he said: O Salma, pour what is in the vessel in a place no one steps over. I took the vessel and drank some of it, then poured the rest. He said to me: What did you do with what was in the vessel? I said: O Messenger of Allah, I envied the earth for it, so I drank some of it, then poured the rest upon the earth. He said: Go, Allah has thereby forbidden you to the Fire. This hadith is not narrated from Salma except with this chain; Mamar ibn Muhammad is alone in transmitting it."
"9230","Nasr ibn Abd al-Malik narrated to us: Mamar ibn Muhammad ibn Ubaydullah ibn Abi Rafi narrated to us: Muhammad narrated to me, from his father Ubaydullah ibn Abi Rafi, from his father Abu Rafi, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the ear of one of you rings, let him remember me, and send blessings upon me, and let him say: May Allah mention with good whoever mentioned me. This hadith is not narrated from Abu Rafi except with this chain; Mamar ibn Muhammad is alone in transmitting it."
"9231","Nasr ibn al-Hakam al-Marwazi narrated to us: Ali ibn Hujr narrated to us: Yahya ibn Sabiq narrated to us: Abu Hazim narrated to us, from Sahl ibn Sad al-Saidi, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every nation has Magians, and every nation has Christians, and every nation has Jews; and the Magians of my nation are the Qadariyyah, and their Christians are the Khashabiyyah, and their Jews are the Murjiah. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Hazim except Yahya ibn Sabiq; Ali ibn Hujr is alone in transmitting it."
"9232","Nasr ibn al-Hakam al-Marwazi narrated to us: Ali ibn Hujr narrated to us: Attab ibn Bashir narrated to us, from Khusayf, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, from Abu Said al-Khudri, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Gold for gold, and silver for silver, like for like. None mastered the chain of this hadith from Khusayf except Attab ibn Bashir."
"9233","Nasr ibn al-Hakam al-Marwazi narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Bassam al-Marwazi narrated to us: Abdullah ibn Jafar al-Madani narrated to us: Nafi ibn Abi Nuaym narrated to us, from Said al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to the people of Madinah: O Allah, bless them in their sa and their mudd. No one narrated this hadith from Nafi ibn Abi Nuaym except Abdullah ibn Jafar; Muhammad ibn Bassam al-Marwazi is alone in transmitting it."
"9234","Those named Nuaym: Nuaym ibn Muhammad al-Suri narrated to us: Musa ibn Ayyub al-Nasibini narrated to us: Damrah ibn Rabiah narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Shawdhab, from Abdullah ibn al-Qasim, from Kathir, freedman of Abd al-Rahman ibn Samurah, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Samurah, who said: Uthman came when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was equipping the army of hardship, with a thousand dinars in his sleeve, and poured them into the lap of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) inserting his hand into them and turning them over, saying: No harm will befall Ibn Affan for what he does after today. He said it twice. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Shawdhab except Damrah, and it is not narrated from Abd al-Rahman ibn Samurah except with this chain."
"9235","Nuaym ibn Muhammad narrated to us: Musa ibn Ayyub narrated to us: Marwan ibn Muawiyah al-Fazari narrated to us, from Mughirah ibn Muslim al-Sarraj, from Abdullah ibn Buraydah, from Muawiyah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is pleased that the children of Adam stand glorifying him while standing, the Fire is assured for him. No one narrated this hadith from Abdullah ibn Buraydah except Mughirah ibn Muslim; Marwan ibn Muawiyah is alone in transmitting it."
"9236","Nuaym ibn Muhammad al-Suri narrated to us: Musa ibn Ayyub al-Nasibini narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Shuayb ibn Shabur narrated to us, from Khalid ibn Dihqan: Abdullah ibn Abi Zakariyya narrated to us, from Umm al-Darda, from Abu al-Darda, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Every sin may Allah forgive, except one who dies a polytheist, or a believer who kills a believer deliberately."
"9237","Nuaym ibn Muhammad narrated to us: Musa ibn Ayyub al-Nasibini narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Shuayb ibn Shabur narrated to us, from Khalid ibn Dihqan, from Abdullah ibn Abi Zakariyya, from Umm al-Darda, from Abu al-Darda, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The believer keeps going swiftly in good so long as he does not shed unlawful blood; when he sheds unlawful blood he is stuck. None narrated these two hadiths from Abdullah ibn Abi Zakariyya except Khalid ibn Dihqan; Muhammad ibn Shuayb is alone in transmitting them."
"9238","Nuaym ibn Muhammad al-Suri narrated to us: Musa ibn Ayyub al-Nasibini narrated to us: Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Hasan Abu Masud al-Zajjaj narrated to us, from Abu Bakr al-Hudhali, from al-Hasan and Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Aishah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever changes the religion of Allah, kill him. This hadith is not narrated from Aishah except with this chain; Musa ibn Ayyub is alone in transmitting it."
"9239","Nuaym ibn Muhammad al-Suri narrated to us: Musa ibn Ayyub narrated to us: al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, from Zuhayr ibn Muhammad, from Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Three whose prayer is not accepted, and no good deed of theirs ascends to Allah: the drunk until he sobers, the woman with whom her husband is angry, and the runaway slave until he returns and puts his hand in the hand of his masters."
"9240","And with the same chain: from Jabir ibn Abdullah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Any slave who dies while runaway will enter the Fire, even if he is killed in the path of Allah. None narrated these two hadiths from Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil except Zuhayr ibn Muhammad; al-Walid is alone in transmitting them, and they are not narrated from Jabir except with this chain."
"9241","Nuaym ibn Muhammad al-Suri narrated to us: Musa ibn Ayyub narrated to us: al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Abu al-Zubayr, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the hire of the stallion, and selling water, and selling tillage. No one narrated this hadith in this complete form from Ibn Jurayj except al-Walid ibn Muslim."
"9242","Nuaym ibn Muhammad al-Suri narrated to us: Musa ibn Ayyub narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Shuayb narrated to us: Suwayd ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The boundary of the road is seven cubits. No one narrated this hadith from Abu al-Zubayr except Suwayd; Muhammad ibn Shuayb is alone in transmitting it."
"9243","Nuaym ibn Muhammad al-Suri narrated to us: Musa ibn Ayyub al-Nasibini narrated to us: Abu Masud al-Zajjaj narrated to us, from Abu Bakr al-Hudhali, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, who said: I was presented to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the Day of Badr when I was thirteen years old, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent me back. Then I was presented to him on the Day of Uhud when I was fourteen and he sent me back. Then I was presented on the Day of the Confederates when I was fifteen and I was allowed. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Bakr al-Hudhali except Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Hasan; Musa ibn Ayyub is alone in transmitting it."
"9244","Nuaym ibn Muhammad al-Suri narrated to us: Musa ibn Ayyub al-Nasibini narrated to us: Abdullah ibn Khalid narrated to us, from Ghalib ibn Ubaydullah, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever enters ihram from Bayt al-Maqdis will enter forgiven. No one narrated this hadith from Nafi except Ghalib ibn Ubaydullah; Musa ibn Ayyub is alone in transmitting it."
"9245","Nuaym ibn Muhammad narrated to us: Musa ibn Ayyub narrated to us: al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, from Shayban, from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid, from Qays ibn Abi Hazim, from al-Mustawrid ibn Shaddad, from his father, who said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and took his hand, and it was softer than silk and cooler than snow. No one narrated this hadith from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid except Shayban; al-Walid ibn Muslim is alone in transmitting it."
"9246","Those named Numan: al-Numan ibn Ahmad al-Wasiti, the judge, narrated to us: Salih ibn Muhammad al-Kilabi narrated to us: Ali ibn Asim narrated to us, from Khalid and Awf and Sawwar the judge, from Abu al-Minhal, from Abu Barzah al-Aslami, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade sleeping before Isha and talking after it. No one narrated this hadith from Sawwar except Ali ibn Asim; Salih ibn Muhammad al-Kilabi is alone in transmitting it."
"9247","al-Numan ibn Ahmad al-Wasiti narrated to us: Abdullah ibn Hamzah al-Zubayri narrated to us: Abdullah ibn Nafi narrated to us, from Nafi ibn Abi Nuaym, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to shorten the prayer at al-Aqiq. No one narrated this hadith as raised from Nafi ibn Abi Nuaym except Abdullah ibn Nafi; Abdullah ibn Hamzah is alone in transmitting it."
"9248","al-Numan ibn Ahmad narrated to us: Ishaq ibn Shahin narrated to us: Hushaym narrated to us, from Yunus and Hisham, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you come to prayer, let each of you walk calmly; let him pray what he catches and make up what he missed. No one narrated this hadith from Yunus except Hushaym; Ishaq ibn Shahin is alone in transmitting it."
"9249","al-Numan ibn Ahmad narrated to us: Muqaddam ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us: My uncle al-Qasim ibn Yahya narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Uthman, from al-Amash, from al-Hakam, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Whoever relieves a distress of the distresses of a Muslim in this world, Allah will relieve from him a distress of the distresses of the Hereafter; and whoever covers the shame of a Muslim in this world, Allah will cover his shame in this world and the Hereafter; and whoever eases for one in hardship in this world, Allah will ease for him in this world and the Hereafter; and Allah is in the aid of the servant so long as the servant is in the aid of his brother. None placed al-Hakam between al-Amash and Abu Salih among those who narrated this hadith from al-Amash except Abu Shaybah, and none narrated it from Abu Shaybah except al-Qasim ibn Yahya; Muqaddam ibn Muhammad is alone in transmitting it."
"9250","al-Numan narrated to us: Muqaddam ibn Muhammad narrated to us: My uncle al-Qasim ibn Yahya narrated to us, from Abu Hamzah al-Awar, from Abu al-Hakam al-Bajali, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: If the people of heaven and the people of earth gathered to kill a believing man, Allah would cast them into the Fire. No one narrated this hadith from Abu al-Hakam al-Bajali, and he is Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Nuaym, except Abu Hamzah, and none from Abu Hamzah except al-Qasim ibn Yahya; Muqaddam ibn Muhammad is alone in transmitting it."
"9251","al-Numan ibn Ahmad narrated to us: Muqaddam ibn Muhammad narrated to us: My uncle al-Qasim ibn Yahya narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Ubayd ibn Umayr, from Aishah, who said: A woman came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asking him what Allah permits for a man of his wife while she is menstruating? He said: What is above the navel. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Khuthaym except al-Qasim; Muqaddam is alone in transmitting it."
"9252","al-Numan narrated to us: Muqaddam narrated to us: My uncle al-Qasim narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Uthman, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Aishah, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray while I was right beside him. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Khuthaym except al-Qasim ibn Yahya; Muqaddam is alone in transmitting it."
"9253","al-Numan ibn Ahmad narrated to us: al-Sari ibn Asim narrated to us: Ismail ibn Ulayyah narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Atiq, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade urinating in stagnant water and then performing ablution from it. No one narrated this hadith as raised from Ibn Ulayyah except al-Sari ibn Asim and Yaqub al-Dawraqi."
"9254","al-Numan ibn Ahmad narrated to us: al-Sari ibn Asim narrated to us: Ismail ibn Ulayyah narrated to us: Umarah ibn Abi Hafsah narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Al-Kawthar is a river in Paradise; its banks are gold, and it flows over pearls and rubies. No one narrated this hadith as connected from Umarah ibn Abi Hafsah except Ibn Ulayyah; al-Sari ibn Asim is alone in transmitting it."
"9255","al-Numan ibn Ahmad narrated to us: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Mahan narrated to us: My father narrated to me: Talhah ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Yazid, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from his father, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he was taken by night to heaven, the call to prayer was revealed to him, so he descended with it, and Jibril taught it to him. No one narrated this hadith from al-Zuhri except Yunus, and none from Yunus except Talhah ibn Zayd; Muhammad ibn Mahan al-Wasiti is alone in transmitting it."
"9256","al-Numan ibn Ahmad narrated to us: Abdullah ibn Hamzah al-Zubayri narrated to us: Abdullah ibn Nafi narrated to us, from Uthman ibn al-Dahhak, from his father, from Ubaydullah ibn Miqsam, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, who said: The sunnah of recitation in prayer is to recite in the first two with the Mother of the Quran and a surah, and in the last two with the Mother of the Quran. This hadith is not narrated from Jabir except with this chain; Ubaydullah ibn Miqsam is alone in transmitting it."
"9257","al-Numan ibn Ahmad narrated to us: Abdullah ibn Hamzah al-Zubayri narrated to us: Sadaqah ibn Bashir, freedman of the family of Umar ibn al-Khattab, narrated to us, from Qudamah ibn Ibrahim, that Abdullah ibn Umar narrated to him that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: A servant among the servants of Allah said: O Lord, to You is praise as befits the majesty of Your Face and the greatness of Your authority. It confounded the two angels, so they ascended to the lowest heaven and said: O Lord, Your servant has said a saying and we do not know how to write it. This hadith is not narrated from Abdullah ibn Umar except with this chain; Sadaqah ibn Bashir is alone in transmitting it."
"9258","al-Numan ibn Ahmad narrated to us: Ahmad ibn Rushd ibn Khuthaym al-Hilali narrated to us: My uncle Said ibn Khuthaym narrated to me, from Hanzalah ibn Abi Sulayman, from Tawus, from Abdullah ibn Abbas: Umm al-Fadl bint al-Harith al-Hilaliyyah narrated to me, saying: I passed by the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was sitting at al-Hijr, and he said: O Umm al-Fadl. I said: At your service, O Messenger of Allah. He said: You are pregnant with a boy. I said: O Messenger of Allah, how, when Quraysh have sworn not to approach women? He said: It is what I tell you; when you deliver him, bring him to me. She said: When I delivered him I brought him to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he called the adhan in his right ear and the iqamah in his left ear, and fed him with his saliva, and named him Abdullah, then said: Go with the father of the caliphs. She said: I came to al-Abbas and informed him, and he was a well-dressed, handsome man of steady stature, so he dressed and came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw him he stood to him and kissed between his eyes, then seated him at his right, then said: This is my uncle; whoever wishes, let him boast of his uncle. Al-Abbas said: Something of a saying, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Why should I not say this, O uncle, when you are my uncle and the counterpart of my father and the remainder of my forefathers, and my heir, and the best of my family whom I leave behind? I said: O Messenger of Allah, Umm al-Fadl said such and such? He said: It is yours, O Abbas, after one hundred and thirty-two, then from you al-Saffah, and al-Mansur, and al-Mahdi, then it is among their children until the last of them will be the one who prays with the Messiah Isa son of Maryam. No one narrated this hadith from Tawus except Hanzalah, and none from Hanzalah except Said ibn Khuthaym; Ahmad ibn Rashad is alone in transmitting it."
"9259","al-Numan ibn Ahmad narrated to us: Ahmad ibn Sinan narrated to us: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us: Sharik informed us, from Asim ibn Abi al-Najud, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The hand of the giver is the upper one; the best charity is what leaves sufficiency; and begin with those you support. Your wife says: Spend upon me or divorce me; your child says: O father, to whom do you entrust us? And your servant says: Feed me and employ me. No one narrated this hadith from Sharik except Yazid ibn Harun, and none raised this hadith from Asim except Sharik and Hammad ibn Salamah."
"9260","al-Numan narrated to us: Ahmad ibn Sinan narrated to us: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Kulthum ibn Jabr and Abu Hafs, from Abu al-Ghadiyah, who said: I saw Ammar ibn Yasir mentioning Uthman ibn Affan, and I said: If I get power over this one. When the Day of Siffin came and he was in arms, he would charge until he entered among the people, then come out. I looked and his knee had become uncovered of armor and the shin, so I aimed the spear at him and stabbed his knee, then killed him. Amr ibn al-As said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: His killer and his despoiler are in the Fire. No one narrated this hadith from Hammad ibn Salamah except Yazid ibn Harun."
"9261","al-Numan ibn Ahmad narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Ubadah al-Wasiti narrated to us: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us: Abd al-Malik ibn Husayn narrated to us, from Yusuf ibn Maymun, from al-Agharr Abu Muslim, from Abu Said and Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah Almighty says: Pride is My cloak; whoever contends with Me for My garment, I shall put him in the Fire. No one narrated this hadith from Yusuf ibn Maymun except Abd al-Malik ibn Husayn; Yazid ibn Harun is alone in transmitting it."
"9262","Chapter of Waw, those named Wathilah: Wathilah ibn al-Hasan al-Irqi narrated to us: Kathir ibn Ubayd al-Himsi narrated to us: Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid narrated to us, from Bahr al-Saqqa, from Muhammad ibn Ziyad, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What secures the one who raises his head before the imam that Allah will not make his head the head of a donkey. No one narrated this hadith from Bahr al-Saqqa except Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid."
"9263","Wathilah ibn al-Hasan narrated to us: Kathir narrated to us: Baqiyyah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn al-Walid al-Zubaydi, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent a detachment in which I was, and our shares reached twelve camels per man, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) then gave us extra a camel a camel. No one narrated this hadith from al-Zubaydi except Baqiyyah."
"9264","Wathilah narrated to us: Kathir narrated to us: Baqiyyah narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn Adham narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ajlan, from Farwah ibn Mujahid, from Sahl ibn Muadh ibn Anas, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Whoever suppresses anger while able to carry it out, Allah will give him choice of the wide-eyed maidens on the Day of Resurrection; and whoever leaves a garment of beauty while able to afford it, Allah will clothe him with the cloak of faith on the Day of Resurrection; and whoever marries a slave, Allah will place upon his head the crown of kingship on the Day of Resurrection. No one narrated this hadith from Ibrahim ibn Adham except Baqiyyah."
"9265","Wathilah ibn al-Hasan al-Irqi narrated to us: Kathir narrated to us: Ayyub ibn Suwayd narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ubaydullah al-Arzami, from Qatadah, who said: I said to Anas ibn Malik: Show us how the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was? He stood and prayed, and he would raise his hands with every takbir. When he finished he said: Such was the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). No one narrated this hadith from Qatadah, from Anas, except al-Arzami."
"9266","Those named Walid: al-Walid ibn Hammad al-Ramli narrated to us: al-Husayn ibn Abi al-Sari al-Asqalani narrated to us: al-Hasan ibn Muhammad ibn Ayan narrated to us: Fulayh ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed over al-Najashi and said takbir over him four takbirs. No one narrated this hadith from Nafi except Fulayh; al-Hasan ibn Muhammad ibn Ayan is alone in transmitting it."
"9267","al-Walid narrated to us: al-Husayn ibn Abi al-Sari narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Dhakwan, from al-Hasan, from Utayy, from Ubayy ibn Kab, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Adam was washed by the angels with water and lote, and they shrouded him, and made a niche grave for him, and buried him, and said: This is your sunnah, O children of Adam, for your dead. No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn Dhakwan except Muhammad ibn Ishaq."
"9268","al-Walid ibn Hammad al-Ramli narrated to us: Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Dimashqi narrated to us: Sadan ibn Yahya narrated to us, from Sadaqah ibn Abi Imran, from Iyad ibn Laqit, from Abu Rimthah, who said: I went with my father to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he had thick hair with traces of henna dye, and upon him were two green garments. No one narrated this hadith from Sadaqah ibn Abi Imran except Sadan ibn Yahya and Abbad ibn Suhayb. And Yazid ibn Ibrahim al-Tustari narrated it from Sadaqah, from Babi ibn Munqidh, from Abu Rimthah."
"9269","al-Walid ibn Hammad narrated to us: Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us: Sadan ibn Yahya narrated to us: Abu al-Rijal al-Basri narrated to us, from al-Nadr ibn Anas, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed with them the midday prayer and raised his voice and recited: By the sun and its brightness, and: By the night when it covers. Ubayy ibn Kab said to him: O Messenger of Allah, were you commanded something in this prayer? He said: No, but I intended to set the time of your prayer for you. No one narrated this hadith from al-Nadr ibn Anas except Abu al-Rijal, and none narrated it from Abu al-Rijal except Sadan ibn Yahya and Salm ibn Qutaybah."
"9270","al-Walid ibn Hammad narrated to us: Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Shuayb narrated to us, from al-Mughirah ibn Ziyad al-Mawsili, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) permitted the stick, the whip, the rope, and the like, which the pilgrim in ihram picks up and keeps. No one narrated this hadith from al-Mughirah ibn Ziyad except Muhammad ibn Shuayb."
"9271","al-Walid narrated to us: Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us: Sadan ibn Yahya narrated to us, from Abd al-Hamid ibn Jafar, from Salih ibn Abi Arib, from Kathir ibn Murrah, from Muadh ibn Jabal, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not gaze continuously at lepers. This hadith is not narrated from Muadh except with this chain; Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman is alone in transmitting it."
"9272","al-Walid narrated to us: Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us: Khalid ibn Abi Khalid al-Azraq narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla narrated to us, from al-Shabi, from Ibn Umar, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The best worship is understanding, and the best religion is piety. No one narrated this hadith from al-Shabi except Ibn Abi Layla, and none from Ibn Abi Layla except Khalid; Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman is alone in transmitting it."
"9273","al-Walid ibn Hammad al-Ramli narrated to us: Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us: al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Namir al-Yahsabi, from al-Zuhri: Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah informed me, from Abdullah ibn Thalabah al-Ansari, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid ibn Jariyah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed Fajr one day early in darkness, then prayed it another day later in brightness, then said: What is between them is the time. No one narrated this hadith from al-Zuhri except Abd al-Rahman ibn Namir; al-Walid is alone in transmitting it."
"9274","al-Walid ibn Hammad narrated to us: Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us: Abd al-Rahman ibn Bashir narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Abu Bakr ibn Muhammad, from Umar ibn Abi Salamah, from Umm Salamah, who said: Mamar ibn Abdullah al-Adawi shaved the head of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the Day of Sacrifice. This hadith is not narrated from Umm Salamah except with this chain; Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman is alone in transmitting it."
"9275","al-Walid ibn Hammad narrated to us: Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us: Sadan ibn Yahya narrated to us: Nafi, freedman of Yusuf al-Sulami, narrated to us, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The key of prayer is purification, its prohibition is the takbir, and its permissibility is the taslim. No one narrated this hadith from Ata except Nafi, and none from Nafi except Sadan ibn Yahya; Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman is alone in transmitting it, and it is not narrated from Ibn Abbas except with this chain."
"9276","al-Walid ibn Hammad narrated to us: Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us: Abd al-Rahman ibn Sawwar narrated to us: Amr ibn Maymun ibn Mihran narrated to us: My father Maymun ibn Mihran narrated to me, from his father Mihran, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Whoever does not recite the Mother of the Book in his prayer, it is defective. This hadith is not narrated from Mihran except with this chain; Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman is alone in transmitting it."
"9277","al-Walid narrated to us: Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us: Khalid ibn Yazid ibn Abi Malik narrated to us, from his father, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Abu Said al-Khudri, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The most wretched of the wretched is one upon whom gather the poverty of this world and the punishment of the Hereafter. This hadith is not narrated from Abu Said except with this chain; Khalid ibn Yazid ibn Abi Malik is alone in transmitting it."
"9278","al-Walid ibn Hammad al-Ramli narrated to us: Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us: Matar ibn al-Ala narrated to us: Abd al-Malik ibn Yasar al-Thaqafi narrated to us: Abu Umayyah al-Shabani narrated to us, and he had reached the Jahiliyyah: Muadh ibn Jabal narrated to me, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Thirty are prophethood and kingship, and thirty are kingship and tyranny, and beyond that there is no good in it. This hadith is not narrated from Abu Umayyah al-Shabani, from Muadh, except with this chain; Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman is alone in transmitting it."
"9279","al-Walid narrated to us: Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Muqri narrated to us: Artah ibn al-Mundhir narrated to us, from Abu al-Bakarat, from Abu Musa al-Ashari, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The great battles are at the hands of the fifth of the family of Heraclius. This hadith is not narrated from Abu Musa except with this chain; Artah ibn al-Mundhir is alone in transmitting it."
"9280","al-Walid ibn al-Abbas al-Addas al-Misri narrated to us: Abdullah ibn Salih narrated to us: Harmalah ibn Imran al-Tujibi narrated to me, from Uqbah ibn Muslim, from Uqbah ibn Amir al-Juhani, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: When you see Allah giving the servant what he loves while he persists in His disobedience, that is only istidraj for him from Him. Then he cited this verse: So when they forgot what they were reminded of, We opened upon them the doors of everything, until when they rejoiced in what they were given, We seized them suddenly, and they were in despair. Then cut off were the people who wronged, and praise be to Allah, Lord of the worlds. This hadith is not narrated from Uqbah ibn Amir except with this chain; Harmalah ibn Imran is alone in transmitting it."
"9281","Narrated al-Walid ibn al-Abbas al-Addas: narrated Abdullah ibn Salih: narrated Abd al-Rahman ibn Zayd ibn Aslam, from his father, from al-Sunabihi, who said: When death approached Ubadah, and I was at his head weeping, he said: What makes you weep? I said: Why should I not weep, given your benefit to me and my benefiting from you? He said: By Allah, I have not concealed from you a single word I heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except one, and I am now narrating it to you. I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever says: There is no god but Allah, alone with no partner, his heart obeying thereby and his tongue humbled thereby, Allah forbids him to the Fire. This hadith was not narrated from Zayd ibn Aslam except by his son Abd al-Rahman; Abu Salih is alone in transmitting it."
"9282","Narrated al-Walid ibn al-Abbas: narrated Abdullah ibn Salih: narrated Mufaddal ibn Faddalah, from Yunus ibn Yazid, from Sad ibn Ibrahim, from his brother al-Miswar ibn Ibrahim, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The thief is not fined when the prescribed punishment is carried out upon him. This hadith is not narrated from Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf except with this chain; Mufaddal ibn Faddalah is alone in transmitting it, and its chain is not connected, because al-Miswar did not hear from his grandfather."
"9283","Narrated al-Walid ibn al-Abbas: narrated Yahya ibn Bukayr: narrated Bakr ibn Mudar, from Jafar ibn Rabiah, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah, that prayer was first obligated as two rakahs; then the prayer of the resident was increased, while the prayer of the traveler was left as two rakahs. This hadith was not narrated from Jafar ibn Rabiah except by Bakr ibn Mudar."
"9284","Narrated al-Walid ibn al-Abbas: narrated Yahya ibn Bukayr: narrated al-Mughirah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from al-Dahhak, from Nafi, from Salim ibn Abdullah, that he heard Abdullah ibn Umar say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by Ibn Sayyad while he was playing with boys; he recognized him, so he called him forward and said: Do you testify that I am the Messenger of Allah? Ibn al-Sayyad said: I testify that you are the Prophet of the unlettered; so do you testify that I am the Messenger of Allah? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I believe in Allah and His messengers. This hadith was not narrated from Nafi, from Salim, except by al-Dahhak; al-Mughirah ibn Abd al-Rahman is alone in transmitting it."
"9285","Narrated al-Walid ibn al-Abbas al-Addas: narrated Abu Salih al-Huddani: narrated Ismail ibn Ayyash, from Damdam ibn Zurah, from Shurayh ibn Ubayd, from Abu Zuhayr al-Anmari, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not kill locusts, for they are the greatest army of Allah. This hadith is not narrated from Abu Zuhayr except with this chain; Ismail ibn Ayyash is alone in transmitting it."
"9286","Narrated al-Walid ibn Aban al-Asbahani: narrated Muhammad ibn Ammar al-Razi: narrated Abd al-Samad ibn Abd al-Aziz al-Muqri: narrated Amr ibn Abi Qays, from Mansur, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The records of the people of the earth are copied into the records of the people of heaven every Monday and Thursday, and every Muslim who does not associate anything with Allah is forgiven, except a man between whom and his brother there is enmity. This hadith was not narrated from Mansur except by Amr ibn Abi Qays, nor from Amr except by Abd al-Samad ibn Abd al-Aziz; Muhammad ibn Ammar is alone in transmitting it."
"9287","Narrated al-Walid ibn Aban: narrated Muhammad ibn Ammar al-Razi: narrated Abd al-Samad ibn Abd al-Aziz: narrated Amr ibn Abi Qays, from Mansur, from Abu Jafar, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: Among what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would recite in the Friday prayer was Surah al-Jumuah, by which he would encourage the believers, and in the second rakah Surah al-Munafiqun, by which he would frighten the hypocrites. This hadith was not narrated from Mansur except by Amr ibn Abi Qays."
"9288","Narrated al-Walid ibn Aban: narrated Muhammad ibn Ammar: narrated Abd al-Samad ibn Abd al-Aziz: narrated Amr ibn Abi Qays, from Bashir ibn Asim, from Abu al-Yaqzan, from Zadham, from Abdullah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Three will not be frightened by the terror, nor will the reckoning touch them, upon a dune of musk until Allah finishes the reckoning of the servants: a man who recited the Quran seeking the Face of Allah, then led a people in prayer while they were pleased with him; a caller who calls to the five prayers seeking the Face of Allah; and a slave who did well in what is between him and his Lord and in what is between him and his masters. This hadith was not narrated from Bashir ibn Asim except by Amr ibn Abi Qays; al-Thawri narrated it from Abu al-Yaqzan, from Zadham, from Ibn Umar."
"9289","Narrated al-Walid: narrated Muhammad ibn Ammar: narrated Abu al-Walid al-Jarudi, from Ibn Abi Dhib, from al-Zuhri, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever deliberately lies about me, let him take his seat in the Fire. This hadith was not narrated from Ibn Abi Dhib except by al-Jarudi; Muhammad ibn Ammar is alone in transmitting it."
"9290","Narrated al-Walid ibn Aban: narrated Abu Muin al-Razi: narrated Abd al-Rahman ibn Abd al-Malik ibn Shaybah al-Hizami: narrated Abu Qatadah ibn Yaqub ibn Abdullah ibn Thalabah ibn Suayr al-Udhri, from the nephew of al-Zuhri, from al-Zuhri, from Anas ibn Malik, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: If the believer were in a hole, Allah would appoint for him therein someone who would harm him. This hadith was not narrated from al-Zuhri except by his nephew, nor from his nephew except by Abu Qatadah; Abd al-Rahman ibn Abd al-Malik ibn Shaybah is alone in transmitting it."
"9291","Narrated al-Walid ibn Aban: reported Muhammad ibn Ammar al-Razi: narrated Muammal ibn Ismail: reported Hammad ibn Zayd, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Abdullah ibn al-Harith, who said: I was with Aishah, and with her was Kab al-Habr; he mentioned Israfil, so Aishah said: O Kab, inform me about Israfil. Kab said: You have the knowledge. She said: Yes, but inform me. He said: He has four wings: two wings in the air, one wing with which he has wrapped himself, and one wing upon his shoulder; the Throne is upon his shoulder and the Pen is upon his ear; when the revelation descends, the Pen writes, then the angels study, and the angel of the Trumpet is kneeling upon one knee with the other set up, having taken up the Trumpet, his back bent, his gaze fixed upon Israfil; and he has been commanded that when he sees Israfil fold his wing, he is to blow into the Trumpet. Aishah said: This is how I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say. This hadith was not narrated from Hammad ibn Zayd except by Muammal."
"9292","Chapter of Ha: Mention of those whose name is Hashim. Narrated Hashim ibn Marthad al-Tabarani: narrated Abu Salih al-Farra: narrated Abu Ishaq al-Fazari, from Abu Ishaq al-Shaybani: narrated Muharib ibn Dithar, who said: I heard Abdullah ibn Yazid say upon the pulpit: Narrated al-Bara ibn Azib - and as far as I knew he was not a liar - that they used to pray with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); when he bowed they bowed, and when he said: Allah hears whoever praises Him, they remained standing until they saw him place his face upon the ground, then they followed him. This hadith was not narrated from Abu Ishaq al-Shaybani except by Abu Ishaq al-Fazari."
"9293","Narrated Hashim ibn Marthad: narrated Yahya ibn Main: narrated Ismail ibn Aban al-Warraq: narrated Misar, from Qatadah, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I entered Paradise and there I was with a palace; I said: Whose is this? It was said: It belongs to Umar ibn al-Khattab. This hadith was not narrated from Misar except by Ismail ibn Aban; Yahya ibn Main is alone in transmitting it."
"9294","Narrated Hashim ibn Marthad: narrated Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Dimashqi: narrated Abd al-Rahman ibn Bashir al-Shaybani, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited Surah al-Najm, and when he reached the prostration he prostrated. This hadith was not narrated from al-Zuhri except by Muhammad ibn Ishaq, nor from Muhammad ibn Ishaq except by Abd al-Rahman ibn Bashir; Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman is alone in transmitting it."
"9295","Narrated Hashim ibn Marthad: narrated Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman: narrated Abdullah ibn Kathir al-Qari: narrated Zuhayr ibn Muhammad, from Abdullah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Husayn, from his father, from al-Mughirah ibn Shubah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Mughirah, when you wish to marry a woman, do not marry her until you look at her. This hadith was not narrated from Ibn Abi Husayn except by Zuhayr ibn Muhammad, nor from Zuhayr except by Abdullah ibn Kathir; Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman is alone in transmitting it."
"9296","Narrated Hashim ibn Marthad: narrated al-Muafa ibn Sulayman: narrated Musa ibn Ayan, from Abu Abd al-Rahim Khalid ibn Abi Yazid, from Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah, from Mujalid ibn Said, from Amir al-Shabi, from Masruq, from Zaynab - the wife of Abdullah - who said: I gathered some wealth of mine from charity, then I came to Aishah and said: O Mother of the Believers, I have gathered some wealth of mine from charity; ask the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for me: in which of these shall I place it? In a slave I free? Or in the path of Allah? Or upon a needy husband and orphaned nephews? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon Aishah, and Aishah mentioned it to him, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Give it in charity to a needy husband and orphaned nephews; charity upon a relative is doubled twice in reward. This hadith was not narrated from Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah except by Khalid ibn Abi Yazid."
"9297","Narrated Hashim ibn Marthad: narrated Muhammad ibn Ismail ibn Ayyash al-Himsi: narrated his father: narrated Abu al-Ashath Jafar ibn al-Harith al-Nakhai al-Kufi, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Asim ibn Umar ibn Qatadah, from Mahmud ibn Labid, from Rafi ibn Khadij, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Pray Fajr at the brightness of dawn, for it is greater in reward. This hadith was not narrated from Jafar ibn al-Harith except by Ismail ibn Ayyash; Muhammad ibn Ismail is alone in transmitting it."
"9298","Narrated Hashim: narrated al-Muafa ibn Sulayman: narrated Musa ibn Ayan, from al-Mualla ibn Irfan, from Abu Wail, from Abdullah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would breathe into the vessel with three breaths, naming Allah at each breath and giving thanks at the end of them. This hadith was not narrated from Abu Wail except by al-Mualla ibn Irfan; Musa ibn Ayan is alone in transmitting it."
"9299","Narrated Hashim ibn Marthad: narrated al-Muafa ibn Sulayman: narrated Isa ibn Yunus, from Uthman ibn Abd al-Rahman, who said: I heard al-Zuhri narrate from Urwah, from Aishah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no marriage except with a guardian and two just witnesses. This hadith was not narrated from Uthman ibn Abd al-Rahman except by Isa ibn Yunus."
"9300","Narrated Hashim ibn Marthad: narrated al-Muafa ibn Sulayman: narrated Musa ibn Ayan, from al-Khalil ibn Murrah, from Ismail ibn Ibrahim, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever digs a grave, Allah builds for him a house in Paradise; whoever washes a dead person emerges from sins as on the day his mother gave birth to him; whoever shrouds a dead person, Allah clothes him with garments of the garments of Paradise; whoever consoles a grieving person, Allah clothes him with piety and sends blessings upon his soul among the souls; whoever consoles an afflicted person, Allah clothes him with two garments of the garments of Paradise which the world cannot match; whoever follows a funeral until its burial is completed, three qirats are written for him, each qirat greater than Mount Uhud; and whoever sponsors an orphan or a widow, Allah shades him in His shade and admits him into His Paradise. This hadith was not narrated from al-Khalil ibn Murrah except by Musa ibn Ayan, and it is not narrated from Jabir except with this chain. The Ismail ibn Ibrahim who narrated this hadith was not identified by lineage to us."
"9301","Narrated Hashim ibn Marthad: narrated al-Muafa ibn Sulayman: narrated Muhammad ibn Salamah, from Abu Abd al-Rahim, from Abd al-Wahhab ibn Bukht, from Abdullah ibn Nafi Abu Yaqub, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: I seek refuge in You from the trial of the False Messiah, and from the punishment of the grave, and from the trial of the grave, and from the evil of the trial of wealth, and from the evil of the trial of poverty; and I seek refuge in You from the evil of the trial of the False Messiah. O Allah, wash away my sins with the water of snow and hail, and purify my heart from sins as You purified the white garment from filth; and I seek refuge in You from laziness, old age, sin, and debt. This hadith was not narrated from Abdullah ibn Nafi except by Abd al-Wahhab ibn Bukht, nor from Abd al-Wahhab except by Khalid ibn Abi Yazid; Muhammad ibn Salamah is alone in transmitting it."
"9302","Narrated Hashim ibn Marthad: narrated al-Muafa ibn Sulayman: narrated Muhammad ibn Salamah, from Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Ulathah, from Hisham ibn Hassan, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever swears a binding oath in which he is lying, let him take for his face a seat in the Fire. This hadith was not narrated from Hisham except by Ibn Ulathah."
"9303","Narrated Hashim ibn Marthad: narrated al-Muafa ibn Sulayman: narrated Musa ibn Ayan, from Ishaq ibn Rashid, from al-Zuhri, from Salim ibn Abdullah, who said: Abdullah ibn Umar was approached and it was said to him: Ibn Abbas permits temporary marriage. Ibn Umar said: Glory be to Allah, I do not think Ibn Abbas would do this. They said: Indeed, he permits it. He said: Was Ibn Abbas anything but a small boy when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - then Ibn Umar said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade it to us, and we were not fornicators."
"9304","Narrated Hashim ibn Marthad: narrated al-Muafa ibn Sulayman: narrated Musa ibn Ayan, from Ishaq ibn Rashid, from al-Zuhri, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The polytheists do not dye their beards, so change the white hair."
"9305","Narrated Hashim ibn Marthad: narrated al-Muafa ibn Sulayman: narrated Musa ibn Ayan, from Ishaq ibn Rashid, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Bakr ibn Ubaydullah, from Abdullah ibn Umar, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever among you eats, let him eat with his right hand, and let him drink with his right hand; for Satan eats with his left and drinks with his left."
"9306","Narrated Hashim ibn Marthad: narrated al-Muafa ibn Sulayman: narrated Musa ibn Ayan, from Ishaq ibn Rashid, from al-Zuhri, from Ibn Kab ibn Malik, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he would not return from a journey except in the forenoon, beginning with the mosque, praying two rakahs in it, then coming to his family after that."
"9307","Narrated Hashim ibn Marthad: narrated al-Muafa ibn Sulayman: narrated Musa ibn Ayan, from Ishaq ibn Rashid, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to encourage the people to stand in prayer in Ramadan without commanding them with a decisive command regarding it; then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed away with the matter upon that, then the matter remained upon that during the caliphate of Abu Bakr and the early part of the caliphate of Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both. These hadiths were not narrated from Ishaq ibn Rashid except by Musa ibn Ayan."
"9308","Narrated Hashim ibn Marthad: narrated al-Muafa ibn Sulayman: narrated Musa ibn Ayan, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from Ibrahim al-Nakhai, from al-Aswad ibn Yazid, from Aishah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray witr with nine rakahs. This hadith was not narrated from Ata ibn al-Saib except by Musa ibn Ayan."
"9309","Narrated Hashim ibn Marthad: narrated al-Muafa ibn Sulayman: narrated Muhammad ibn Salamah, from Abu Abd al-Rahim Khalid ibn Abi Yazid, from Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah, from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid, from Qays ibn Abi Hazim, from Jarir ibn Abdullah al-Bajali, who said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) one night with the moon rising on the night of full moon, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed you will see your Lord in Paradise as you see this moon; you will not be harmed in seeing Him. So if you are able not to be overcome regarding a prayer before the rising of the sun and before its setting - then he recited: And glorify with the praise of your Lord before the rising of the sun and before the setting. This hadith was not narrated from Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah except by Abu Abd al-Rahim. And none of those who narrated this hadith from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid said: you will see your Lord, except Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah and Abu Shihab al-Hannat."
"9310","Narrated Hashim ibn Marthad: narrated Muhammad ibn Ismail al-Jafari: narrated Abdullah ibn Salamah al-Rabai, from Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Sasah, from his father, from Abu Said al-Khudri, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever spends generously upon his family on the day of Ashura, Allah will grant him abundance throughout his whole year. This hadith is not narrated from Abu Said al-Khudri except with this chain; Muhammad ibn Ismail al-Jafari is alone in transmitting it."
"9311","Narrated Hashim ibn Marthad: narrated Adam ibn Abi Iyas: narrated Israil, from Qarazah, from Ikrimah, from Aishah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out while the Abyssinians were playing, and I was looking from a small window of mine. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) drew near to me, so I placed my hands upon his shoulders and kept looking. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: They are the daughters of Arfidah. I kept looking while they played and danced until I was the one who stopped. This hadith was not narrated from Qarazah except by Israil; Adam is alone in transmitting it."
"9312","Narrated Hashim ibn Marthad: narrated Adam: narrated Hibban ibn Ali: narrated Sad ibn Tarif al-Iskaf, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wished to relieve himself, he went far. One day he went out for his need, then performed ablution and put on one of his leather socks, then a green bird came, took the other sock, rose with it, then cast it down, and from it came out a black gliding snake. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This is a honor by which Allah has honored me. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from the evil of what walks upon its belly, from the evil of what walks upon two legs, and from the evil of what walks upon four. This hadith was not narrated from Ikrimah except by Sad ibn Tarif; Hibban ibn Ali is alone in transmitting it, and it is not narrated from Ibn Abbas except with this chain."
"9313","Narrated Hashim ibn Marthad: narrated Adam: narrated Ibn Abi Fudayk al-Madani, from Abd al-Malik ibn Zayd, from Musab ibn Musab, from Ibn Shihab, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf, from his father, who said: Talhah ibn Ubaydullah spoke to Amir ibn Fuhayrah about something, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Gently, O Talhah, for he attended Badr as you attended it, and the best of you are the best of you to their freedmen. This hadith was not narrated from al-Zuhri except by Musab ibn Musab, nor from Musab except by Abd al-Malik ibn Zayd, nor from Abd al-Malik except by Ibn Abi Fudayk; Adam is alone in transmitting it, and it is not narrated from Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf except with this chain."
"9314","Narrated Hashim ibn Marthad: narrated Adam: narrated Shayban, from Jabir, from Muhammad ibn Ali, from Abdullah ibn Jafar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was cupped upon his horn after he was poisoned. This hadith is not narrated from Abdullah ibn Jafar except with this chain; Shayban is alone in transmitting it."
"9315","Narrated Hashim ibn Marthad: narrated Adam: narrated al-Masudi, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) lay upon a mat, and the mat left marks upon his skin. When he awoke, I began wiping from him, saying: O Messenger of Allah, had you permitted me before sleeping upon this mat, I would have spread something upon it to protect you from it? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What have I to do with the world, and what has the world to do with me? I and the world are but like a rider who rested in the shade of a tree, then departed and left it. This hadith was not narrated from Amr ibn Murrah except by al-Masudi."
"9316","Narrated Hashim ibn Marthad: narrated Adam: narrated Warqa, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, who said: When this verse was revealed: The Messenger believes in what was sent down to him from his Lord, and the believers - the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited it. When he reached: Your forgiveness, our Lord, and to You is the return - Allah said: I have forgiven you. When he said: Our Lord, do not take us to task if we forget or err, our Lord - Allah said: I will not take you to task. When he said: And lay not upon us a burden as You laid upon those before us - Allah, mighty and majestic, said: I will not lay upon you. When he said: And burden us not with what we have no strength for - Allah, blessed and exalted, said: I will not burden you. When he said: And pardon us - He said: I have pardoned you. When he said: And forgive us - He said: I have forgiven you. When he said: And have mercy upon us - He said: I have had mercy upon you. When he said: And grant us victory over the disbelieving people - He said: I have granted you victory over the disbelieving people. This hadith was not narrated from Ata except by Warqa; Adam is alone in transmitting it."
"9317","Narrated Hashim ibn Marthad: narrated Adam: narrated Shayban, from Mansur ibn al-Mutamir, from Ribi ibn Hirash, from Kharashah ibn al-Hurr, from Abu Dharr, who said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) awoke, he would say: Praise be to Allah who gave us life after He caused us to die, and to Him is the resurrection. And when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood, he would say: In Your name, O Allah, we die and we live. This hadith was not narrated from Mansur except by Shayban."
"9318","Narrated Hashim ibn Marthad: narrated Adam: narrated Warqa, from Mughirah, from al-Shabi, from al-Numan ibn Bashir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The likeness of the one who upholds the limits of Allah, the one who compromises regarding the limits of Allah, and the one who violates the limits of Allah is like three groups who were in a ship, dividing its places. The place of drawing water and pouring it fell to one of them, and they were harmed by him. He took an axe and struck his place. One of the remaining two said to the other: Do you not see this one who wishes to pierce our ship and drown us? The other said to him: Leave him, for he only pierces his own place. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If they prevent him, he is saved and they are saved; and if they leave him, he drowns and they drown. This hadith was not narrated from Warqa except by Adam."
"9319","Narrated Hashim ibn Marthad: narrated Adam: narrated Mubarak ibn Fadalah, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah, who said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) bathed from major impurity, he washed his hands three times before dipping them into the vessel, then poured with his right over his left, washing his private part until he cleansed it with his left, then performed his ablution for prayer. She said: And he had hair, and he would take water and enter it into the roots of his hair, combing it through, until when he had ensured the skin was reached, he poured over his head three times, then poured over his body. This hadith was not narrated from Mubarak ibn Fadalah except by Adam and Abu al-Nadr Hashim ibn al-Qasim."
"9320","Narrated Hashim ibn Marthad: narrated Adam: narrated Shayban, from Jabir, from al-Shabi, from Murrah al-Hamdani, from Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: None who is evil in authority over those under him enters Paradise; cursed is whoever harms a Muslim or deceives him. This hadith was not narrated from al-Shabi except by Jabir al-Jufi, and none narrated it from Jabir except Shayban and Abu Hamzah al-Sukkari."
"9321","Narrated Hashim ibn Marthad: narrated Adam: narrated Mubarak ibn Fadalah, from Thabit, from Anas, who said: Fatimah said: O the distress of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: O my daughter, there has come upon your father a matter from which Allah will leave no one when meeting the Day of Resurrection. This hadith was not narrated from Thabit except by Mubarak ibn Fadalah."
"9322","Narrated Hashim ibn Marthad: narrated Adam: narrated Shayban: narrated Qatadah, from Azrah ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Khuzai, from Rashid ibn Khunays al-Himsi - he once said: Hunays - from Ubadah ibn al-Samit, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) visited me in illness and said: Do you know who the martyrs of my nation are on the Day of Resurrection? The people fell silent, so I said: O Messenger of Allah, the one killed in the path of Allah, patient and seeking reward, is a martyr. He said: If the martyrs of my nation were only these, then they would indeed be few. The one killed in the path of Allah is a martyr, the drowned is a martyr, the one who dies of abdominal illness is a martyr, the plague is martyrdom, and the woman who dies in childbirth - her child draws her with its umbilical cord to Paradise. This hadith was not narrated from Qatadah except by Shayban and Said ibn Bashir; from Shayban, Adam is alone in transmitting it."
"9323","Narrated Hashim ibn Marthad: narrated Adam: narrated Abu Ghassan Muhammad ibn Mutarrif, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ata ibn Yasar, from al-Sunabihi, from Ubadah ibn al-Samit, who said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Five prayers Allah has obligated upon His servants. Whoever perfects their ablution and prays them at their times, completing their bowing, prostration, and humility, has a covenant from Allah that He will forgive him; and whoever does not do so has no covenant from Allah - if He wills He punishes him, and if He wills He forgives him. This hadith was not narrated from Zayd ibn Aslam except by Abu Ghassan; Adam is alone in transmitting it."
"9324","Narrated Hashim ibn Marthad: narrated Adam: narrated Shayban, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from his mother, from Aishah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to perform ablution with a mudd. None narrated it from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from his mother, from Aishah, except Shayban."
"9325","Narrated Hashim ibn Marthad: narrated Adam: narrated Abu Jafar al-Razi, from Abdullah ibn Dinar, from Bushayr ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Kinship is a branch from the Most Merciful; it clung to the waist of the Most Merciful, saying: O Allah, join whoever joins me, and cut whoever cuts me. This hadith was not narrated from Abdullah ibn Dinar, from Bushayr ibn Yasar, except by Abu Jafar al-Razi. And Warqa narrated it from Abdullah ibn Dinar, from Said ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah."
"9326","Narrated Hashim ibn Marthad: narrated Adam: narrated Abu Yusuf the judge, from Sad ibn Tarif, from al-Asbagh ibn Nubatah, from Ali ibn Abi Talib, who said: We alighted at a stopping place and the fleas harmed us, so we reviled them. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not revile them, for what an excellent creature; it awakened you for the remembrance of Allah. This hadith is not narrated from Ali except with this chain; Adam is alone in transmitting it."
"9327","Narrated Hashim ibn Marthad: narrated Adam: narrated Israil, from Jabir, from Abdullah ibn Nujayy, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, regarding the statement of Allah: Among them are those whose stories We have related to you, and among them are those whose stories We have not related to you. He said: Allah sent an Abyssinian servant as a prophet, and he is among those He did not narrate to Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). It is not narrated from Ali except with this chain; Adam is alone in transmitting it."
"9328","Narrated Hashim ibn Marthad: narrated Adam: narrated Mubarak ibn Fadalah: narrated Ziyad ibn Jubayr ibn Hayyah: informed me my father, that al-Numan ibn Muqarrin said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he raided and did not fight at the beginning of the day, would not hasten until the prayer times arrived, the winds blew, and fighting became pleasant. This hadith was not narrated from Ziyad ibn Jubayr ibn Hayyah except by Mubarak ibn Fadalah."
"9329","Narrated Hashim ibn Marthad: narrated Adam: narrated Shayban, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from al-Uryan ibn al-Haytham, from Qabisah ibn Jabir al-Asadi, who said: Abdullah ibn Masud said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) curse the women who pluck eyebrows, those who widen gaps between teeth, those who tattoo, and those who change the creation of Allah. This hadith was not narrated from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr except by Shayban."
"9330","Narrated Hashim ibn Marthad: narrated Zakariyya ibn Nafi al-Ursufi: narrated Muhammad ibn Muslim al-Taifi, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever, being in ihram, does not find a waist-wrapper but finds trousers, let him wear them; and whoever does not find sandals, let him wear the leather socks, cutting them below the ankles. This hadith was not narrated from Amr ibn Dinar, from Jabir, except by Muhammad ibn Muslim."
"9331","Narrated Hashim ibn Marthad: narrated Muhammad ibn Abd al-Aziz al-Ramli: narrated Abu Khalid al-Ahmar, from al-Amash, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from Aishah, and from Yahya ibn Said, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from Aishah, who said: It is as though I am looking at the glisten of perfume in the parting of the hair of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was chanting the talbiyah. This hadith was not narrated from Yahya ibn Said except by Abu Khalid al-Ahmar; Muhammad ibn Abd al-Aziz is alone in transmitting it."
"9332","Mention of those whose name is Hammam. Narrated Hammam ibn Yahya ibn Hammam ibn Maslamah ibn Uqbah ibn Hammam ibn Munabbih al-Sanani: narrated Ibrahim ibn Ahmad al-Yamami: narrated Yazid ibn Abi Hakim: narrated Yasin al-Zayyat, from Ashath, from al-Hasan, from Abu Hurayrah and Abu Said, who said: The first prayer obligated upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was Zuhr."
"9333","Narrated Hammam ibn Yahya: narrated Hariz ibn al-Musallam al-Sanani: narrated Abd al-Majid ibn Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Rawwad, from Yasin al-Zayyat, from al-Amash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: How will you be when your youth become corrupt and your women transgress? They said: O Messenger of Allah, will that indeed happen? He said: And worse than that will happen. How will you be when you see the right as wrong and the wrong as right? This hadith was not narrated from al-Amash except by Yasin, nor from Yasin except by Abd al-Majid; Hariz ibn al-Musallam is alone in transmitting it."
"9334","Narrated Hammam ibn Yahya: narrated Hariz ibn al-Musallam: narrated Abd al-Majid ibn Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Rawwad, from his father, from Layth ibn Abi Sulaym, from Amr ibn Shuayb, from his father, from his grandfather, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not pluck white hair, for it is light; whoever grows a white hair in Islam, ten good deeds are written for him thereby, a sin is removed from him thereby, and a rank is raised for him thereby."
"9335","Narrated Hammam ibn Yahya: narrated Hariz ibn al-Musallam: narrated Abd al-Majid, from his father, from Layth, from Abu Uthman, from al-Qasim, from Aishah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whatever a faraq intoxicates from, a sip of it is unlawful."
"9336","Narrated Hammam ibn Yahya: narrated Hariz ibn al-Musallam: narrated Abd al-Majid, from his father, from Abu Ishaq, from Asim ibn Damrah, who said: We asked Ali about the daytime prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: You cannot bear it. They said: We wish to know it. He said: He would wait until, when the sun from its east was like al-Asr time from its west, he would come to his family and nap if he wished. When the sun declined he stood and prayed four rakahs, and he would pray two rakahs after Zuhr and four rakahs before Asr. These hadiths were not narrated from Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Rawwad except by his son; Hariz ibn al-Musallam is alone in transmitting them."
"9337","Mention of those whose name is Harun. Narrated Harun ibn Mallul al-Misri: narrated Abdullah ibn Yazid - the brother of Abd al-Rahman al-Muqri - narrated Haywah ibn Shurayh, from Abu Sakhr, from Yazid ibn Abdullah ibn Qusayt, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no Muslim who sends salutations upon me except that Allah returns my soul to me so that I return them upon him. This hadith was not narrated from Ibn Qusayt except by Abu Sakhr."
"9338","Narrated Harun ibn Mallul: narrated Abdullah ibn Yazid al-Muqri: narrated Haywah ibn Shurayh, from Bashir ibn Abi Amr al-Khawlani, that al-Walid ibn Qays al-Tujibi narrated to him that he heard Abu Said al-Khudri say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: There will be a generation after sixty years who neglect prayer and follow desires, so they will meet error; then there will be a generation who recite the Quran and it does not pass their collarbones; and the Quran is recited by three: a believer, a hypocrite, and a wicked one. This hadith is not narrated from Abu Said except with this chain; Haywah is alone in transmitting it."
"9339","Narrated Harun ibn Mallul: narrated Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Muqri, from Abdullah ibn Ayyash, who said: I heard my father Ayyash ibn Abbas say: I heard Isa ibn Hilal al-Sadafi and Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Hubuli say: We heard Abdullah ibn Amr say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: There will be at the end of my nation women clothed yet naked, upon their heads like the humps of camels. Curse them, for they are cursed. If there were behind you a nation among the nations, they would serve them as the women of the nations before you serve you. This hadith is not narrated from Abdullah ibn Amr except with this chain; Abdullah ibn Ayyash is alone in transmitting it."
"9340","Narrated Harun ibn Mallul: narrated Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Muqri, from Said ibn Abi Ayyub, from Abu al-Aswad, from Abbad ibn Tamim al-Mazini, from his father, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) perform ablution and wipe with water over his feet. This hadith is not narrated from Tamim al-Mazini except with this chain; Said ibn Abi Ayyub is alone in transmitting it."
"9341","Narrated Harun ibn Mallul: narrated Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Muqri, from Said ibn Abi Ayyub, from Abdullah ibn al-Walid, from Abdullah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Hujayrah, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called Salman and said: The Prophet of Allah wishes to grant you words from the Most Merciful; desire Him through them and supplicate with them by night and day: O Allah, I ask You for soundness in faith, faith in good character, salvation followed by success, mercy from You and well-being, and forgiveness from You and pleasure. This hadith is not narrated from Abu Hurayrah except with this chain; Said ibn Abi Ayyub is alone in transmitting it."
"9342","Narrated Harun ibn Mallul: narrated Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Muqri: narrated Harmalah ibn Imran, from Abu Yunus Sulaym ibn Jubayr, who said: I heard Abu Hurayrah say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited this verse: Allah commands you to render trusts to those entitled to them, up to His statement: Allah is Hearing, Seeing - placing his thumb upon his ear and the next one upon his eye, and saying to us: This is how I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recite, placing his two fingers. This hadith was not narrated from Abu Yunus except by Harmalah ibn Imran."
"9343","Narrated Harun ibn Mallul: narrated Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Muqri: narrated Haywah ibn Shurayh, from Kab ibn Alqamah, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Jubayr, from Abdullah ibn Amr, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you hear the caller to prayer, say as he says, then send blessings upon me; for whoever sends one blessing upon me, Allah sends ten upon him. And ask Allah for me al-Wasilah, for it is a station in Paradise befitting only a servant among the servants of Allah, and I hope that I am he. Whoever asks al-Wasilah for me, intercession becomes due for him. This hadith was not narrated from Abd al-Rahman ibn Jubayr except by Kab ibn Alqamah; Haywah is alone in transmitting it."
"9344","Narrated Harun ibn Mallul: narrated Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Muqri: narrated Said ibn Abi Ayyub: narrated Yazid ibn Abi Habib, who said: I heard Abu al-Khayr say: I came to Uqbah ibn Amir and said: Shall I not amuse you with Abu Tamim al-Jayshani? He prays two rakahs before the Maghrib prayer. Uqbah said: We used to do it in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). This hadith was not narrated from Yazid ibn Abi Habib except by Said ibn Abi Ayyub, and it is not narrated from Uqbah ibn Amir except with this chain."
"9345","Narrated Harun ibn Mallul: narrated Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Muqri: narrated Said ibn Abi Ayyub: narrated Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Suwayd ibn Qays, from Muawiyah ibn Hudayj, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If there is healing in anything, it is in the incision of a cupper, or a sip of honey, or cauterization with fire touching pain; and I do not like to be cauterized. This hadith is not narrated from Muawiyah ibn Hudayj except with this chain; Yazid ibn Abi Habib is alone in transmitting it."
"9346","Narrated Harun ibn Mallul: narrated Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Muqri: narrated Said ibn Abi Ayyub, from Uqayl and Yunus and Ibn Saman, from Ibn Shihab, from Abu Salamah, from Aishah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever of my nation bears a debt then strives to repay it but dies before repaying it, I am his guardian. This hadith was not narrated from al-Zuhri except by Uqayl and Yunus and Ibn Saman, and none narrated it from them except Said ibn Abi Ayyub; al-Muqri is alone in transmitting it."
"9347","Narrated Harun ibn Mallul: narrated Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Muqri: narrated Said ibn Abi Ayyub: narrated Abdullah ibn al-Walid, from Abu al-Khayr, from Uqbah ibn Amir, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Three things - if there is healing in anything, it is in the incision of a cupper, or a sip of honey, or cauterization with fire touching pain; and I dislike cauterization and do not like it. This hadith was not narrated from Abdullah ibn al-Walid except by Said ibn Abi Ayyub."
"9348","Narrated Harun ibn Mallul: narrated Abu Abd al-Rahman: narrated Said ibn Abi Ayyub, from Yahya ibn Abi Sulaym, from Said al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever shoots at us by night is not of us. This hadith was not narrated from al-Maqburi except by Yahya ibn Abi Sulaym; Said ibn Abi Ayyub is alone in transmitting it."
"9349","Narrated Harun ibn Mallul: narrated Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Muqri: narrated Said: narrated Abdullah ibn al-Walid, from Abdullah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Hujayrah, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The right of the believer upon the believer is six traits: he greets him when he meets him, he says Yarhamuk Allah when he sneezes, he answers him when he invites him, he visits him when he is ill, he attends him when he dies, and he advises him sincerely when he is absent. This hadith was not narrated from Ibn Hujayrah except by his son, nor from his son except by Abdullah ibn al-Walid; Said ibn Abi Ayyub is alone in transmitting it."
"9350","Narrated Harun ibn Mallul: narrated Abu Abd al-Rahman: narrated Said, from Ayyash ibn Abbas, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Hubuli, from Abdullah ibn Amr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Being killed in the path of Allah expiates everything, except debt. This hadith was not narrated from Ayyash ibn Abbas except by Said ibn Abi Ayyub."
"9351","Narrated Harun ibn Mallul: narrated Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Muqri: narrated al-Hasan ibn Umarah, from Adi ibn Thabit, from Salim ibn Abi al-Jad, from Thawban, who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, what suffices me of the world? He said: What fills your hunger and covers your nakedness; and if you have a house that shades you, that is enough; and if you have a mount, then excellent. This hadith was not narrated from Adi ibn Thabit except by al-Hasan ibn Umarah."
"9352","Narrated Harun ibn Mallul: narrated Hafs ibn Umar al-Adani: narrated al-Hakam ibn Aban, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: A spear was planted before the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at Arafat, and he prayed toward it, while donkeys passed beyond the spear."
"9353","Narrated Harun ibn Mallul: narrated Hafs ibn Umar al-Adani: narrated al-Hakam ibn Aban, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The sun eclipsed in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he stood for prayer; he stood long, then bowed long, then stood long, then bowed long, then prostrated, then repeated the like of it. Ikrimah said: Ibn Abbas said: I was beside the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and did not hear the recitation."
"9354","Narrated Harun ibn Mallul: narrated Hafs ibn Umar al-Adani: narrated al-Hakam ibn Aban, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mention the Hour that is on Friday, upon the pulpit, minimizing it."
"9355","Narrated Harun ibn Kamil al-Misri: narrated Abdullah ibn Salih: narrated al-Layth: narrated Yunus, from Ibn Shihab: narrated Ata ibn Abi Rabah, that Jabir ibn Abdullah claimed that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever eats garlic or onion, let him keep away from us, or: let him keep away from our mosque, or: let him sit in his house. This hadith was not narrated from al-Zuhri except by Yunus, and al-Zuhri did not narrate as musnad from Ata ibn Abi Rabah any hadith other than this."
"9356","Narrated Harun ibn Kamil: narrated Said ibn Ufayr: narrated Ibn Lahiah, from Musa ibn Wardan, from Abu al-Haytham, from Abu Basrah al-Ghifari, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Abu Basrah, the disbeliever eats in seven intestines, while the believer eats in one intestine. This hadith is not narrated from Abu Basrah except with this chain; Ibn Lahiah is alone in transmitting it."
"9357","Narrated Harun ibn Kamil: narrated Said ibn Ufayr: narrated Yahya ibn Fulayh, from Thawr ibn Yazid, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the drinkers were beaten in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with hands, sandals, and sticks. This hadith was not narrated from Thawr except by Yahya; Said ibn Ufayr is alone in transmitting it."
"9358","Narrated Harun ibn Kamil: narrated Said ibn Abi Maryam: narrated Ibrahim ibn Ismail ibn Abi Habibah, from Dawud ibn al-Husayn, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever has intercourse with a mahram relative, kill him."
"9359","Narrated Harun ibn Kamil: narrated Yahya ibn Bukayr: narrated Khunays ibn Amir al-Maafiri, from Abu Qabil, from Junadah ibn Abi Umayyah, from Muadh ibn Jabal, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: There is no prophet but that he warned his nation of the Dajjal, and I warn you of the affair of the Dajjal. He is one-eyed, and your Lord is not one-eyed. Written between his eyes is: disbeliever; the literate and the illiterate will read it. With him are a paradise and a fire; his fire is paradise and his paradise is fire. This hadith was not narrated from Khunays ibn Amir except by Yahya ibn Bukayr."
"9360","Narrated Harun ibn Kamil: narrated Said ibn Abi Maryam: narrated Ibrahim ibn Suwayd al-Madani: narrated Abu Hazrah Yaqub ibn Mujahid: informed me Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, from Aishah, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Allah says: Whoever humiliates a wali of Mine has made lawful war with Me. No servant of Mine draws near to Me with the like of performing My obligations; and My servant continues to draw near to Me with supererogatory acts until I love him. When I love him, I am his eyes with which he sees, his ears with which he hears, his hand with which he strikes, and his feet with which he walks. If he calls upon Me I answer him, and if he asks Me I give him. And I have not hesitated about anything I do as I hesitate about his death - for he dislikes death and I dislike displeasing him. This hadith was not narrated from Abu Hazrah except by Ibrahim ibn Suwayd, and none narrated it from Urwah except Abu Hazrah and Abd al-Wahid ibn Maymun."
"9361","Narrated Harun ibn Kamil: narrated Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani: narrated Ibn Lahiah, from Muhammad ibn Ajlan, from al-Qaqa ibn Hakim, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Reputation is only here - and he pointed with his hand toward the heaven. None of those who narrated this hadith from Ibn Ajlan mentioned al-Qaqa except Ibn Lahiah."
"9362","Narrated Harun ibn Kamil: narrated Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani: narrated Ibn Lahiah, from Wahib ibn Abdullah, from Abdullah ibn Amr, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let none of you approach with his garment upon his nose, for that is the muzzling of Satan. This hadith is not narrated from Abdullah ibn Amr except with this chain; Ibn Lahiah is alone in transmitting it."
"9363","Narrated Harun ibn Kamil: narrated Yahya ibn Bukayr: narrated Ibn Lahiah: narrated Ammar ibn Sad, from Abu Salamah, from Aishah, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praying one night, so I stood behind him praying with his prayer. When he sat he shortened his standing and prayed two light rakahs, then gave salutations, then stood and prayed two rakahs, then gave salutations and made me hear the salutation. Then he turned to me and said: Take upon yourselves of deeds what you can bear - saying it three times. This hadith was not narrated from Ammar ibn Sad except by Ibn Lahiah."
"9364","Narrated Harun ibn Kamil: narrated Yahya ibn Bukayr: narrated Ibn Lahiah: narrated Abu Jamil al-Ansari, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when morning came, would say: In the morning I call You to witness, O my Lord, and I call to witness Your angels, Your prophets, Your messengers, and all Your creation, upon my testimony against myself that I testify that You are Allah, there is no god but You, alone with no partner, and that Muhammad is Your servant and Messenger; and I believe in You and rely upon You - saying it three times. This hadith was not narrated from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad except by Abu Jamil al-Ansari; Ibn Lahiah is alone in transmitting it."
"9365","Narrated Harun ibn Kamil: narrated Yahya ibn Bukayr: narrated Ibn Lahiah, from Musa ibn Ayyub al-Ghafiqi, from Iyas ibn Amir, from Ali ibn Abi Talib, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade temporary marriage, and it was only for one who did not find means; then when marriage, divorce, waiting period, and inheritance were revealed, he forbade it. This hadith was not narrated from Musa ibn Ayyub except by Ibn Lahiah."
"9366","Narrated Harun ibn Kamil: narrated Abd al-Ghaffar ibn Dawud Abu Salih al-Harrani: narrated Ibn Lahiah, from Bukayr ibn Abdullah ibn al-Ashajj, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from Aishah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon me while in the house there was a curtain hung with images in it; I recognized anger in the face of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so I cut it and made it into two cushions. This hadith was not narrated from Bukayr ibn Abdullah except by Ibn Lahiah."
"9367","Narrated Harun ibn Kamil: narrated Abu Salih al-Harrani: narrated Ibn Lahiah, from al-Walid ibn Abi al-Walid, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no good in the congregation of women, except in a congregational mosque or the funeral of one slain. This hadith was not narrated from al-Walid ibn Abi al-Walid except by Ibn Lahiah."
"9368","Narrated Harun ibn Kamil: narrated Said ibn Abi Maryam: narrated Ibn Lahiah: narrated Yazid ibn Abi Habib: informed me Amir ibn Yahya al-Maafiri, from Hanash al-Sanani, who said: When the fitnah of Ibn al-Zubayr occurred, the Haruriyyah sent to him: Come to us. He came to them, stood and addressed them, praising Allah. They said: We know your inclination is with us; come so that we make you caliph. He said: By Allah, my insight regarding you before today was firm, and I have increased in insight regarding you. How can I be among you when I heard Abu Said al-Khudri say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: There will emerge from this nation people who pass through the religion as the arrow passes through the target? This hadith is not narrated from Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr, from Abu Said al-Khudri, except with this chain; Ibn Lahiah is alone in transmitting it."
"9369","Narrated Harun ibn Sulayman Abu Dharr al-Misri: narrated Sufyan ibn Bishr al-Kufi: narrated Abd al-Rahim ibn Sulayman, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Ishaq ibn Kab ibn Ujrah, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not revile Ali, for he is deeply immersed in the essence of Allah. This hadith was not narrated from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad except by Abd al-Rahim ibn Sulayman."
"9370","Narrated Harun ibn Sulayman: narrated Zuhayr ibn Abbad al-Ruasi: narrated Isa ibn Yunus, from Faid Abu al-Warqa, who said: I heard Abdullah ibn Abi Awfa say: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed ablution three times three times, and wiped his head once. This hadith is not narrated from Abdullah ibn Abi Awfa except with this chain."
"9371","Narrated Harun ibn Sulayman: narrated Zuhayr ibn Abbad: narrated Sallam al-Tawil, from Zayd al-Ammi, from Abu Uthman al-Ansari, from Ibn Umar, from Abdullah ibn Salam, that he said: O Messenger of Allah, before you we were People of the Book, and we are commanded to wash after excrement and urine. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah is pleased with you, has praised you, and loves you, so do not abandon it. This hadith is not narrated from Ibn Umar, from Abdullah ibn Salam, except with this chain; Zuhayr ibn Abbad is alone in transmitting it."
"9372","Narrated Harun ibn Sulayman Abu Dharr al-Misri: narrated Yusuf ibn Adi: narrated Amr ibn Thabit, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Abd al-Rahman the nephew of Zayd ibn Arqam, who said: We entered upon Umm Salamah, and she said: From where are you? We said: From the people of Kufa. She said: Are you those who revile the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? I said: I do not know anyone who reviled the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). She said: Rather, you curse Ali and whoever loves him, while the Messenger of Allah loved him. This hadith was not narrated from Abd al-Rahman the nephew of Zayd ibn Arqam except by Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, nor from Yazid except by Amr ibn Thabit; Yusuf ibn Adi is alone in transmitting it."
"9373","Narrated Harun ibn Sulayman: narrated Yahya ibn Sulayman al-Jufi: narrated Muhammad ibn Sulayman al-Asbahani, from Abu Sinan Dirar ibn Murrah, from Abdullah ibn Abi al-Hudhayl, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: When the people of Hell are driven to it, it meets them and scorches them with a scorch that leaves no flesh upon a bone except that it casts it upon the ankles. This hadith was not narrated from Abdullah ibn Abi al-Hudhayl except by Abu Sinan; Muhammad ibn Sulayman al-Asbahani is alone in transmitting it."
"9374","Narrated Harun ibn Sulayman Abu Dharr: narrated Sufyan ibn Bishr al-Kufi: narrated Hatim ibn Ismail, from Kathir ibn Zayd, from al-Muttalib ibn Abdullah ibn Hantab, who said: Abu Ayyub al-Ansari said to Marwan ibn al-Hakam: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not weep over the religion when you entrust it to its people, but weep over it when you entrust it to other than its people. This hadith is not narrated from Abu Ayyub except with this chain; Sufyan ibn Bishr is alone in transmitting it."
"9375","Narrated Harun ibn Sulayman: narrated Yahya ibn Sulayman al-Jufi: narrated al-Muharibi, that he heard al-Amash mention, from Tarif ibn Maymun, from Ibn Abbas - raising it - who said: There is no man in charge of ten except that he will be brought on the Day of Resurrection with his hand chained to his neck, until judgment is passed between him and them. This hadith was not narrated from al-Amash except by al-Muharibi; Yahya ibn Sulayman al-Jufi is alone in transmitting it."
"9376","Narrated Harun ibn Sulayman Abu Dharr: narrated Zuhayr ibn Abbad: narrated Hafs ibn Maysarah, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you prays, let him wear his two garments, for Allah is most deserving of being adorned for. Whoever does not have two garments, let him wrap himself in his lower garment when he prays, and let none of you wrap himself in his prayer as the Jews wrap themselves. This hadith was not narrated from Musa ibn Uqbah except by Hafs ibn Maysarah; Zuhayr ibn Abbad is alone in transmitting it."
"9377","Narrated Harun ibn Sulayman Abu Dharr: narrated Yusuf ibn Adi: narrated Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad al-Muharibi, from Sufyan al-Thawri, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When Allah wills evil for a servant, He makes building with bricks and clay attractive to him until he builds. This hadith was not narrated from Sufyan except by al-Muharibi, nor from al-Muharibi except by Yusuf ibn Adi; Abu Dharr is alone in transmitting it."
"9378","Narrated Harun ibn Musa al-Akhash al-Muqri al-Dimashqi: narrated Sallam ibn Sulayman al-Madaini: narrated Abu Amr ibn al-Ala, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, who said: I recited to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Allah is He who created you from weakness. He said: From weakness. Then He made after weakness strength. He said: Then He made after weakness strength. Then He made after strength weakness. He said: After strength weakness."
"9379","Narrated Harun ibn Musa: narrated Sallam ibn Sulayman: narrated Abu Amr ibn al-Ala, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited: Then you will drink boiling water upon it."
"9380","Narrated Harun ibn Muhammad ibn al-Munakhal al-Harithi al-Wasiti: narrated al-Abbas ibn Abi Talib: narrated Hafs ibn Umar al-Adani: narrated Musa ibn Sad al-Basri, from al-Hasan, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: A bird was gifted to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: O Allah, bring me the most beloved of Your creation to You, to eat with me from this bird. Then Ali ibn Abi Talib came. This hadith was not narrated from al-Hasan except by Musa ibn Sad; Hafs ibn Umar is alone in transmitting it."
"9381","Narrated Harun ibn Muhammad ibn al-Munakhal: narrated al-Fadl ibn Abi Talib: narrated al-Harith ibn Mansur: narrated Umar ibn Qays, from al-Zuhri, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A woman is not married except with the permission of a guardian. This hadith was not narrated from al-Zuhri except by Umar ibn Qays; al-Harith ibn Mansur is alone in transmitting it."
"9382","Narrated Harun ibn Muhammad ibn al-Munakhal: narrated Ahmad ibn Mani: narrated Ashath ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Zubayd, from Abidah: narrated Sufyan, from Hudhayfah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) urinated upon the rubbish heap of a people, then performed ablution and wiped over his leather socks. This hadith was not narrated from Abidah except by Ashath ibn Abd al-Rahman; Ahmad ibn Mani is alone in transmitting it."
"9383","Narrated Harun ibn Muhammad ibn al-Munakhal: narrated Muhammad ibn Sulayman Luwayn: narrated Rawh ibn al-Musayyib, from Yazid al-Raqashi, from Ghunaym ibn Qays, from Abu Musa al-Ashari, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When Allah, majestic is His mention, created Adam, He took two handfuls from his loins; every good one fell into His right hand and every evil one into His other hand. He said: These are the companions of the right, and I do not care; and these are the companions of Paradise, and these are the companions of the Fire. Then He returned them into the loins of Adam, and they are being propagated upon that now. This hadith is not narrated from Abu Musa except with this chain; Rawh ibn al-Musayyib is alone in transmitting it."
"9384","Mention of those whose name is al-Haytham. Narrated al-Haytham ibn Khalid al-Massisi: narrated Abd al-Kabir ibn al-Muafa ibn Imran: narrated Sharik, from al-Abbas ibn Dhurayh, from al-Shabi, from Anas ibn Malik - raising it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - who said: Among the approach of the Hour is that the crescent is seen large, so it is said: it is of two nights; and that mosques are taken as thoroughfares; and that sudden death appears. This hadith was not narrated from al-Abbas ibn Dhurayh except by Sharik; Abd al-Kabir ibn al-Muafa is alone in transmitting it."
"9385","Narrated Haytham ibn Khalid: narrated Muhammad ibn Isa ibn al-Tabba: narrated Hushaym, from Mansur ibn Zadham, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about one who shaved before slaughtering. He said: No harm. This hadith was not narrated from Mansur except by Hushaym."
"9386","Narrated Haytham ibn Khalid: narrated Abd al-Kabir ibn al-Muafa: narrated Hushaym, from Abidah, from Ibrahim, from Abdullah ibn Ubaydullah al-Hashimi, from Abdullah ibn Ukaym, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not benefit from carrion by hide or sinew. This hadith was not narrated from Abidah except by Hushaym; Abd al-Kabir ibn al-Muafa is alone in transmitting it."
"9387","Narrated Haytham ibn Khalid: narrated Abd al-Kabir ibn al-Muafa ibn Imran: narrated my father: narrated Ibn Lahiah, from Abu al-Aswad, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, from Aishah, who said: Bilal stood to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Such-and-such woman has died and found rest. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) became angry and said: Only one who is forgiven has found rest. This hadith was not narrated from Abu al-Aswad except by Ibn Lahiah, nor from Ibn Lahiah except by al-Muafa; Abd al-Kabir is alone in transmitting it."
"9388","Narrated Haytham ibn Khalid: narrated Abd al-Kabir ibn al-Muafa: narrated Abu al-Ahwas, from Said ibn Masruq, from Ikrimah, from Uqbah ibn Amir, that he said: O Messenger of Allah, my sister vowed to walk to the House. He said: Command her to ride, for Allah gains nothing from the hardship of this woman. This hadith was not narrated from Said ibn Masruq except by Abu al-Ahwas; Abd al-Kabir is alone in transmitting it."
"9389","Narrated Haytham ibn Khalid: narrated Abd al-Kabir: narrated Salih ibn Musa al-Talhi: narrated Muawiyah ibn Ishaq, from Aishah bint Talhah, from Aishah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He has not honored his father who fixes his glance upon him in anger. This hadith was not narrated from Aishah bint Talhah except by Muawiyah ibn Ishaq; Salih ibn Musa is alone in transmitting it."
"9390","Narrated Haytham: narrated Abd al-Kabir ibn al-Muafa: narrated Salih ibn Musa, from Muawiyah ibn Ishaq, from Aishah bint Talhah, from Aishah, who said: Talhah came forward, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is pleased to look at a man who has fulfilled his vow, let him look at Talhah. This hadith was not narrated from Muawiyah ibn Ishaq except by Salih ibn Musa."
"9391","Narrated Haytham ibn Khalid: narrated Abd al-Kabir ibn al-Muafa ibn Imran: narrated Salih ibn Musa, from Muawiyah ibn Ishaq, from Aishah bint Talhah, from Aishah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The quickest good in reward is maintaining kinship, and the quickest evil in punishment is severing kinship. This hadith was not narrated from Muawiyah ibn Ishaq except by Salih ibn Musa."
"9392","Narrated Haytham ibn Khalid: narrated Abd al-Kabir: narrated Salih ibn Musa, from Muawiyah ibn Ishaq, from Aishah bint Talhah, from Aishah, who said: While the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was among his companions facing the House, my father came forward, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever wishes to look at one freed from the Fire, let him look at Abu Bakr. This hadith was not narrated from Muawiyah ibn Ishaq except by Salih ibn Musa."
"9393","Narrated Haytham ibn Khalid: narrated Dawud ibn Mansur: narrated Ayyub ibn Khut, from Qatadah, from Anas, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The world is the prison of the believer and the paradise of the disbeliever. This hadith was not narrated from Qatadah except by Ayyub ibn Khut; Dawud ibn Mansur is alone in transmitting it."
"9394","Narrated Haytham ibn Khalid: narrated Dawud ibn Mansur: narrated Jarir ibn Hazim, from Yazid ibn Ruman, from Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr, from Aishah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Were it not that your people are recent in the time of ignorance, I would have ordered the House to be demolished, until I included in it what was excluded from it - al-Hijr. This hadith was not narrated from Yazid ibn Ruman except by Jarir ibn Hazim and Abu Uways."
"9395","Narrated Haytham: narrated Dawud ibn Mansur: narrated Jarir ibn Hazim, from Thabit, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the prayer is established, do not stand until you see me. This hadith was not narrated from Thabit except by Jarir ibn Hazim."
"9396","Narrated Haytham ibn Khalid: narrated Dawud ibn Mansur: narrated Jarir ibn Hazim, who said: I heard Abu al-Zubayr narrate from Jabir, who said: There would be prepared for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) drink in a stone vessel, and he would drink from it that day of his. This hadith was not narrated from Jarir ibn Hazim except by Dawud ibn Mansur."
"9397","Narrated Haytham ibn Khalid: narrated Yahya ibn Muhammad ibn Sabiq: narrated Ziyad ibn al-Hasan ibn al-Furat al-Qazzaz, from his father, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Ahwas, from his father, that he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and began asking the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw his poor appearance, he said: Do you have wealth? He said: Yes, Allah has given me of every wealth - of camels, sheep, and horses. He said: When Allah gives you wealth, let it be seen upon you. This hadith was not narrated from al-Hasan ibn Furat except by his son Ziyad ibn al-Hasan; Yahya ibn Muhammad ibn Sabiq is alone in transmitting it."
"9398","Narrated Haytham ibn Khalid al-Massisi: narrated Muhammad ibn Isa al-Tabba: narrated Faraj ibn Fadalah, from Yahya ibn Said, from Amrah, from Umm Salamah, that she had a sheep she milked; the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) missed it and said: What happened to your sheep? They said: It died. He said: Why did you not benefit from its hide? We said: It is carrion. He said: Its tanning makes it lawful, just as vinegar makes wine lawful. This hadith was not narrated from Yahya ibn Said except by Faraj ibn Fadalah, and it is not narrated from Umm Salamah except with this chain."
"9399","Narrated al-Haytham ibn Khalid: narrated Dawud ibn Mansur: narrated Jarir ibn Hazim, from Abu Ishaq, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from Hujayyah ibn Adi, from Ali, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded us to examine the eye and the ear of the sacrificial animal. This hadith was not narrated from Abu Ishaq except by Jarir ibn Hazim."
"9400","Narrated Haytham ibn Khalaf al-Duri: narrated Muhammad ibn Ammar al-Mawsili: narrated al-Muafa ibn Imran al-Mawsili, from al-Hasan ibn Hayy, from Ibrahim ibn Muhajir, from Abu Bakr ibn Hafs, from Sad ibn Abi Waqqas, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: What an excellent death it is for a man to die defending his right. This hadith was not narrated from al-Hasan ibn Hayy except by al-Muafa ibn Imran."
"9401","Narrated Haytham ibn Khalaf: narrated al-Husayn ibn Yazid al-Tahhan: narrated Abd al-Salam ibn Harb, from Yazid Abu Khalid al-Dalani, from al-Hakam ibn Utaybah, from Abu Mamar, from Abdullah ibn Muawiyah, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) give salutations to his right and to his left, until the whiteness of his cheeks was seen. This hadith was not narrated from al-Hakam except by Abu Khalid al-Dalani; Abd al-Salam ibn Harb is alone in transmitting it."
"9402","Narrated al-Haytham ibn Khalaf al-Duri: narrated Muhammad ibn Marzuq: narrated al-Haytham ibn Salih, from Sallam Abu al-Mundhir, from Matar al-Warraq, from Ata, from Jabir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The cupper and the one cupped have broken the fast. This hadith was not narrated from Matar except by Sallam Abu al-Mundhir; al-Haytham ibn Salih is alone in transmitting it."
"9403","Narrated Haytham ibn Khalaf: narrated Ibrahim ibn Said al-Jawhari: narrated Abu al-Jawwab, from Sulayman ibn Qarm, from al-Amash, from Shaqiq, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: It is not lawful for a Muslim to boycott his brother for more than three days. This hadith was not narrated from al-Amash except by Sulayman ibn Qarm, nor from Sulayman except by Abu al-Jawwab; Ibrahim ibn Said is alone in transmitting it."
"9404","Narrated al-Haytham ibn Khalaf: narrated Yazid ibn Amr ibn al-Bara al-Ghanawi: narrated Hafs ibn Umar al-Adani: narrated Musa ibn Sad, from Maymun al-Qannad, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: Muhammad, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), looked at his Lord, blessed and exalted. Ikrimah said: I said to Ibn Abbas: Did Muhammad look at his Lord? He said: Yes; He made speech for Musa, close friendship for Ibrahim, and the vision for Muhammad, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. This hadith was not narrated from Maymun al-Qannad except by Musa ibn Sad; Hafs ibn Umar al-Adani is alone in transmitting it."
"9405","Narrated al-Haytham ibn Khalaf: narrated Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Madaini: narrated Shababab ibn Sawwar: narrated Warqa, from Mansur, from Qatadah, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married Safiyyah, making her freedom her dowry, and he served the people hays upon a leather mat as a wedding feast. This hadith was not narrated from Mansur ibn al-Mutamir except by Warqa, nor from Warqa except by Shababah; Zakariyya ibn Yahya is alone in transmitting it."
"9406","Narrated al-Haytham ibn Khalaf: narrated Muammal ibn Hisham: narrated Yahya ibn Abbad, from al-Sari ibn Yahya, from Abd al-Karim, from Mujahid, who said: Ibn Umar said: I have been given of it something none was given except the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - meaning: intercourse. This hadith was not narrated from al-Sari ibn Yahya except by Yahya ibn Abbad; Muammal ibn Hisham is alone in transmitting it."
"9407","Narrated al-Haytham ibn Khalaf: narrated Muhammad ibn Salih ibn al-Nattah: narrated Asim ibn Hilal, from Ayyub, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was cupped and gave him his wage; and had it been unlawful he would not have given it to him. This hadith was not narrated from Ikrimah except by Asim ibn Hilal, and others narrated it from Ayyub, from Muhammad."
"9408","Narrated al-Haytham ibn Khalaf: narrated Ali ibn Siyabah al-Kufi: narrated Kathir ibn Hisham: narrated Sulayman al-Basri - he is al-Qaflani - from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu al-Tufayl, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: It used to be said: Indeed among what people attained of the speech of prophethood is: If you do not feel shame, do whatever you wish. This hadith is not narrated from Abu al-Tufayl except with this chain; Ali ibn Siyabah is alone in transmitting it."
"9409","Narrated al-Haytham ibn Khalaf: narrated Ismail ibn Musa al-Suddi: narrated Sharik, from Bayan, or another, from Anas, who said: The ring of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was of silver. This hadith was not narrated from Bayan except by Sharik; Ismail ibn Musa is alone in transmitting it."
"9410","Narrated al-Haytham ibn Khalaf: narrated Muhammad ibn al-Ala Abu Kurayb: narrated Muhammad ibn Fudayl, from Bayan, from Amir - and Qays mentioned - who said: Ibn Masud would narrate for a month without saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). When he mentioned the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he would say: Like this, or something like this, or close to this - and he would tremble. This hadith was not narrated from Bayan except by Muhammad ibn Fudayl; Abu Kurayb is alone in transmitting it. And the Qays from whom al-Shabi narrated this hadith is Qays ibn Qahd."
"9411","Narrated al-Haytham ibn Khalaf: narrated Muhammad ibn Hashish: narrated Mufaddal ibn Salih, from Muhammad ibn Juhadah, from al-Hasan, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A person is with whom he loves. This hadith was not narrated from Ibn Juhadah except by Mufaddal ibn Salih."
"9412","Narrated al-Haytham ibn Khalaf: narrated Abu Musa al-Ansari: narrated Ahmad ibn Bashir al-Hamdani, from Abu al-Bilad, from Muslim ibn Subayh, from Masruq, who said: I entered upon Aishah while with her was a blind man; she was cutting citron for him and feeding it to him with honey. I said: Who is this, O Mother of the Believers? She said: This is Ibn Umm Maktum. He came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while with him were Utbah and Shaybah, so he turned to them both, and there was revealed: He frowned and turned away, because the blind man came to him - she said: Ibn Umm Maktum. This hadith was not narrated from Abu al-Bilad, from Muslim ibn Subayh, except by Ahmad ibn Bashir; Abu Musa al-Ansari is alone in transmitting it."
"9413","Narrated al-Haytham ibn Khalaf al-Duri: narrated Ahmad ibn Ibrahim al-Mawsili: narrated Abu Ismail al-Muaddib, from Yaqub ibn Ata, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Take suhur, for in suhur there is blessing. This hadith was not narrated from Yaqub ibn Ata except by Abu Ismail; Ahmad ibn Ibrahim is alone in transmitting it."
"9414","Narrated al-Haytham ibn Khalaf al-Duri: narrated Ahmad ibn Yazid ibn Sulayman - the freedman of Banu Hashim - narrated Husayn ibn al-Hasan al-Ashqar: narrated Hushaym, from Abu Hashim al-Rummani, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The feet of the servant will not move on the Day of Resurrection until he is asked about four: about his life in what he spent it, about his body in what he wore it out, about his wealth in what he spent it and from where he earned it, and about our love, the People of the House. This hadith was not narrated from Abu Hashim except by Hushaym, nor from Hushaym except by Husayn ibn Hasan; Ahmad ibn Yazid is alone in transmitting it."
"9415","Narrated al-Haytham ibn Khalaf: narrated Harun ibn Ishaq: narrated Abu Khalid al-Ahmar, from Yahya ibn Said, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - similar to the hadith of Qabilah -: There is no charity upon the horse of the warrior and his slave. This hadith was not narrated from Yahya ibn Said except by Abu Khalid; Harun ibn Ishaq is alone in transmitting it."
"9416","Narrated al-Haytham ibn Khalaf: narrated Yaqub ibn Ibrahim Abu al-Asbat: narrated Abu Bilal al-Ashari, from Qays ibn al-Rabi, from Abu Husayn, from al-Qasim ibn Hassan, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Harmalah, from Abdullah ibn Masud, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade ten traits: changing white hair and plucking it, saffron dye, letting the lower garment hang, tying amulets, striking dice, seeking refuge - meaning incantations - wearing a gold ring, displaying adornment to other than its proper place, withdrawing water from its place, and corrupting the child without making him unlawful to marry. This hadith was not narrated from Abu Husayn except by Qays, nor from Qays except by Abu Bilal; Abu al-Asbat is alone in transmitting it."
"9417","Narrated al-Haytham ibn Khalaf: narrated Abbad ibn Yaqub: narrated Abdullah ibn Abd al-Quddus, from Fitr, from Abu Harun, from Abu Said, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed over al-Najashi. This hadith was not narrated from Fitr except by Abdullah ibn Abd al-Quddus; Abbad ibn Yaqub is alone in transmitting it."
"9418","Narrated al-Haytham ibn Khalaf: narrated Muhammad ibn Aban al-Balkhi: narrated Abu Usamah, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Mamar, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah, that she was gifted to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - and with her were her dolls. Abu Usamah narrated from Abd al-Razzaq only this hadith and one other hadith."
"9419","Narrated al-Haytham ibn Khalaf: narrated Abu Bakr ibn Abi al-Nadr: narrated Abu al-Nadr: narrated Abu Malik al-Nakhai Abd al-Malik ibn al-Husayn, from Abu al-Muhajjal, from the nephew of Anas ibn Malik, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: My station was between the shoulders of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); when he gave salutations he would say: O Allah, make the best of my life its end; O Allah, make the seals of my deeds Your pleasure; O Allah, make the best of my days the day I meet You. This hadith was not narrated from Abu al-Muhajjal except by Abd al-Malik ibn Husayn, nor from Abd al-Malik except by Abu al-Nadr; Abu Bakr ibn Abi al-Nadr is alone in transmitting it."
"9420","Narrated al-Haytham ibn Khalaf: narrated Ahmad ibn Ibrahim al-Dawraqi: narrated Abd al-Samad ibn Abd al-Warith: narrated Shubah, from Zaidah, from Abu Husayn, from Dhakwan, from Aishah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed in a garment part of which was upon me. This hadith was not narrated from Shubah except by Abd al-Samad; Ahmad al-Dawraqi is alone in transmitting it."
"9421","Narrated al-Haytham ibn Khalaf: narrated al-Fadl ibn Ishaq al-Duri: narrated Umar ibn Ayyub al-Mawsili, from Isa ibn al-Musayyib al-Bajali, from Amir al-Shabi, from al-Subayy ibn Mabad al-Taghlibi, that he entered ihram for Hajj and Umrah together. When he emerged from al-Qadisiyyah, two riders passed by him while he was chanting the talbiyah for Hajj and Umrah together. One of them said: Do you not hear? He said: Leave him, for he is more astray than his camel. I was seized by what was short and long, so I hurried until I met one who informed me about them. I said: Who are these two riders? He said: This is Salman ibn Rabiah al-Bahili and Zayd ibn Suhan. I came to Madinah and went to Umar, narrating to him and informing him of what they said. He said: They erred and you were right; you were guided to the practice of your Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Then he sent to them both and forbade them. This hadith was not narrated from al-Shabi except by Isa ibn al-Musayyib, nor from Isa except by Umar ibn Ayyub; al-Fadl ibn Ishaq is alone in transmitting it."
"9422","Narrated al-Haytham ibn Khalaf: narrated Ubaydullah ibn Umar al-Qawariri: narrated Abd al-Ala: narrated Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Khalid ibn Kathir al-Hamdani, from Asim ibn Abi al-Najud, from Zirr ibn Hubaysh, from Safwan ibn Assal al-Muradi, who said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asking him about wiping over the leather socks. I said: O Messenger of Allah, I came to ask you about knowledge. He said: The angels lower their wings for the seeker of knowledge out of their love for what he came seeking. And about which knowledge do you ask? I said: O Messenger of Allah, about wiping over the leather socks. He said: Yes, a day and a night for the resident, and three for the traveler, after relieving oneself of excrement and urine; then renew ablution. This hadith was not narrated from Khalid ibn Kathir except by Muhammad ibn Ishaq; Abd al-Ala is alone in transmitting it."
"9423","Narrated al-Haytham ibn Khalaf: narrated Hashim ibn al-Walid al-Harawi: narrated Kinanah ibn Jabalah, from Ibrahim ibn Tahman, from al-Hajjaj ibn Artah, from Abd al-Karim, from Abu Uthman, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded me to announce among the people of Madinah: In every prayer there is recitation, even if with the Opening of the Book. This hadith was not narrated from al-Hajjaj except by Ibrahim ibn Tahman."
"9424","Narrated al-Haytham ibn Khalaf: narrated Muhammad ibn Ammar al-Mawsili: narrated Umar ibn Ayyub, from Masad ibn Uqbah, from Ziyad ibn Sad, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Fast upon seeing it, and break fast upon seeing it. This hadith was not narrated from Ziyad ibn Sad except by Masad ibn Uqbah, nor from Masad except by Umar ibn Ayyub; Muhammad ibn Ammar is alone in transmitting it."
"9425","Narrated Haytham ibn Khalaf: narrated Abu Musa al-Ansari: narrated Abu Ghazziyah Muhammad ibn Musa: narrated Ibrahim ibn Sad, from Umar ibn Muhammad, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) facing the Kabah, sitting with his arms around his knees. This hadith was not narrated from Umar ibn Muhammad except by Ibrahim ibn Sad, nor from Ibrahim except by Abu Ghazziyah; Abu Musa al-Ansari is alone in transmitting it."
"9426","Haytham narrated to us, Abu Musa narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Jafar ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best speech is the Book of Allah, and the best guidance is the guidance of Muhammad, and the worst of matters are the newly invented ones, and every innovation is misguidance; and whoever leaves wealth, it is for his family, and whoever leaves debt or helpless dependents, then it is upon me. No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn Jafar ibn Muhammad except Abu Musa al-Ansari."
"9427","Haytham ibn Khalaf narrated to us, Ali ibn Siyabah narrated to us, Ali ibn Yunus al-Balkhi narrated to us, from Hisham ibn al-Ghaz, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Mounts are not saddled except to three mosques: the Sacred Mosque, and this mosque of mine, and al-Aqsa Mosque. No one narrated this hadith from Hisham ibn al-Ghaz except Ali ibn Yunus; Ali ibn Siyabah is alone in transmitting it."
"9428","Haytham ibn Khalaf narrated to us, Ali ibn Siyabah narrated to us, Amr the nephew of al-Hasan ibn Amr narrated to us, my uncle al-Hasan ibn Amr narrated to us, from al-Shabi, from Jarir, he said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw me that I kept nothing, I only spent it, he said to me: O Jarir, there is no harm upon you in holding your wealth for yourself, for this affair has a duration. No one narrated this hadith from al-Shabi except al-Hasan ibn Amr, nor from al-Hasan except his nephew Amr ibn Abd al-Ghaffar; Ali ibn Siyabah is alone in transmitting it."
"9429","Haytham ibn Khalaf narrated to us, Ali ibn Siyabah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Kathir al-Qurashi narrated to us, Abu Sinan Sad ibn Sinan al-Shaybani narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Silah ibn Zufar, from Hudhayfah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Look closely at the eye and the ear (of the sacrificial animal). No one narrated this hadith from Silah, from Hudhayfah, except Abu Sinan, nor from Abu Sinan except Muhammad ibn Kathir; Ali ibn Siyabah is alone in transmitting it. And the people narrated it from Abu Ishaq, from Surayj ibn al-Numan, from Ali. And Abu Waki narrated it from Abu Ishaq, from Hubayrah ibn Yarim, from Ali."
"9430","Haytham ibn Khalaf narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Shawkar narrated to us, Yusuf ibn Atiyyah al-Saffar narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Hassan, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not complete fasting a month after Ramadan except Rajab and Shaban. No one narrated it from Hisham except Yusuf ibn Atiyyah."
"9431","Haytham ibn Khalaf narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ammar al-Mawsili narrated to us, al-Qasim ibn Yazid al-Jarmi narrated to us, from Sadaqah ibn Abdullah al-Dimashqi, from Ibn Jurayj, from Muhammad ibn Ziyad al-Madani, from Furat the freedman of Aishah, he said: Aishah said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever has dust enter his belly will never enter the Fire. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Jurayj except Sadaqah, nor from Sadaqah except al-Qasim ibn Yazid; Muhammad ibn Ammar is alone in transmitting it."
"9432","Haytham narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Bakkar narrated to us, Abu Mashar narrated to us, from Shurahbil ibn Sad, he said: I caught a bird among Banu Harithah, so Rafi ibn Khadij took it and released it, and said: Do you not know that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) declared inviolable what is between the two lava tracts of Madinah. No one narrated this hadith from Shurahbil, from Rafi, except Abu Mashar; Muhammad ibn Bakkar is alone in transmitting it. And the people narrated it from Shurahbil, from Zayd ibn Thabit."
"9433","Haytham ibn Khalaf narrated to us, Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Madaini narrated to us, Shabbabah ibn Sawwar narrated to us, al-Mughirah ibn Muslim narrated to us, from Matar al-Warraq, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded us to bestow favor upon the children of adultery - meaning: in setting free (by freeing them). No one narrated this hadith from Matar except al-Mughirah, nor from al-Mughirah except Shabbabah; Zakariyya ibn Yahya is alone in transmitting it."
"9434","Haytham ibn Khalaf narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Hammad al-Warraq narrated to us, Abu Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, from Yusuf ibn Maymun, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) conquered Makkah he said: Allah and His Messenger have forbidden you drinking wine and its price, and have forbidden you eating carrion and its price, and have forbidden you pigs, eating them and their price. And he said: Trim the mustaches, leave the beards, and do not walk in the markets except wearing lower garments; whoever acts upon a practice other than ours is not of us."
"9435","Haytham ibn Khalaf narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Hammad al-Warraq narrated to us, Abu Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, from Yusuf ibn Maymun, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon Umar with some of his Companions with him, and said: Are you believers? They remained silent - three times - then Umar at the last of them said: Yes, we believe in what you have brought us, and we praise Allah in ease, and we are patient in affliction, and we believe in the Decree. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Believers, by the Lord of the Kabah. No one narrated these two hadiths from Ata except Yusuf ibn Maymun, nor from Yusuf except Abu Yahya al-Himmani; al-Hasan ibn Hammad al-Warraq is alone in transmitting them."
"9436","Haytham narrated to us, Ali ibn Siyabah narrated to us, Bishr ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Imran al-Wasiti narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from Abdullah ibn Abi Awfa, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Part of the justice of Allah on the Day of Resurrection will reach the point that He will retaliate for the hornless one against the one with horns. No one narrated this hadith from Ata ibn al-Saib except Abdullah ibn Imran, nor from Abdullah except Bishr ibn Muhammad; Ali ibn Siyabah is alone in transmitting it."
"9437","Haytham ibn Khalaf narrated to us, al-Husayn ibn Mahdi al-Ubulli narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn Nusayr narrated to us, Warqa ibn Umar narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed ablution once for each limb. No one narrated this hadith from Amr ibn Dinar except Warqa, nor from Warqa except Hajjaj ibn Nusayr; al-Husayn ibn Mahdi is alone in transmitting it."
"9438","Hushaym ibn Khalaf narrated to us, Umar ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Asadi narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Sharik ibn Abdullah narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid, from Qays ibn Abi Hazim, he said: Umar ibn al-Khattab addressed the people one day upon the pulpit of Madinah, and said in his sermon: In the Gardens of Eden there is a palace with five hundred gates, upon every gate five thousand of the wide-eyed houris; none shall enter it except a prophet. Then he looked toward the grave of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Glad tidings to you, O dweller of the grave. Then he said: Or a truthful one. Then he turned toward the grave of Abu Bakr and said: Glad tidings to you, O Abu Bakr. Then he said: Or a martyr. Then he turned to himself and said: And how would martyrdom come to you, O Umar. Then he said: The One Who brought me out from Makkah to the emigration to Madinah is surely able to drive martyrdom to me. Ibn Masud said: So Allah drove it to him at the hand of the worst of His creatures, a Magian slave owned by al-Mughirah. No one narrated this hadith from Ismail except Sharik; Muhammad ibn al-Hasan is alone in transmitting it."
"9439","Haytham ibn Khalaf narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Umar al-Duri narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Ishaq al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Bayan, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Spitting in the mosque is a sin, and its expiation is burying it. No one narrated this hadith from Bayan except Abu Awanah, nor from Abu Awanah except Ahmad ibn Ishaq; Muhammad ibn Abi Umar is alone in transmitting it."
"9440","Haytham ibn Khalaf narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Mansur al-Tusi narrated to us, Hajib ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Adham, from Muqatil ibn Hayyan, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, he said: I said to Umm Salamah: What was the most frequent supplication of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? She said: O Turner of the hearts, make my heart firm upon Your religion. I said: O Messenger of Allah, how frequent is this supplication of yours? He said: The hearts are between two fingers of the fingers of the Most Merciful; whatever He wills He causes to deviate, and whatever He wills He keeps upright. No one narrated from Ibrahim ibn Adham except Baqiyyah, nor from Baqiyyah except Hajib ibn al-Walid; Muhammad ibn Mansur al-Tusi is alone in transmitting it."
"9441","Haytham ibn Khalaf narrated to us, Maymun ibn al-Asbagh narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Ismah al-Nasibini narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Salamah al-Affani narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade laughing at the passing of wind. No one narrated this hadith from al-Amash except Muhammad ibn Salamah, nor from Muhammad ibn Salamah except Abdullah ibn Ismah; Maymun ibn al-Asbagh is alone in transmitting it."
"9442","Haytham narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ubayd al-Muharibi narrated to us, al-Walid narrated to us, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Harithi, from Muslim al-Mulai, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah ibn Masud, he said: Ali was commanded to fight the oath-breakers, the unjust, and the renegades. No one narrated this hadith from Muslim except Abu Abd al-Rahman, nor from Abu Abd al-Rahman except al-Walid; Muhammad ibn Ubayd is alone in transmitting it."
"9443","Haytham ibn Khalaf narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Salih ibn al-Nattah narrated to us, Artah Abu Hatim narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Were it not to be a regular practice, I would command the tooth-stick at every prayer. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Jurayj except Artah Abu Hatim; Muhammad ibn Salih is alone in transmitting it."
"9444","Haytham ibn Khalaf narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Ibrahim al-Mawsili narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Harun Abu Ishaq al-Kufi, that he heard Abu Burdah narrating from his father Abu Musa - raising it (to the Prophet) - he said: Whoever prays twelve rakahs, Allah will build for him a house in Paradise. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Burdah except Harun Abu Ishaq; Hammad ibn Zayd is alone in transmitting it, and it is not narrated from Abu Musa except with this chain."
"9445","Haytham narrated to us, Humayd ibn Zanjawayh al-Nasai narrated to us, al-Khadir ibn Muhammad ibn Shuja al-Harrani narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, from Ubaydah, from Ribi ibn Hirash, from Hudhayfah, he said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, the hyenas have consumed us. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The world will be opened for you, but would that my nation would not wear silk brocade. No one narrated this hadith from Ubaydah except Hushaym; al-Khadir ibn Muhammad is alone in transmitting it, and it is not narrated from Hudhayfah except with this chain."
"9446","Haytham ibn Khalaf narrated to us, Abu Hafs Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Salt Abu Yala al-Tawwazi narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Malik ibn Mighwal, from Talhah ibn Musarrif, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurairah - raising it (to the Prophet) - he said: A man is approached in his grave; when he is approached from the side of his head, the recitation of the Quran repels it, and when he is approached from before his hands, charity repels it, and when he is approached from before his feet, his walking to the mosques repels it, and patience restrains him. And he said: As for me, if I had seen a close friend, I would have been his companion. No one narrated this hadith from Talhah ibn Musarrif except Malik ibn Mighwal, nor from Malik except Sufyan, nor from Sufyan except Muhammad ibn al-Salt; Abu Hafs is alone in transmitting it."
"9447","Yaqub ibn Ishaq ibn al-Zubayr al-Halabi narrated to us, Abu Jafar al-Nufayli narrated to me, Asim ibn Said narrated to me, from Mabad ibn Khalid, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever revives my practice has loved me, and whoever loves me will be with me in Paradise. No one narrated this hadith from Mabad ibn Khalid except Asim ibn Said; al-Nufayli is alone in transmitting it."
"9448","Yaqub ibn Ishaq ibn al-Zubayr al-Halabi narrated to us, Abu Jafar al-Nufayli narrated to us, Marwan ibn Muawiyah narrated to us, Abu al-Ala al-Khaffaf narrated to us, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would not wipe his face during prayer. No one narrated this hadith from Khalid ibn Tahman Abu al-Ala except Marwan ibn Muawiyah; al-Nufayli is alone in transmitting it."
"9449","Yaqub ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Abu Jafar al-Nufayli narrated to us, Abu Sufyan al-Mamari narrated to us, from Mamar, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever performs ablution and performs it well, and visits his Muslim brother seeking reward, will be kept far from Hell the distance of sixty autumns. I said: O Abu Hamzah, what is an autumn? He said: A year. No one narrated this hadith from Mamar except Abu Sufyan al-Mamari; Abu Jafar al-Nufayli is alone in transmitting it."
"9450","Yaqub ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Abu Jafar al-Nufayli narrated to us, Abu Muawiyah al-Darir narrated to us, from Khalid ibn Ilyas, from Yahya ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Hatib, from Abu Said al-Khudri, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no Muslim man who sees a fault of his brother and conceals it except that Allah will admit him to Paradise thereby. This hadith is not narrated from Abu Said except with this chain; Khalid ibn Ilyas is alone in transmitting it."
"9451","Yaqub ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Abd al-Majid ibn Kathir al-Harrani narrated to us, Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid narrated to us, he said: Abu Bakr al-Ansi narrated to me, Abu Qabil al-Misri narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Fasting emaciates the flesh and keeps one far from the heat of the Blaze; Allah has a table spread with what no eye has seen, nor ear has heard, nor has occurred to the heart of a human; none shall sit at it except the fasting ones. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Qabil except Abu Bakr al-Ansi; Baqiyyah is alone in transmitting it."
"9452","Yaqub ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Makhlad ibn Malik narrated to us, Attaf ibn Khalid al-Makhzumi narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Zayd ibn Aslam narrated to me, from his father, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed us at the Mosque of al-Khayf in Mina, and said: May Allah brighten a man who hears my saying and memorizes it, then conveys it to one who did not hear it; for many a carrier of understanding is not a man of understanding, and many a carrier of understanding conveys it to one more understanding than him. Three things over which the heart of a believing man holds no malice: sincerity of deed for Allah, giving counsel to those whom Allah has placed in authority over you, and adhering to the community of the Muslims; for their supplication encompasses those behind them. No one narrated this hadith from Zayd ibn Aslam except his son; Attaf ibn Khalid and Muhammad ibn Shuayb ibn Shabur are alone in transmitting it."
"9453","Yaqub ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Jafar ibn Asim al-Harrani narrated to us, Mujashi ibn Amr narrated to us, from Dawud ibn Abi Hind, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no loneliness for the people of There is no god but Allah at death, nor at the grave. No one narrated this hadith from Dawud ibn Abi Hind except Mujashi ibn Amr; Jafar ibn Asim is alone in transmitting it."
"9454","Yaqub ibn Ishaq ibn al-Zubayr narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr al-Harrani narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever recites Say: He is Allah, the One fifty times every day will be called on the Day of Resurrection from his grave: Rise and enter Paradise."
"9455","Yaqub ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Yahya ibn Raja al-Harrani narrated to us, Musa ibn Ayan narrated to us, from Layth, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The people of kindness in this world are the people of kindness in the Hereafter. No one narrated this hadith from Layth except Musa ibn Ayan."
"9456","Yaqub ibn Ishaq ibn al-Zubayr narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Muhammad Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Adhrami narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by a bedouin while he was supplicating in his prayer, saying: O One Whom eyes do not see, and thoughts do not mingle with, and describers cannot describe, and events do not change, and Who does not fear vicissitudes; Who knows the weights of the mountains, and the measures of the seas, and the number of the drops of rain, and the number of the leaves of the trees, and the number of what the night darkens upon and the day brightens upon; no heaven conceals a heaven from Him, nor earth an earth, nor sea what is in its depth, nor mountain what is in its ruggedness; make the best of my life its end, and the best of my deeds their final ones, and the best of my days the day I meet You in it. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entrusted a man with the bedouin, and said: When he has prayed, bring him to me. When he had prayed, he brought him, and some gold from one of the mines had been gifted to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). When the bedouin came to him, he gave him the gold, and said: From whom are you, O bedouin? He said: From Banu Amir ibn Sasah, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Do you know why I gave you the gold? He said: Because of the kinship between us and you, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Kinship indeed has a right, but I gave you the gold for your beautiful praise of Allah, Mighty and Majestic. No one narrated this hadith from Humayd except Hushaym; al-Adhrami is alone in transmitting it."
"9457","Yaqub ibn Ishaq al-Mukharrimi narrated to us, Said ibn Sulayman al-Nashiti narrated to us, Jarir ibn Hazim narrated to us, from Harmalah ibn Imran al-Misri, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Shammasah al-Mahri, he said: I entered upon Aishah, and she said: From whom are you? I said: From the people of Egypt. She said: How did you find Ibn Khadij in this campaign of yours? I said: We found him the best of commanders; whenever a horse of one of us died, he gave him a horse. She said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: O Allah, whoever undertakes anything of the affair of my nation and is gentle with them, be gentle with him; and whoever causes hardship upon them, cause hardship upon him. This hadith is not narrated from Abd al-Rahman ibn Shammasah, from Aishah, except with this chain; Harmalah ibn Imran is alone in transmitting it."
"9458","Yaqub ibn Ishaq al-Mukharrimi narrated to us, Ali ibn Bahr ibn Barri narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Anas narrated to us, Mutarrif ibn Tarif narrated to us, from Abu al-Jahm, from al-Bara ibn Azib, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would not pray an obligatory prayer except that he recited qunut in it. No one narrated this hadith from Mutarrif except Muhammad ibn Anas."
"9459","Yaqub ibn Ishaq al-Mukharrimi narrated to us, Shadh ibn al-Fayyad narrated to us, al-Harith ibn Shibl narrated to us, from Umm al-Numan, from Aishah, Mother of the Believers, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The women with the lightest dowry are the greatest in blessing. This hadith is not narrated from Umm al-Numan, from Aishah, except with this chain; al-Harith ibn Shibl is alone in transmitting it."
"9460","Yaqub ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Yahya ibn Zuhayr al-Qurashi narrated to us, Azhar ibn Sad narrated to us, from Ibn Awn, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah has an angel who calls at every prayer: O children of Adam, rise to your fires which you have kindled upon yourselves, and extinguish them with prayer. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Awn except Azhar; Yahya ibn Zuhayr al-Qurashi is alone in transmitting it."
"9461","Yaqub ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Muslim al-Taifi narrated to us, from Ayyub ibn Musa, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The slaughter of the fetus is the slaughter of its mother. No one narrated this hadith from Ayyub ibn Musa except Muhammad ibn Muslim al-Taifi."
"9462","Yaqub ibn Ishaq al-Mukharrimi narrated to us, al-Abbas ibn Bakkar al-Dabbi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Jad al-Qurashi narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ali ibn Zayd ibn Judan, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is overtaken by his term while seeking knowledge will meet Allah with nothing between him and the prophets except the degree of prophethood. No one narrated this hadith from al-Zuhri except Muhammad ibn al-Jad; al-Abbas ibn Bakkar is alone in transmitting it."
"9463","Yaqub ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Talut ibn Abbad narrated to us, Asim ibn Abd al-Wahid al-Wazzan narrated to us, that he heard Anas ibn Malik say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was cupped, and he gave him his wage. No one narrated this hadith from Asim ibn Abd al-Wahid except Talut."
"9464","Yaqub ibn Ishaq al-Mukharrimi narrated to us, Affan ibn Muslim narrated to us, Asim ibn Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us, Uthman ibn Hakim narrated to us, from Amir ibn Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr, from his father, he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sat in prayer, he placed his left foot under his left thigh, and spread his right foot, and placed his left hand upon his knee, and placed his right hand upon his right thigh, and pointed with his finger. No one narrated this hadith from Uthman ibn Hakim except Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad."
"9465","Yaqub ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Affan narrated to us, Wuhayb ibn Khalid narrated to us, from Musa ibn Uqbah, my grandfather narrated to me, that he entered the house upon Uthman while he was besieged in it, and that he heard Abu Hurairah asking permission of Uthman to speak, so he gave him permission. He stood, praised Allah and extolled Him, then said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: There will be trials and dissension after me. A man among the people said: Who is there for us, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Upon you is the commander and his companions - while he was pointing to Uthman. No one narrated this hadith from Musa ibn Uqbah except Wuhayb; and the grandfather of Musa ibn Uqbah on his mothers side is kunyaed Abu Habibah."
"9466","Yaqub ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Salm ibn Qadim narrated to us, Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid narrated to us, from Muawiyah ibn Yahya, from Sulayman ibn Muslim, from Anas, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Guard yourselves against people by means of bad opinion. This hadith is not narrated from Anas except with this chain; Baqiyyah is alone in transmitting it."
"9467","Yaqub narrated to us, Affan narrated to us, Imran al-Qattan Abu al-Awwam narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Abu al-Khalil, from Abdullah ibn al-Harith, from Umm Salamah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allegiance will be given to a man between the Corner and the Station with the number of the people of Badr; the bands of the people of Iraq and the substitutes of the people of Sham will come to him. An army from the people of Sham will attack him, until when they are at al-Bayda they will be swallowed up. Then a man from Quraysh whose maternal uncles are from Kalb will attack them, and they will meet, and Allah will defeat them; deprived is whoever is deprived of the spoils of Kalb. No one narrated this hadith from Qatadah except Imran al-Qattan."
"9468","Yaqub ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Affan narrated to us, Imran narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to me, Abu Nadrah narrated to me, from Abu Said al-Khudri, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: A man from my household will rule, with a clear forehead and an aquiline nose; he will fill the earth with equity and justice as it was filled with wrongdoing and tyranny. He lives this long - and he spread his right palm, and spread two fingers beside it, and spread his left palm. No one narrated this hadith from Qatadah except Imran al-Qattan."
"9469","Yaqub ibn Ishaq al-Mukharrimi narrated to us, Affan narrated to us, Yazid ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Layth ibn Abi Sulaym narrated to us, from Mujahid, from Ibn Umar, he said: We were forbidden to follow a funeral procession accompanied by a wailing woman. No one narrated this hadith from Yazid ibn Ibrahim except Affan."
"9470","Yaqub ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Said ibn Sulayman al-Nashiti narrated to us, Jarir ibn Hazim narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah, she said: Upon my door there was a curtain with winged horses on it, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Remove this."
"9471","And with the same chain, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray at night while I lay across between him and the prayer direction; when he wanted to pray witr, he would wake me, and I would slip away from before him. Jarir ibn Hazim narrated only these two hadiths from Hisham ibn Urwah."
"9472","Yaqub ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Abd al-Samad al-Ansari narrated to us, Man ibn Isa al-Qazzaz narrated to us, Qays ibn al-Rabi narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Layla, from Dawud ibn Ali, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: I have remitted for you (the zakat) on horses and slaves, and there is no zakat in less than two hundred. This hadith is not narrated from Ibn Abbas except with this chain; Man ibn Isa is alone in transmitting it."
"9473","Yaqub ibn Ishaq ibn Abi Israil narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Muhammad ibn Jabir narrated to us, Damdam ibn Jaws ibn Damdam narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Hurairah, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) perform ablution and wipe his head a single time. No one narrated this hadith from Damdam ibn Jaws except Muhammad ibn Jabir."
"9474","Yaqub ibn Ishaq narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Muhammad ibn Jabir narrated to us, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Makkah is a sanctuary; its herbage is not to be cleared away, nor its trees cut down, nor its game frightened. No one narrated this hadith from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Ibn Abbas, except Muhammad ibn Jabir."
"9475","Yaqub ibn Ishaq narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Muhammad ibn Jabir narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Shaqiq ibn Salamah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade us the flesh of domestic donkeys, out of keeping the riding animals. No one narrated this hadith from al-Amash except Hibban and Muhammad ibn Jabir; Ishaq ibn Abi Israil is alone in transmitting it from Muhammad ibn Jabir, and Bakr ibn Yahya ibn Zabban is alone in transmitting it from Hibban."
"9476","Yaqub narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Muhammad ibn Jabir narrated to us, from Hammad, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to Jam (Muzdalifah), he ordered the weak of his family to proceed at night, and said: Do not stone the Jamrah until the sun rises. No one narrated this hadith from Hammad except Muhammad ibn Jabir and Abu Hanifah; Ishaq ibn Abi Israil is alone in transmitting it from Muhammad ibn Jabir, and Abd al-Rahim ibn Sulayman from Abu Hanifah."
"9477","Yaqub ibn Ishaq narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Muhammad ibn Jabir narrated to us, from Yaqub ibn Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: All of Muzdalifah is a place of rites, but keep away from the interior of Uranah; and all of Arafat is a standing place, but keep away from the valley of Muhassir. No one narrated this hadith from Yaqub ibn Ata except Muhammad ibn Jabir and Sufyan ibn Uyaynah."
"9478","Yaqub ibn Ishaq ibn Abi Israil narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Jabir narrated to us, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Abu Mamar, from Uqbah ibn Amr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to wipe our shoulders in prayer, and say: Straighten the shoulders, establish the rows, and do not differ, lest your hearts differ. No one narrated this hadith from Amr ibn Murrah except Muhammad ibn Jabir; Ishaq ibn Abi Israil is alone in transmitting it."
"9479","Yaqub ibn Ishaq ibn Abi Israil narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Muhammad ibn Jabir narrated to us, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Rufay, from Ikrimah, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to kiss while fasting. No one narrated this hadith from Abd al-Aziz ibn Rufay except Muhammad ibn Jabir and Ubaydah ibn Humayd."
"9480","Yaqub ibn Ishaq narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Muhammad ibn Jabir narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Layla, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Allah effaces whatever He wills except wretchedness and felicity, and life and death. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Abi Layla except Muhammad ibn Jabir, nor did anyone narrate it from Nafi except Ibn Abi Layla."
"9481","Yaqub ibn Ishaq narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, Ammar al-Duhni narrated to us, he said: I said to Abu Ishaq: Did you mention - meaning the hadith of Muslim ibn Nudhayr from Hudhayfah: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took hold of the muscle of my leg? So he narrated it to me. Sufyan said: Then I met him and asked him, and he narrated it to me."
"9482","Yaqub ibn Ishaq narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Qays ibn Sad, from al-Hajjaj ibn Artah, from al-Minhal ibn Amr, the hadith of the grave, the hadith of Zadhab, from al-Bara, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), like the hadith of al-Amash. No one narrated this hadith from al-Hajjaj except Qays ibn Sad, nor from Qays ibn Sad except Jarir ibn Hazim, nor from Jarir except Wahb; Ishaq ibn Abi Israil is alone in transmitting it."
"9483","Yaqub ibn Ishaq narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Muhammad ibn Sulayman ibn Masmul narrated to us, Umar ibn Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir narrated to me, from his father, from Jabir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Forelocks are not cut except in hajj or umrah."
"9484","Yaqub ibn Ishaq narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, he said: Muhammad ibn Sulayman ibn Masmul narrated to us, from Umar ibn Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from his father, from Jabir, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) trained horses and raced them; he saw me riding upon a camel and said: O Jabir, you keep pressing him down - meaning: you keep beating him. No one narrated these two hadiths from Umar ibn Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir except Muhammad ibn Sulayman ibn Masmul."
"9485","Yaqub narrated to us, Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Imran ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from his father, from Abd al-Karim, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) circumambulated upon his mount, with a hooked staff in his hand with which he touched the Corner. No one narrated this hadith from Abd al-Karim except Ibn Abi Layla; Imran ibn Muhammad is alone in transmitting it."
"9486","Yaqub ibn Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Abbad ibn al-Awwam al-Wasiti narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abd al-Hamid al-Himmani narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Zayd ibn Aslam narrated to us, from his father, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no loneliness for the people of There is no god but Allah in their graves, nor in their resurrection; as if I see the people of There is no god but Allah shaking the dust off their heads, saying: All praise is due to Allah Who has removed grief from us."
"9487","Yaqub ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Zayd ibn Aslam narrated to us, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out on a campaign and said: No one who has harmed his neighbor shall accompany us today. A man among the people said: I urinated at the base of my neighbors wall? He said: Do not accompany us today."
"9488","And with the same chain: From Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to dislike seven parts of the sheep: the gallbladder, the urinary bladder, the vulva, the male organ, the testicles, the gland, and blood; and the most beloved of the sheep to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was its forequarter. He said: And the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought food, and the people began feeding him meat, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best of meat is the meat of the back."
"9489","And with the same chain: From Ibn Umar, concerning the saying of Allah, Mighty and Majestic: Forgiver of sin and Accepter of repentance, Severe in punishment, Owner of abundance; there is no god but He; to Him is the return: He said: Forgiver of sin for whoever says: There is no god but Allah; and Accepter of repentance from whoever says: There is no god but Allah; Severe in punishment for whoever does not say: There is no god but Allah; Owner of abundance, Owner of independence, there is no god but He - the disbelievers of Quraysh did not declare Him One, so He declared Himself One; to Him is the return: to Him will return whoever says: There is no god but Allah, and he will enter Paradise; and whoever does not say: There is no god but Allah will return and He will admit him to the Fire."
"9490","Yaqub ibn Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Abbad ibn al-Awwam narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Zayd ibn Aslam narrated to us, from his father, from al-Husayn ibn Ali, concerning the saying of Allah, Mighty and Majestic: By the witness and the witnessed: He said: The witness is my grandfather, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the witnessed is the Day of Resurrection. Then he recited this verse: We have sent you as a witness and a bringer of glad tidings and a warner. Then he recited: That is a day for which mankind will be gathered, and that is a witnessed day. No one narrated these hadiths from Zayd ibn Aslam except his son Abd al-Rahman ibn Zayd."
"9491","Yaqub ibn Mujahid al-Basri narrated to us, al-Mundhir ibn al-Walid al-Jarudi narrated to us, my father narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Abi Jafar narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Juhadah, from al-Hakam ibn Utaybah, from al-Hasan ibn Ali, he said: I heard my grandfather, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), say: There is no servant who prays the dawn prayer, then sits remembering Allah until the sun rises, except that he will have a barrier from Hell. No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn Juhadah except al-Hasan ibn Abi Jafar; al-Mundhir is alone in transmitting it from his father."
"9492","Yaqub ibn Mujahid narrated to us, al-Mundhir ibn al-Walid narrated to us, my father narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Abi Jafar narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Juhadah, from Marzuq the freedman of Anas, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded us to seek forgiveness in the pre-dawn hours seventy times. No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn Juhadah except al-Hasan ibn Abi Jafar."
"9493","Yaqub ibn Mujahid narrated to us, al-Mundhir ibn al-Walid narrated to us, my father narrated to us, al-Hasan narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Juhadah narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Adiyy ibn Hatim, he said: Bedouins came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the heat of midday, wearing swords and wrapped in striped outer garments. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) urged the people to give charity for them, and said: Let the owner of a dinar give from his dinar, and the owner of a dirham from his dirham, and the owner of wheat from his wheat, and the owner of barley from his barley, and the owner of dates from his dates, before there comes upon him a day when he will look before him and see nothing but the Fire, and look to his right and see nothing but the Fire, and look to his left and see nothing but the Fire, and look behind him and see nothing but the Fire, and see nothing with which to shield his face from the Fire. No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn Juhadah except al-Hasan ibn Abi Jafar; al-Mundhir is alone in transmitting it from his father."
"9494","And with the same chain: From Muhammad ibn Juhadah, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The imam is a guarantor, and the caller to prayer is entrusted. O Allah, guide the imams and forgive the callers to prayer."
"9495","And with the same chain: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best charity is what leaves sufficiency, and the upper hand is better than the lower hand, and begin with those you support."
"9496","Yaqub ibn Mujahid narrated to us, al-Mundhir ibn al-Walid narrated to us, my father narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Abi Jafar narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Juhadah, from Atiyyah, from Abu Said, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The people of Paradise will see the people of the highest ranks as the people of this world see the brilliant star in the sky; and Abu Bakr and Umar are of them, and they enjoy blessings."
"9497","And with the same chain: From Muhammad ibn Juhadah, from Fulan ibn Sayyah, from al-Mughirah ibn al-Akhnas, he said: We entered upon al-Mughirah ibn Shubah while he was governor over Kufa, and with him was Said ibn Zayd. Then Ghunaym ibn Alqamah entered and said: Who is Ali? So Said ibn Zayd ibn Amr ibn Nufayl said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Abu Bakr is in Paradise, and Umar is in Paradise, and Ali is in Paradise, and Uthman is in Paradise. And Allah knows best what is correct. End of al-Mujam, and praise be to Allah, Lord of the worlds. And Allah knows best what is correct. End of al-Mujam, and praise be to Allah, Lord of the worlds."
